    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "ef27d18c",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ef27d18c"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section C — Getting the Data (Roboflow)\n",
        "\n",
        "We use Roboflow simply to store and download our dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this section, the code automatically downloads the images and labels, looks at how the folders are organized, and checks for any warnings (like if Roboflow automatically resized the images before we downloaded them)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "0bede47e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0bede47e"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION C — Roboflow download, readme inspection, and raw directory summary\n",
        "\n",
        "IMAGE_EXTENSIONS = {\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\", \".bmp\", \".tif\", \".tiff\", \".webp\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "def directory_summary(root: Path, max_depth: int = 3, max_entries_per_dir: int = 40) -> None:\n",
        "    root = Path(root)\n",
        "    if not root.exists():\n",
        "        print(f\"[directory_summary] Missing path: {root}\")\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    print(f\"Directory summary for: {root.resolve()}\")\n",
        "    for path in sorted(root.rglob(\"*\")):\n",
        "        rel = path.relative_to(root)\n",
        "        depth = len(rel.parts)\n",
        "        if depth > max_depth:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        if path.is_dir():\n",
        "            try:\n",
        "                children = list(path.iterdir())\n",
        "            except Exception:\n",
        "                children = []\n",
        "            n_dirs = sum(p.is_dir() for p in children)\n",
        "            n_files = sum(p.is_file() for p in children)\n",
        "            print(f\"[DIR ] {rel} (dirs={n_dirs}, files={n_files})\")\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            print(f\"[FILE] {rel}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def find_dataset_root(download_path: Path) -> Path:\n",
        "    download_path = Path(download_path)\n",
        "    if (download_path / \"data.yaml\").exists():\n",
        "        return download_path\n",
        "    candidates = sorted(download_path.rglob(\"data.yaml\"))\n",
        "    if candidates:\n",
        "        return candidates[0].parent\n",
        "    return download_path\n",
        "\n",
        "def read_text_if_exists(path: Path) -> str:\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        return path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\")\n",
        "    except Exception:\n",
        "        return \"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "def parse_upstream_preprocessing_notes(dataset_root: Path) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    notes = {}\n",
        "    for readme_name in [\"README.roboflow.txt\", \"README.dataset.txt\"]:\n",
        "        txt = read_text_if_exists(dataset_root / readme_name)\n",
        "        if txt:\n",
        "            notes[readme_name] = txt[:4000]\n",
        "    data_yaml = {}\n",
        "    data_yaml_path = dataset_root / \"data.yaml\"\n",
        "    if data_yaml_path.exists():\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            data_yaml = yaml.safe_load(data_yaml_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n",
        "        except Exception as exc:\n",
        "            data_yaml = {\"_parse_error\": str(exc)}\n",
        "    return {\"readmes\": notes, \"data_yaml\": data_yaml}\n",
        "\n",
        "with timed_block(\"Roboflow download\"):\n",
        "    rf = Roboflow(api_key=CFG.roboflow_api_key)\n",
        "    project = rf.workspace(CFG.roboflow_workspace).project(CFG.roboflow_project)\n",
        "    version = project.version(CFG.roboflow_version)\n",
        "    dataset = version.download(CFG.roboflow_download_format, location=str(CFG.paths.raw_download_root))\n",
        "\n",
        "RAW_DOWNLOAD_PATH = Path(dataset.location).resolve()\n",
        "DATASET_ROOT = find_dataset_root(RAW_DOWNLOAD_PATH)\n",
        "RAW_DATASET_NOTES = parse_upstream_preprocessing_notes(DATASET_ROOT)\n",
        "\n",
        "raw_meta_path = CFG.paths.audit_root / \"raw_dataset_notes.json\"\n",
        "with open(raw_meta_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "    json.dump(RAW_DATASET_NOTES, f, indent=2, default=str)\n",
        "\n",
        "print_rule(\"ROBOFLOW RAW DOWNLOAD\")\n",
        "print(\"RAW_DOWNLOAD_PATH:\", RAW_DOWNLOAD_PATH)\n",
        "print(\"DATASET_ROOT:\", DATASET_ROOT)\n",
        "directory_summary(DATASET_ROOT, max_depth=3)\n",
        "\n",
        "readme_blob = \"\\n\\n\".join(RAW_DATASET_NOTES.get(\"readmes\", {}).values()).lower()\n",
        "if any(tok in readme_blob for tok in [\"augment\", \"auto-orient\", \"resize\", \"stretch\", \"preprocess\"]):\n",
        "    print_rule(\"UPSTREAM PREPROCESSING WARNING\")\n",
        "    print(\n",
        "        \"This Roboflow version appears to include upstream preprocessing metadata \"\n",
        "        \"(for example auto-orient and/or resize). The notebook continues, but all \"\n",
        "        \"new training-time augmentation remains controlled locally in code.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Saved raw dataset notes to:\", raw_meta_path.resolve())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "a284d736",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "a284d736"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section D & E — Organizing and Cleaning Our Data\n",
        "\n",
        "Before we train anything, we need to know exactly what we have. We build a \"Manifest\"—essentially a giant spreadsheet that lists every single image, its label, its size, and any metadata we can guess from the filename.\n",
        "\n",
        "More importantly, we run an **Audit** to check for dirty data:\n",
        "- Are there corrupted images?\n",
        "- Are there exact duplicates?\n",
        "- Are there *near* duplicates? (Images that look almost exactly the same)\n",
        "- Is there a risk that images from the same camera session got split into both the train and test sets?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "0ec9b346",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0ec9b346"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION D + E — Manifest helpers\n",
        "\n",
        "SPLIT_ALIASES = {\n",
        "    \"train\": \"train\",\n",
        "    \"training\": \"train\",\n",
        "    \"trn\": \"train\",\n",
        "    \"valid\": \"valid\",\n",
        "    \"val\": \"valid\",\n",
        "    \"validation\": \"valid\",\n",
        "    \"dev\": \"valid\",\n",
        "    \"test\": \"test\",\n",
        "    \"testing\": \"test\",\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "def normalize_token(value: Any) -> str:\n",
        "    value = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n",
        "    value = value.strip().lower()\n",
        "    value = re.sub(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\", \"_\", value)\n",
        "    value = re.sub(r\"_+\", \"_\", value).strip(\"_\")\n",
        "    return value\n",
        "\n",
        "def strip_roboflow_suffix(filename_or_stem: str) -> str:\n",
        "    s = filename_or_stem\n",
        "    s = re.sub(r\"\\.rf\\.[a-f0-9]+$\", \"\", s)\n",
        "    s = re.sub(r\"\\.rf\\.[a-z0-9]+$\", \"\", s)\n",
        "    return s\n",
        "\n",
        "def infer_source_split_from_path(path: Path) -> str:\n",
        "    for part in path.parts:\n",
        "        key = normalize_token(part)\n",
        "        if key in SPLIT_ALIASES:\n",
        "            return SPLIT_ALIASES[key]\n",
        "    return \"unknown\"\n",
        "\n",
        "def safe_image_open(path: Path) -> Tuple[Optional[Image.Image], Optional[str]]:\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        img = Image.open(path)\n",
        "        img.load()\n",
        "        return img, None\n",
        "    except Exception as exc:\n",
        "        return None, f\"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}\"\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_sha1(path: Path, chunk_size: int = 1024 * 1024) -> str:\n",
        "    h = __import__(\"hashlib\").sha1()\n",
        "    with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n",
        "        while True:\n",
        "            chunk = f.read(chunk_size)\n",
        "            if not chunk:\n",
        "                break\n",
        "            h.update(chunk)\n",
        "    return h.hexdigest()\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_dhash(path: Path, hash_size: int = 8) -> Optional[int]:\n",
        "    img, err = safe_image_open(path)\n",
        "    if img is None:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        img = img.convert(\"L\").resize((hash_size + 1, hash_size), Image.Resampling.BILINEAR)\n",
        "        arr = np.asarray(img, dtype=np.int16)\n",
        "        diff = arr[:, 1:] > arr[:, :-1]\n",
        "        bit_string = \"\".join(\"1\" if v else \"0\" for v in diff.flatten())\n",
        "        return int(bit_string, 2)\n",
        "    except Exception:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "\n",
        "def hamming_distance_int(a: Optional[int], b: Optional[int]) -> Optional[int]:\n",
        "    if a is None or b is None:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    return int((a ^ b).bit_count())\n",
        "\n",
        "def find_label_file_for_image(image_path: Path) -> Optional[Path]:\n",
        "    parts = list(image_path.parts)\n",
        "    if \"images\" in parts:\n",
        "        idx = parts.index(\"images\")\n",
        "        parts[idx] = \"labels\"\n",
        "        label_path = Path(*parts).with_suffix(\".txt\")\n",
        "        if label_path.exists():\n",
        "            return label_path\n",
        "    candidate = image_path.with_suffix(\".txt\")\n",
        "    if candidate.exists():\n",
        "        return candidate\n",
        "    return None\n",
        "\n",
        "def yolo_bbox_to_xyxy(xc: float, yc: float, w: float, h: float, img_w: int, img_h: int) -> Tuple[float, float, float, float]:\n",
        "    bw = w * img_w\n",
        "    bh = h * img_h\n",
        "    x1 = (xc * img_w) - bw / 2.0\n",
        "    y1 = (yc * img_h) - bh / 2.0\n",
        "    x2 = (xc * img_w) + bw / 2.0\n",
        "    y2 = (yc * img_h) + bh / 2.0\n",
        "    return x1, y1, x2, y2\n",
        "\n",
        "def xyxy_to_yolo_bbox(x1: float, y1: float, x2: float, y2: float, img_w: int, img_h: int) -> Tuple[float, float, float, float]:\n",
        "    x1 = max(0.0, min(x1, img_w))\n",
        "    y1 = max(0.0, min(y1, img_h))\n",
        "    x2 = max(0.0, min(x2, img_w))\n",
        "    y2 = max(0.0, min(y2, img_h))\n",
        "    xc = ((x1 + x2) / 2.0) / img_w\n",
        "    yc = ((y1 + y2) / 2.0) / img_h\n",
        "    w = max(1.0, x2 - x1) / img_w\n",
        "    h = max(1.0, y2 - y1) / img_h\n",
        "    return xc, yc, w, h\n",
        "\n",
        "def parse_yolo_label_file(label_path: Optional[Path], img_w: int, img_h: int) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    if label_path is None or not Path(label_path).exists():\n",
        "        return {\n",
        "            \"label_path\": None,\n",
        "            \"label_source_format\": \"none\",\n",
        "            \"class_id\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_count\": 0,\n",
        "            \"bbox_xc\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_yc\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_w\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_h\": None,\n",
        "            \"label_note\": \"missing_label_file\",\n",
        "        }\n",
        "\n",
        "    lines = [ln.strip() for ln in Path(label_path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"ignore\").splitlines() if ln.strip()]\n",
        "    if not lines:\n",
        "        return {\n",
        "            \"label_path\": str(label_path),\n",
        "            \"label_source_format\": \"yolo\",\n",
        "            \"class_id\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_count\": 0,\n",
        "            \"bbox_xc\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_yc\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_w\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_h\": None,\n",
        "            \"label_note\": \"empty_label_file\",\n",
        "        }\n",
        "\n",
        "    class_ids = []\n",
        "    boxes_xyxy = []\n",
        "    for line in lines:\n",
        "        parts = line.split()\n",
        "        if len(parts) < 5:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        class_id = int(float(parts[0]))\n",
        "        coords = [float(v) for v in parts[1:5]]\n",
        "        class_ids.append(class_id)\n",
        "        boxes_xyxy.append(yolo_bbox_to_xyxy(coords[0], coords[1], coords[2], coords[3], img_w, img_h))\n",
        "\n",
        "    if not class_ids:\n",
        "        return {\n",
        "            \"label_path\": str(label_path),\n",
        "            \"label_source_format\": \"yolo\",\n",
        "            \"class_id\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_count\": 0,\n",
        "            \"bbox_xc\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_yc\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_w\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_h\": None,\n",
        "            \"label_note\": \"unparseable_label_file\",\n",
        "        }\n",
        "\n",
        "    unique_classes = sorted(set(class_ids))\n",
        "    if len(unique_classes) > 1:\n",
        "        label_note = \"multiple_classes_in_single_image\"\n",
        "        class_id = unique_classes[0]\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        label_note = \"ok\"\n",
        "        class_id = unique_classes[0]\n",
        "\n",
        "    x1 = min(b[0] for b in boxes_xyxy)\n",
        "    y1 = min(b[1] for b in boxes_xyxy)\n",
        "    x2 = max(b[2] for b in boxes_xyxy)\n",
        "    y2 = max(b[3] for b in boxes_xyxy)\n",
        "    xc, yc, w, h = xyxy_to_yolo_bbox(x1, y1, x2, y2, img_w, img_h)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"label_path\": str(label_path),\n",
        "        \"label_source_format\": \"yolo\",\n",
        "        \"class_id\": int(class_id),\n",
        "        \"bbox_count\": int(len(boxes_xyxy)),\n",
        "        \"bbox_xc\": float(xc),\n",
        "        \"bbox_yc\": float(yc),\n",
        "        \"bbox_w\": float(w),\n",
        "        \"bbox_h\": float(h),\n",
        "        \"label_note\": label_note,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "def infer_label_from_class_folder(path: Path, class_names: Sequence[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n",
        "    normalized = {normalize_token(name): name for name in class_names}\n",
        "    for part in reversed(path.parts[:-1]):\n",
        "        key = normalize_token(part)\n",
        "        if key in normalized:\n",
        "            return normalized[key]\n",
        "    return None\n",
        "\n",
        "def parse_metadata_from_name(path: Path) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    filename = path.name\n",
        "    stem = strip_roboflow_suffix(path.stem)\n",
        "    stem_no_ext = strip_roboflow_suffix(path.name.split(\".\")[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "    meta: Dict[str, Any] = {\n",
        "        \"base_stem\": stem,\n",
        "        \"session_date\": None,\n",
        "        \"session_time\": None,\n",
        "        \"session_hour\": None,\n",
        "        \"session_minute_bucket\": None,\n",
        "        \"source_kind\": None,\n",
        "        \"setup_hint\": None,\n",
        "        \"run_hint\": None,\n",
        "        \"batch_hint\": None,\n",
        "        \"strain_hint\": None,\n",
        "        \"metadata_parse_note\": \"\",\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    capture_match = re.search(r\"capture_(\\d{8})_(\\d{6})\", stem_no_ext, flags=re.IGNORECASE)\n",
        "    screenshot_match = re.search(\n",
        "        r\"screenshot[-_](\\d{4})[-_](\\d{2})[-_](\\d{2}).*?at[-_](\\d{1,2})[-_](\\d{2})\",\n",
        "        stem_no_ext,\n",
        "        flags=re.IGNORECASE,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    if capture_match:\n",
        "        date_str, time_str = capture_match.groups()\n",
        "        meta[\"session_date\"] = date_str\n",
        "        meta[\"session_time\"] = time_str\n",
        "        meta[\"session_hour\"] = time_str[:2]\n",
        "        minute = int(time_str[2:4])\n",
        "        meta[\"session_minute_bucket\"] = f\"{minute // max(1, CFG.group_time_bucket_minutes):02d}\"\n",
        "        meta[\"source_kind\"] = \"capture\"\n",
        "        meta[\"metadata_parse_note\"] = \"capture_pattern\"\n",
        "    elif screenshot_match:\n",
        "        yyyy, mm, dd, hh, minute = screenshot_match.groups()\n",
        "        date_str = f\"{yyyy}{mm}{dd}\"\n",
        "        hh_int = int(hh)\n",
        "        meta[\"session_date\"] = date_str\n",
        "        meta[\"session_time\"] = f\"{hh_int:02d}{int(minute):02d}00\"\n",
        "        meta[\"session_hour\"] = f\"{hh_int:02d}\"\n",
        "        meta[\"session_minute_bucket\"] = f\"{int(minute) // max(1, CFG.group_time_bucket_minutes):02d}\"\n",
        "        meta[\"source_kind\"] = \"screenshot\"\n",
        "        meta[\"metadata_parse_note\"] = \"screenshot_pattern\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        meta[\"metadata_parse_note\"] = \"filename_pattern_not_found\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Parent-folder hints for setup / run / batch / strain.\n",
        "    parent_tokens = [normalize_token(p) for p in path.parts[:-1]]\n",
        "    informative_tokens = [p for p in parent_tokens if p not in SPLIT_ALIASES and p not in {\"images\", \"labels\"}]\n",
        "    if informative_tokens:\n",
        "        meta[\"setup_hint\"] = informative_tokens[-1]\n",
        "        if len(informative_tokens) >= 2:\n",
        "            meta[\"run_hint\"] = informative_tokens[-2]\n",
        "        if len(informative_tokens) >= 3:\n",
        "            meta[\"batch_hint\"] = informative_tokens[-3]\n",
        "\n",
        "    strain_match = re.search(r\"(line|strain|stock)[-_]?([a-z0-9]+)\", stem_no_ext, flags=re.IGNORECASE)\n",
        "    if strain_match:\n",
        "        meta[\"strain_hint\"] = normalize_token(\"_\".join(strain_match.groups()))\n",
        "\n",
        "    return meta\n",
        "\n",
        "def infer_group_id(record: Dict[str, Any], time_bucket_minutes: int) -> str:\n",
        "    components = []\n",
        "    if record.get(\"session_date\"):\n",
        "        components.append(str(record[\"session_date\"]))\n",
        "    if record.get(\"session_hour\"):\n",
        "        components.append(f\"h{record['session_hour']}\")\n",
        "    if record.get(\"session_minute_bucket\") is not None:\n",
        "        components.append(f\"b{record['session_minute_bucket']}\")\n",
        "    if record.get(\"setup_hint\"):\n",
        "        components.append(str(record[\"setup_hint\"]))\n",
        "    if record.get(\"run_hint\"):\n",
        "        components.append(str(record[\"run_hint\"]))\n",
        "    if record.get(\"source_kind\"):\n",
        "        components.append(str(record[\"source_kind\"]))\n",
        "    if not components:\n",
        "        components.append(record.get(\"base_stem\", \"ungrouped\"))\n",
        "    return \"__\".join([normalize_token(c) for c in components if c])\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_manifest_record(image_path: Path, class_names: Sequence[str], label_override: Dict[int, str]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    img, img_err = safe_image_open(image_path)\n",
        "    record: Dict[str, Any] = {\n",
        "        \"filepath\": str(image_path.resolve()),\n",
        "        \"filename\": image_path.name,\n",
        "        \"file_size_bytes\": image_path.stat().st_size if image_path.exists() else None,\n",
        "        \"source_split\": infer_source_split_from_path(image_path),\n",
        "        \"parent_1\": image_path.parent.name if image_path.parent else None,\n",
        "        \"parent_2\": image_path.parent.parent.name if image_path.parent and image_path.parent.parent else None,\n",
        "        \"parent_3\": image_path.parent.parent.parent.name if image_path.parent and image_path.parent.parent and image_path.parent.parent.parent else None,\n",
        "        \"corrupt\": img is None,\n",
        "        \"corrupt_reason\": img_err,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    if img is not None:\n",
        "        record[\"width\"], record[\"height\"] = img.size\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        record[\"width\"], record[\"height\"] = None, None\n",
        "\n",
        "    record[\"file_sha1\"] = compute_sha1(image_path) if image_path.exists() else None\n",
        "    record[\"dhash64\"] = compute_dhash(image_path) if CFG.compute_dhash and image_path.exists() else None\n",
        "\n",
        "    label_file = find_label_file_for_image(image_path) if image_path.exists() else None\n",
        "    if img is not None:\n",
        "        label_info = parse_yolo_label_file(label_file, img_w=img.size[0], img_h=img.size[1])\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        label_info = {\n",
        "            \"label_path\": str(label_file) if label_file else None,\n",
        "            \"label_source_format\": \"none\",\n",
        "            \"class_id\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_count\": 0,\n",
        "            \"bbox_xc\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_yc\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_w\": None,\n",
        "            \"bbox_h\": None,\n",
        "            \"label_note\": \"image_corrupt\",\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    record.update(label_info)\n",
        "\n",
        "    label_name = None\n",
        "    if record.get(\"class_id\") is not None:\n",
        "        label_name = label_override.get(int(record[\"class_id\"]))\n",
        "    if label_name is None:\n",
        "        label_name = infer_label_from_class_folder(image_path, class_names)\n",
        "\n",
        "    record[\"label\"] = label_name\n",
        "    record[\"label_idx\"] = class_names.index(label_name) if label_name in class_names else None\n",
        "\n",
        "    meta = parse_metadata_from_name(image_path)\n",
        "    record.update(meta)\n",
        "    record[\"group_id\"] = infer_group_id(record, time_bucket_minutes=CFG.group_time_bucket_minutes)\n",
        "    record[\"parse_notes\"] = \";\".join([n for n in [record.get(\"label_note\"), record.get(\"metadata_parse_note\")] if n])\n",
        "    return record\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_canonical_manifest(dataset_root: Path, class_names: Sequence[str], label_override: Dict[int, str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n",
        "    image_paths = sorted([p for p in dataset_root.rglob(\"*\") if p.is_file() and p.suffix.lower() in IMAGE_EXTENSIONS])\n",
        "    print(f\"Discovered {len(image_paths)} candidate image files.\")\n",
        "    for image_path in tqdm(image_paths, desc=\"Building manifest\"):\n",
        "        rows.append(build_manifest_record(image_path, class_names=class_names, label_override=label_override))\n",
        "    df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "\n",
        "    expected_cols = [\n",
        "        \"filepath\", \"filename\", \"label\", \"label_idx\", \"source_split\",\n",
        "        \"file_sha1\", \"file_size_bytes\", \"width\", \"height\",\n",
        "        \"parent_1\", \"parent_2\", \"parent_3\",\n",
        "        \"session_date\", \"session_time\", \"session_hour\",\n",
        "        \"setup_hint\", \"run_hint\", \"batch_hint\", \"strain_hint\",\n",
        "        \"group_id\", \"corrupt\", \"parse_notes\",\n",
        "        \"label_path\", \"label_source_format\", \"class_id\", \"bbox_count\",\n",
        "        \"bbox_xc\", \"bbox_yc\", \"bbox_w\", \"bbox_h\", \"dhash64\",\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    for col in expected_cols:\n",
        "        if col not in df.columns:\n",
        "            df[col] = None\n",
        "    return df\n",
        "\n",
        "def summarize_class_balance(df: pd.DataFrame, class_names: Sequence[str]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    summary = (\n",
        "        df[~df[\"corrupt\"]]\n",
        "        .groupby([\"source_split\", \"label\"])\n",
        "        .size()\n",
        "        .unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
        "        .reindex(columns=class_names, fill_value=0)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return summary\n",
        "\n",
        "def exact_duplicate_table(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    dup = df.groupby(\"file_sha1\").agg(\n",
        "        n=(\"filepath\", \"size\"),\n",
        "        splits=(\"source_split\", lambda x: sorted(set(x))),\n",
        "        labels=(\"label\", lambda x: sorted(set(x))),\n",
        "        filepaths=(\"filepath\", list),\n",
        "    ).reset_index()\n",
        "    dup = dup[dup[\"n\"] > 1].sort_values([\"n\", \"file_sha1\"], ascending=[False, True]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "    return dup\n",
        "\n",
        "def suspicious_filename_reuse_table(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    stem_series = df[\"filename\"].astype(str).map(lambda x: strip_roboflow_suffix(Path(x).stem))\n",
        "    tmp = df.copy()\n",
        "    tmp[\"filename_base\"] = stem_series\n",
        "    reuse = tmp.groupby(\"filename_base\").agg(\n",
        "        n=(\"filepath\", \"size\"),\n",
        "        splits=(\"source_split\", lambda x: sorted(set(x))),\n",
        "        labels=(\"label\", lambda x: sorted(set(x))),\n",
        "        filepaths=(\"filepath\", list),\n",
        "    ).reset_index()\n",
        "    reuse = reuse[reuse[\"n\"] > 1].sort_values([\"n\", \"filename_base\"], ascending=[False, True]).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "    return reuse\n",
        "\n",
        "def near_duplicate_pairs_table(df: pd.DataFrame, threshold: int = 5, max_pairs: int = 5000) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    work = df[~df[\"corrupt\"] & df[\"dhash64\"].notna()].reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    for i in range(len(work)):\n",
        "        a = work.iloc[i]\n",
        "        for j in range(i + 1, len(work)):\n",
        "            b = work.iloc[j]\n",
        "            dist = hamming_distance_int(int(a[\"dhash64\"]), int(b[\"dhash64\"]))\n",
        "            if dist is not None and dist <= threshold:\n",
        "                rows.append({\n",
        "                    \"idx_a\": int(i),\n",
        "                    \"idx_b\": int(j),\n",
        "                    \"filepath_a\": a[\"filepath\"],\n",
        "                    \"filepath_b\": b[\"filepath\"],\n",
        "                    \"label_a\": a[\"label\"],\n",
        "                    \"label_b\": b[\"label\"],\n",
        "                    \"source_split_a\": a[\"source_split\"],\n",
        "                    \"source_split_b\": b[\"source_split\"],\n",
        "                    \"hamming_distance\": int(dist),\n",
        "                    \"same_label\": a[\"label\"] == b[\"label\"],\n",
        "                    \"cross_split\": a[\"source_split\"] != b[\"source_split\"],\n",
        "                })\n",
        "                if len(rows) >= max_pairs:\n",
        "                    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "\n",
        "def cross_split_group_overlap_table(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    tmp = (\n",
        "        df.groupby([\"group_id\", \"source_split\"]).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
        "        if \"group_id\" in df.columns else pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    if tmp.empty:\n",
        "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "    tmp[\"num_splits_present\"] = (tmp > 0).sum(axis=1)\n",
        "    overlap = tmp[tmp[\"num_splits_present\"] > 1].reset_index()\n",
        "    return overlap.sort_values(\"num_splits_present\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "ce4b6657",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ce4b6657"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION D + E — Build canonical manifest and run duplicate / leakage audits\n",
        "\n",
        "with timed_block(\"Canonical manifest build\"):\n",
        "    canonical_manifest_df = build_canonical_manifest(\n",
        "        DATASET_ROOT,\n",
        "        class_names=CFG.class_names,\n",
        "        label_override=CFG.label_id_to_name_override,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "manifest_csv_path = CFG.paths.manifest_root / \"canonical_manifest.csv\"\n",
        "manifest_parquet_path = CFG.paths.manifest_root / \"canonical_manifest.parquet\"\n",
        "canonical_manifest_df.to_csv(manifest_csv_path, index=False)\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    canonical_manifest_df.to_parquet(manifest_parquet_path, index=False)\n",
        "except Exception as exc:\n",
        "    print(\"Parquet export skipped:\", exc)\n",
        "\n",
        "invalid_label_rows = canonical_manifest_df[\n",
        "    (~canonical_manifest_df[\"corrupt\"]) &\n",
        "    (~canonical_manifest_df[\"label\"].isin(CFG.class_names))\n",
        "]\n",
        "if not invalid_label_rows.empty:\n",
        "    display(invalid_label_rows.head(10))\n",
        "    raise ValueError(\n",
        "        \"Found non-corrupt images whose labels could not be resolved to the expected class set. \"\n",
        "        \"Inspect the manifest and label parsing logic before continuing.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "exact_dups_df = exact_duplicate_table(canonical_manifest_df)\n",
        "filename_reuse_df = suspicious_filename_reuse_table(canonical_manifest_df)\n",
        "near_dups_df = near_duplicate_pairs_table(\n",
        "    canonical_manifest_df,\n",
        "    threshold=CFG.near_duplicate_hamming_threshold,\n",
        "    max_pairs=CFG.max_near_duplicate_pairs_to_save,\n",
        ")\n",
        "group_overlap_df = cross_split_group_overlap_table(canonical_manifest_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "exact_dups_path = CFG.paths.audit_root / \"exact_duplicates.csv\"\n",
        "filename_reuse_path = CFG.paths.audit_root / \"filename_reuse.csv\"\n",
        "near_dups_path = CFG.paths.audit_root / \"near_duplicates.csv\"\n",
        "group_overlap_path = CFG.paths.audit_root / \"raw_group_overlap.csv\"\n",
        "\n",
        "exact_dups_df.to_csv(exact_dups_path, index=False)\n",
        "filename_reuse_df.to_csv(filename_reuse_path, index=False)\n",
        "near_dups_df.to_csv(near_dups_path, index=False)\n",
        "group_overlap_df.to_csv(group_overlap_path, index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "class_balance_tbl = summarize_class_balance(canonical_manifest_df, CFG.class_names)\n",
        "class_balance_path = CFG.paths.audit_root / \"source_split_class_balance.csv\"\n",
        "class_balance_tbl.to_csv(class_balance_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "print_rule(\"CANONICAL MANIFEST SUMMARY\")\n",
        "print(\"Manifest rows:\", len(canonical_manifest_df))\n",
        "print(\"Corrupt images:\", int(canonical_manifest_df[\"corrupt\"].sum()))\n",
        "print(\"Exact duplicate groups:\", len(exact_dups_df))\n",
        "print(\"Filename reuse groups:\", len(filename_reuse_df))\n",
        "print(\"Near duplicate pairs:\", len(near_dups_df))\n",
        "print(\"Raw group overlap groups:\", len(group_overlap_df))\n",
        "display(class_balance_tbl)\n",
        "\n",
        "overall_class_counts = canonical_manifest_df[~canonical_manifest_df[\"corrupt\"]][\"label\"].value_counts().reindex(CFG.class_names, fill_value=0)\n",
        "display(pd.DataFrame({\"count\": overall_class_counts, \"fraction\": overall_class_counts / max(1, overall_class_counts.sum())}))\n",
        "\n",
        "imbalance_ratio = (\n",
        "    float(overall_class_counts.max()) / max(1.0, float(overall_class_counts.min()))\n",
        "    if len(overall_class_counts) and overall_class_counts.min() > 0 else float(\"inf\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(\"Overall class imbalance ratio (majority/minority):\", f\"{imbalance_ratio:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "if not exact_dups_df.empty:\n",
        "    cross_split_exact = exact_dups_df[exact_dups_df[\"splits\"].map(lambda x: len(x) > 1)]\n",
        "    if len(cross_split_exact) > 0:\n",
        "        print_rule(\"WARNING — EXACT DUPLICATES ACROSS RAW SPLITS\")\n",
        "        display(cross_split_exact.head(10))\n",
        "\n",
        "if not group_overlap_df.empty:\n",
        "    print_rule(\"WARNING — RAW GROUP OVERLAP ACROSS SPLITS\")\n",
        "    display(group_overlap_df.head(10))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Saved manifest to:\", manifest_csv_path.resolve())\n",
        "print(\"Saved audits to:\", CFG.paths.audit_root.resolve())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "0b4e9acd",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0b4e9acd"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section F — Splitting the Data Fairly\n",
        "\n",
        "We need to split our images into Training, Validation, and Testing sets.\n",
        "\n",
        "If the data downloaded from Roboflow is already split perfectly and passes our safety checks, we keep it.\n",
        "\n",
        "If the data is messy (for example, if the same video session leaked into both the train and test sets), this code will automatically completely rebuild the split. It ensures that images from the same time/group stay together, preventing the AI from cheating."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "0aedf748",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "0aedf748"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION F — Canonical split builder\n",
        "\n",
        "def raw_splits_have_required_structure(df: pd.DataFrame) -> bool:\n",
        "    required = {\"train\", \"valid\", \"test\"}\n",
        "    present = set(df[\"source_split\"].dropna().unique().tolist())\n",
        "    return required.issubset(present)\n",
        "\n",
        "def raw_splits_have_all_classes(df: pd.DataFrame, class_names: Sequence[str]) -> bool:\n",
        "    tmp = (\n",
        "        df[~df[\"corrupt\"]]\n",
        "        .groupby([\"source_split\", \"label\"])\n",
        "        .size()\n",
        "        .unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
        "        .reindex(columns=class_names, fill_value=0)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    required = {\"train\", \"valid\", \"test\"}\n",
        "    if not required.issubset(set(tmp.index)):\n",
        "        return False\n",
        "    for split_name in required:\n",
        "        row = tmp.loc[split_name]\n",
        "        if (row <= 0).any():\n",
        "            return False\n",
        "    return True\n",
        "\n",
        "def raw_splits_have_cross_split_exact_duplicates(exact_dup_table: pd.DataFrame) -> bool:\n",
        "    if exact_dup_table.empty:\n",
        "        return False\n",
        "    return bool(exact_dup_table[\"splits\"].map(lambda x: len(x) > 1).any())\n",
        "\n",
        "def raw_splits_have_group_overlap(group_overlap_table: pd.DataFrame) -> bool:\n",
        "    return not group_overlap_table.empty\n",
        "\n",
        "def is_raw_split_trustworthy(df: pd.DataFrame) -> Tuple[bool, List[str]]:\n",
        "    reasons = []\n",
        "    if CFG.force_rebuild_splits:\n",
        "        reasons.append(\"force_rebuild_splits=True\")\n",
        "    if not raw_splits_have_required_structure(df):\n",
        "        reasons.append(\"raw splits missing one or more of train/valid/test\")\n",
        "    if not raw_splits_have_all_classes(df, CFG.class_names):\n",
        "        reasons.append(\"one or more raw splits do not contain both classes\")\n",
        "    if raw_splits_have_cross_split_exact_duplicates(exact_dups_df):\n",
        "        reasons.append(\"exact duplicate leakage across raw splits\")\n",
        "    if CFG.split_by_group_if_available and raw_splits_have_group_overlap(group_overlap_df):\n",
        "        reasons.append(\"inferred group overlap across raw splits\")\n",
        "    trustworthy = len(reasons) == 0\n",
        "    return trustworthy, reasons\n",
        "\n",
        "def split_counts_table(df: pd.DataFrame, split_col: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    table = (\n",
        "        df.groupby([split_col, \"label\"])\n",
        "        .size()\n",
        "        .unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
        "        .reindex(columns=CFG.class_names, fill_value=0)\n",
        "        .reset_index()\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    table[\"n_total\"] = table[CFG.class_names].sum(axis=1)\n",
        "    for name in CFG.class_names:\n",
        "        table[f\"frac_{name}\"] = table[name] / table[\"n_total\"].clip(lower=1)\n",
        "    group_counts = df.groupby(split_col)[\"group_id\"].nunique().rename(\"n_groups\").reset_index()\n",
        "    table = table.merge(group_counts, on=split_col, how=\"left\")\n",
        "    return table\n",
        "\n",
        "def random_greedy_group_split(\n",
        "    df: pd.DataFrame,\n",
        "    seed: int,\n",
        "    ratios: Tuple[float, float, float],\n",
        "    group_col: str = \"group_id\",\n",
        "    label_col: str = \"label_idx\",\n",
        "    trials: int = 400,\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, str]:\n",
        "    work = df.copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "    if group_col not in work.columns or work[group_col].isna().all():\n",
        "        # Fall back to image-level grouping.\n",
        "        work[group_col] = [f\"img_{i:06d}\" for i in range(len(work))]\n",
        "\n",
        "    group_table = (\n",
        "        work.groupby(group_col)[label_col]\n",
        "        .value_counts()\n",
        "        .unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
        "        .reindex(columns=list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes)), fill_value=0)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    group_table[\"n_total\"] = group_table.sum(axis=1)\n",
        "    groups = group_table.index.to_list()\n",
        "    total_counts = group_table[list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes))].sum(axis=0).to_dict()\n",
        "    total_n = int(group_table[\"n_total\"].sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "    split_names = [\"train\", \"valid\", \"test\"]\n",
        "    target_n = {\n",
        "        \"train\": int(round(ratios[0] * total_n)),\n",
        "        \"valid\": int(round(ratios[1] * total_n)),\n",
        "        \"test\": total_n - int(round(ratios[0] * total_n)) - int(round(ratios[1] * total_n)),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    target_class = {\n",
        "        split: {\n",
        "            c: ratios[i] * total_counts.get(c, 0)\n",
        "            for c in range(CFG.expected_num_classes)\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        for i, split in enumerate(split_names)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    def assignment_score(state_counts: Dict[str, Dict[int, int]], state_n: Dict[str, int]) -> float:\n",
        "        score = 0.0\n",
        "        for split in split_names:\n",
        "            n_err = (state_n[split] - target_n[split]) / max(1.0, target_n[split])\n",
        "            score += 2.0 * (n_err ** 2)\n",
        "            for c in range(CFG.expected_num_classes):\n",
        "                target = max(1.0, target_class[split][c])\n",
        "                c_err = (state_counts[split].get(c, 0) - target) / target\n",
        "                score += 3.0 * (c_err ** 2)\n",
        "            if state_n[split] == 0:\n",
        "                score += 50.0\n",
        "        return score\n",
        "\n",
        "    best_assignment = None\n",
        "    best_score = float(\"inf\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    for trial in range(trials):\n",
        "        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed + trial)\n",
        "        order = groups.copy()\n",
        "        rng.shuffle(order)\n",
        "\n",
        "        counts = {split: defaultdict(int) for split in split_names}\n",
        "        n_counts = {split: 0 for split in split_names}\n",
        "        assignment: Dict[str, str] = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "        for group in order:\n",
        "            g_row = group_table.loc[group]\n",
        "            g_counts = {c: int(g_row.get(c, 0)) for c in range(CFG.expected_num_classes)}\n",
        "            g_n = int(g_row[\"n_total\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "            split_scores = []\n",
        "            for split in split_names:\n",
        "                tmp_counts = {k: defaultdict(int, v) for k, v in counts.items()}\n",
        "                tmp_n = dict(n_counts)\n",
        "                for c, val in g_counts.items():\n",
        "                    tmp_counts[split][c] += int(val)\n",
        "                tmp_n[split] += g_n\n",
        "                penalty = assignment_score(tmp_counts, tmp_n)\n",
        "                split_scores.append((penalty, split))\n",
        "\n",
        "            split_scores.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n",
        "            chosen_split = split_scores[0][1]\n",
        "            assignment[group] = chosen_split\n",
        "            for c, val in g_counts.items():\n",
        "                counts[chosen_split][c] += int(val)\n",
        "            n_counts[chosen_split] += g_n\n",
        "\n",
        "        # Hard requirements: every split must have at least one image and ideally both classes.\n",
        "        ok = all(n_counts[split] > 0 for split in split_names)\n",
        "        if ok:\n",
        "            for split in split_names:\n",
        "                present_classes = sum(1 for c in range(CFG.expected_num_classes) if counts[split].get(c, 0) > 0)\n",
        "                if present_classes < min(CFG.expected_num_classes, 2):\n",
        "                    ok = False\n",
        "                    break\n",
        "\n",
        "        score = assignment_score(counts, n_counts)\n",
        "        if ok and score < best_score:\n",
        "            best_score = score\n",
        "            best_assignment = assignment\n",
        "\n",
        "    if best_assignment is None:\n",
        "        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find a satisfactory group-aware split assignment.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    return best_assignment\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def stratified_image_level_split(df: pd.DataFrame, seed: int) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "    work = df.copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "    train_valid_idx, test_idx = train_test_split(\n",
        "        np.arange(len(work)),\n",
        "        test_size=CFG.test_fraction,\n",
        "        random_state=seed,\n",
        "        stratify=work[\"label_idx\"] if CFG.stratify_split else None,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    remaining = work.iloc[train_valid_idx].reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "    valid_fraction_adjusted = CFG.valid_fraction / max(1e-8, (CFG.train_fraction + CFG.valid_fraction))\n",
        "    train_idx_2, valid_idx_2 = train_test_split(\n",
        "        np.arange(len(remaining)),\n",
        "        test_size=valid_fraction_adjusted,\n",
        "        random_state=seed,\n",
        "        stratify=remaining[\"label_idx\"] if CFG.stratify_split else None,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    split_series = pd.Series(index=work.index, dtype=object)\n",
        "    split_series.iloc[test_idx] = \"test\"\n",
        "    split_series.iloc[train_valid_idx[train_idx_2]] = \"train\"\n",
        "    split_series.iloc[train_valid_idx[valid_idx_2]] = \"valid\"\n",
        "    work[\"split_canonical\"] = split_series.values\n",
        "    work[\"split_build_strategy\"] = \"fallback_image_level_stratified\"\n",
        "    work[\"split_build_reason\"] = \"group_split_failed_fallback\"\n",
        "    return work\n",
        "\n",
        "def assign_canonical_splits(df: pd.DataFrame, seed: int) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    work = df[~df[\"corrupt\"]].copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "    trusted_raw, reasons = is_raw_split_trustworthy(work)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if trusted_raw and CFG.prefer_raw_splits_when_trustworthy:\n",
        "        work[\"split_canonical\"] = work[\"source_split\"].map(SPLIT_ALIASES).fillna(work[\"source_split\"])\n",
        "        strategy = \"trusted_raw_splits\"\n",
        "        reason_blob = \"raw splits preserved as canonical\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            assignment = random_greedy_group_split(\n",
        "                work,\n",
        "                seed=seed,\n",
        "                ratios=(CFG.train_fraction, CFG.valid_fraction, CFG.test_fraction),\n",
        "                group_col=\"group_id\",\n",
        "                label_col=\"label_idx\",\n",
        "                trials=CFG.group_trial_count,\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            work[\"split_canonical\"] = work[\"group_id\"].map(assignment)\n",
        "            strategy = \"rebuilt_group_aware\"\n",
        "            reason_blob = \"; \".join(reasons) if reasons else \"raw splits not used\"\n",
        "        except Exception as exc:\n",
        "            print(f\"WARNING: group-aware split failed ({exc}); falling back to image-level stratified split.\")\n",
        "            return stratified_image_level_split(work, seed=seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "    work[\"split_build_strategy\"] = strategy\n",
        "    work[\"split_build_reason\"] = reason_blob\n",
        "    return work\n",
        "\n",
        "with timed_block(\"Canonical split assignment\"):\n",
        "    canonical_manifest_df = assign_canonical_splits(canonical_manifest_df, seed=CFG.random_seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "split_manifest_path = CFG.paths.split_root / \"canonical_split_manifest.csv\"\n",
        "canonical_manifest_df.to_csv(split_manifest_path, index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "split_audit_df = split_counts_table(canonical_manifest_df, \"split_canonical\")\n",
        "split_audit_path = CFG.paths.split_root / \"split_audit.csv\"\n",
        "split_audit_df.to_csv(split_audit_path, index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "canonical_group_overlap = (\n",
        "    canonical_manifest_df.groupby([\"group_id\", \"split_canonical\"]).size().unstack(fill_value=0)\n",
        ")\n",
        "canonical_group_overlap[\"num_splits_present\"] = (canonical_group_overlap > 0).sum(axis=1)\n",
        "canonical_group_overlap_df = canonical_group_overlap[canonical_group_overlap[\"num_splits_present\"] > 1].reset_index()\n",
        "canonical_group_overlap_df.to_csv(CFG.paths.split_root / \"canonical_group_overlap.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "print_rule(\"CANONICAL SPLIT AUDIT\")\n",
        "display(split_audit_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "if not canonical_group_overlap_df.empty:\n",
        "    print_rule(\"WARNING — CANONICAL GROUP OVERLAP DETECTED\")\n",
        "    display(canonical_group_overlap_df.head(10))\n",
        "else:\n",
        "    print(\"No inferred group overlap across canonical splits.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "for split_name in [\"train\", \"valid\", \"test\"]:\n",
        "    subset = canonical_manifest_df[canonical_manifest_df[\"split_canonical\"] == split_name]\n",
        "    if subset.empty:\n",
        "        raise RuntimeError(f\"Canonical split '{split_name}' is empty.\")\n",
        "    class_counts = subset[\"label\"].value_counts().reindex(CFG.class_names, fill_value=0)\n",
        "    if (class_counts < CFG.min_images_per_class_per_split).any():\n",
        "        print(f\"WARNING: split={split_name} has very low class counts:\\n{class_counts}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Saved canonical split manifest to:\", split_manifest_path.resolve())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "18e5e576",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "18e5e576"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section G — Creating Image Variations (Branches)\n",
        "\n",
        "Sometimes AI learns the wrong things—like assuming that a darker background means \"male\".\n",
        "\n",
        "To test if our model is actually looking at the fly, we create multiple \"branches\" (versions) of our dataset:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **RAW** — The original, untouched image.\n",
        "2. **TIGHT_CROP** — Zoomed in right on the fly.\n",
        "3. **BACKGROUND_REDUCED** — The background is blurred out to force the AI to focus on the bug.\n",
        "4. **STANDARDIZED_FRAME** — The fly is centered nicely on a blank canvas.\n",
        "\n",
        "We can train and test models on these different versions to see what works best."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "05f3d4bd",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "05f3d4bd"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION G — Branch materialization\n",
        "\n",
        "def clamp_xyxy(x1: float, y1: float, x2: float, y2: float, w: int, h: int) -> Tuple[int, int, int, int]:\n",
        "    x1 = int(max(0, min(round(x1), w - 1)))\n",
        "    y1 = int(max(0, min(round(y1), h - 1)))\n",
        "    x2 = int(max(x1 + 1, min(round(x2), w)))\n",
        "    y2 = int(max(y1 + 1, min(round(y2), h)))\n",
        "    return x1, y1, x2, y2\n",
        "\n",
        "def bbox_xyxy_from_record(row: pd.Series) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int, int, int]]:\n",
        "    if any(pd.isna(row.get(col)) for col in [\"bbox_xc\", \"bbox_yc\", \"bbox_w\", \"bbox_h\", \"width\", \"height\"]):\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    x1, y1, x2, y2 = yolo_bbox_to_xyxy(\n",
        "        float(row[\"bbox_xc\"]),\n",
        "        float(row[\"bbox_yc\"]),\n",
        "        float(row[\"bbox_w\"]),\n",
        "        float(row[\"bbox_h\"]),\n",
        "        int(row[\"width\"]),\n",
        "        int(row[\"height\"]),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return clamp_xyxy(x1, y1, x2, y2, int(row[\"width\"]), int(row[\"height\"]))\n",
        "\n",
        "def expand_bbox(box: Tuple[int, int, int, int], image_size: Tuple[int, int], margin_frac: float) -> Tuple[int, int, int, int]:\n",
        "    x1, y1, x2, y2 = box\n",
        "    w = x2 - x1\n",
        "    h = y2 - y1\n",
        "    margin_x = w * margin_frac\n",
        "    margin_y = h * margin_frac\n",
        "    return clamp_xyxy(x1 - margin_x, y1 - margin_y, x2 + margin_x, y2 + margin_y, image_size[0], image_size[1])\n",
        "\n",
        "def robust_background_color(img: Image.Image) -> Tuple[int, int, int]:\n",
        "    arr = np.asarray(img.convert(\"RGB\"))\n",
        "    return tuple(int(np.median(arr[:, :, i])) for i in range(3))\n",
        "\n",
        "def resize_with_pad(img: Image.Image, target_size: int, fill: Tuple[int, int, int]) -> Image.Image:\n",
        "    img = img.convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "    w, h = img.size\n",
        "    max_side = max(w, h)\n",
        "    pad_left = (max_side - w) // 2\n",
        "    pad_right = max_side - w - pad_left\n",
        "    pad_top = (max_side - h) // 2\n",
        "    pad_bottom = max_side - h - pad_top\n",
        "    img = ImageOps.expand(img, border=(pad_left, pad_top, pad_right, pad_bottom), fill=fill)\n",
        "    img = img.resize((target_size, target_size), Image.Resampling.BILINEAR)\n",
        "    return img\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_branch_image(img: Image.Image, row: pd.Series, branch_name: str) -> Tuple[Image.Image, str]:\n",
        "    img = img.convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "    fill = robust_background_color(img)\n",
        "    box = bbox_xyxy_from_record(row)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if branch_name == \"RAW\":\n",
        "        return img.copy(), \"raw_copy\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    if box is None:\n",
        "        return resize_with_pad(img, CFG.branch_export_size, fill), f\"{branch_name.lower()}_fallback_no_bbox\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    if branch_name == \"TIGHT_CROP\":\n",
        "        crop_box = expand_bbox(box, img.size, CFG.tight_crop_margin)\n",
        "        crop = img.crop(crop_box)\n",
        "        return resize_with_pad(crop, CFG.branch_export_size, fill), \"tight_crop_bbox\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    if branch_name == \"BACKGROUND_REDUCED\":\n",
        "        crop_box = expand_bbox(box, img.size, CFG.background_margin)\n",
        "        x1, y1, x2, y2 = crop_box\n",
        "        arr = np.asarray(img.convert(\"RGB\")).copy()\n",
        "        blurred = np.asarray(img.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(radius=6)).convert(\"RGB\"))\n",
        "        mask = np.zeros(arr.shape[:2], dtype=np.uint8)\n",
        "        mask[y1:y2, x1:x2] = 1\n",
        "        arr[mask == 0] = blurred[mask == 0]\n",
        "        out = Image.fromarray(arr)\n",
        "        return out.resize((CFG.branch_export_size, CFG.branch_export_size), Image.Resampling.BILINEAR), \"background_reduced_bbox\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    if branch_name == \"STANDARDIZED_FRAME\":\n",
        "        crop_box = expand_bbox(box, img.size, CFG.standardized_frame_margin)\n",
        "        crop = img.crop(crop_box).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "        crop = resize_with_pad(crop, int(CFG.branch_export_size * CFG.standardized_object_fraction), fill)\n",
        "        canvas = Image.new(\"RGB\", (CFG.branch_export_size, CFG.branch_export_size), color=fill)\n",
        "        offset_x = (CFG.branch_export_size - crop.size[0]) // 2\n",
        "        offset_y = (CFG.branch_export_size - crop.size[1]) // 2\n",
        "        canvas.paste(crop, (offset_x, offset_y))\n",
        "        return canvas, \"standardized_frame_bbox\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    raise KeyError(f\"Unknown branch_name: {branch_name}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def materialize_branch_manifest(branch_name: str, base_manifest: pd.DataFrame, force: bool = False) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    branch_root = CFG.paths.branch_root / branch_name\n",
        "    manifest_path = branch_root / \"manifest.csv\"\n",
        "    if manifest_path.exists() and not force:\n",
        "        return pd.read_csv(manifest_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "    branch_root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    for row in tqdm(base_manifest.itertuples(index=False), total=len(base_manifest), desc=f\"Branch {branch_name}\"):\n",
        "        src_path = Path(row.filepath)\n",
        "        dst_dir = branch_root / row.split_canonical / row.label\n",
        "        dst_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "        dst_path = dst_dir / f\"{Path(row.file_sha1).stem if row.file_sha1 else strip_roboflow_suffix(src_path.stem)}.png\"\n",
        "\n",
        "        note = \"\"\n",
        "        if not dst_path.exists() or force:\n",
        "            img, err = safe_image_open(src_path)\n",
        "            if img is None:\n",
        "                continue\n",
        "            built_img, note = build_branch_image(img, pd.Series(row._asdict()), branch_name)\n",
        "            built_img.save(dst_path, format=\"PNG\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        rec = dict(row._asdict())\n",
        "        rec[\"branch_name\"] = branch_name\n",
        "        rec[\"branch_filepath\"] = str(dst_path.resolve())\n",
        "        rec[\"branch_note\"] = note\n",
        "        rows.append(rec)\n",
        "\n",
        "    branch_df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "    branch_df.to_csv(manifest_path, index=False)\n",
        "    return branch_df\n",
        "\n",
        "BRANCH_MANIFESTS: Dict[str, pd.DataFrame] = {}\n",
        "with timed_block(\"Branch materialization\"):\n",
        "    for branch_name in CFG.branch_names_enabled:\n",
        "        BRANCH_MANIFESTS[branch_name] = materialize_branch_manifest(\n",
        "            branch_name,\n",
        "            canonical_manifest_df,\n",
        "            force=CFG.force_rebuild_branches,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "preview_branch = \"RAW\" if \"RAW\" in BRANCH_MANIFESTS else list(BRANCH_MANIFESTS.keys())[0]\n",
        "print_rule(\"BRANCH MANIFEST SUMMARY\")\n",
        "for branch_name, branch_df in BRANCH_MANIFESTS.items():\n",
        "    counts = branch_df.groupby([\"split_canonical\", \"label\"]).size().unstack(fill_value=0).reindex(columns=CFG.class_names, fill_value=0)\n",
        "    print(f\"Branch={branch_name}\")\n",
        "    display(counts)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Save a small side-by-side branch preview for quick visual sanity-checking.\n",
        "preview_dir = CFG.paths.analysis_root / \"branch_previews\"\n",
        "preview_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "sample_rows = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[preview_branch].sample(min(6, len(BRANCH_MANIFESTS[preview_branch])), random_state=CFG.random_seed)\n",
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(len(sample_rows), len(BRANCH_MANIFESTS), figsize=(3.2 * len(BRANCH_MANIFESTS), 2.8 * len(sample_rows)), dpi=140)\n",
        "if len(sample_rows) == 1:\n",
        "    axes = np.array([axes])\n",
        "if axes.ndim == 1:\n",
        "    axes = axes[None, :]\n",
        "for r, (_, base_row) in enumerate(sample_rows.iterrows()):\n",
        "    for c, branch_name in enumerate(BRANCH_MANIFESTS.keys()):\n",
        "        ax = axes[r, c]\n",
        "        branch_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[branch_name]\n",
        "        row_match = branch_df[branch_df[\"file_sha1\"] == base_row[\"file_sha1\"]]\n",
        "        if row_match.empty:\n",
        "            ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        img = Image.open(row_match.iloc[0][\"branch_filepath\"]).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "        ax.imshow(img)\n",
        "        ax.set_title(f\"{branch_name}\\n{row_match.iloc[0]['label']}\", fontsize=9)\n",
        "        ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.savefig(preview_dir / \"branch_preview_grid.png\")\n",
        "plt.close()\n",
        "print(\"Saved branch preview grid to:\", (preview_dir / \"branch_preview_grid.png\").resolve())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "cf8b04ef",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cf8b04ef"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section H — Image Augmentation (Adding Noise, Flips, etc.)\n",
        "\n",
        "To make our AI smarter, we randomly tweak the training images. This is called \"Augmentation\". By rotating, flipping, and changing the brightness of the flies, the model learns to recognize them in any situation.\n",
        "\n",
        "We have a few policies ranging from `none` to `medium` to `morphology_safe_strong`.\n",
        "\n",
        "We only apply these tweaks to the **Training** data. The Validation and Test sets are kept pristine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "6d748bb7",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6d748bb7"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION H — Augmentation policies, cache materialization, and dataset wrappers\n",
        "\n",
        "AUG_POLICIES: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {\n",
        "    \"none\": {\n",
        "        \"copies_per_image\": 0,\n",
        "        \"rotation_degrees\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"translate\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"scale_min\": 1.0,\n",
        "        \"scale_max\": 1.0,\n",
        "        \"hflip_p\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"brightness\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"contrast\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"saturation\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"hue\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"blur_p\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"blur_radius\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"noise_std\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"grayscale_p\": 0.0,\n",
        "        \"gamma_jitter\": 0.0,\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"light\": {\n",
        "        \"copies_per_image\": CFG.max_offline_aug_copies_per_image,\n",
        "        \"rotation_degrees\": 4.0,\n",
        "        \"translate\": 0.02,\n",
        "        \"scale_min\": 0.98,\n",
        "        \"scale_max\": 1.03,\n",
        "        \"hflip_p\": 0.50,\n",
        "        \"brightness\": 0.05,\n",
        "        \"contrast\": 0.05,\n",
        "        \"saturation\": 0.03,\n",
        "        \"hue\": 0.01,\n",
        "        \"blur_p\": 0.05,\n",
        "        \"blur_radius\": 0.8,\n",
        "        \"noise_std\": 0.01,\n",
        "        \"grayscale_p\": 0.05,\n",
        "        \"gamma_jitter\": 0.03,\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"medium\": {\n",
        "        \"copies_per_image\": CFG.max_offline_aug_copies_per_image,\n",
        "        \"rotation_degrees\": 8.0,\n",
        "        \"translate\": 0.03,\n",
        "        \"scale_min\": 0.95,\n",
        "        \"scale_max\": 1.05,\n",
        "        \"hflip_p\": 0.50,\n",
        "        \"brightness\": 0.08,\n",
        "        \"contrast\": 0.08,\n",
        "        \"saturation\": 0.05,\n",
        "        \"hue\": 0.015,\n",
        "        \"blur_p\": 0.10,\n",
        "        \"blur_radius\": 1.1,\n",
        "        \"noise_std\": 0.015,\n",
        "        \"grayscale_p\": 0.08,\n",
        "        \"gamma_jitter\": 0.05,\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"morphology_safe_strong\": {\n",
        "        \"copies_per_image\": CFG.max_offline_aug_copies_per_image,\n",
        "        \"rotation_degrees\": 10.0,\n",
        "        \"translate\": 0.04,\n",
        "        \"scale_min\": 0.93,\n",
        "        \"scale_max\": 1.06,\n",
        "        \"hflip_p\": 0.50,\n",
        "        \"brightness\": 0.10,\n",
        "        \"contrast\": 0.10,\n",
        "        \"saturation\": 0.06,\n",
        "        \"hue\": 0.015,\n",
        "        \"blur_p\": 0.12,\n",
        "        \"blur_radius\": 1.3,\n",
        "        \"noise_std\": 0.02,\n",
        "        \"grayscale_p\": 0.10,\n",
        "        \"gamma_jitter\": 0.06,\n",
        "    },\n",
        "    \"background_robustness\": {\n",
        "        \"copies_per_image\": CFG.max_offline_aug_copies_per_image,\n",
        "        \"rotation_degrees\": 6.0,\n",
        "        \"translate\": 0.03,\n",
        "        \"scale_min\": 0.95,\n",
        "        \"scale_max\": 1.05,\n",
        "        \"hflip_p\": 0.50,\n",
        "        \"brightness\": 0.06,\n",
        "        \"contrast\": 0.06,\n",
        "        \"saturation\": 0.02,\n",
        "        \"hue\": 0.01,\n",
        "        \"blur_p\": 0.08,\n",
        "        \"blur_radius\": 0.9,\n",
        "        \"noise_std\": 0.01,\n",
        "        \"grayscale_p\": 0.12,\n",
        "        \"gamma_jitter\": 0.04,\n",
        "    },\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "class SquarePadResize:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, size: int, fill: Tuple[int, int, int] = (0, 0, 0)):\n",
        "        self.size = int(size)\n",
        "        self.fill = fill\n",
        "\n",
        "    def __call__(self, img: Image.Image) -> Image.Image:\n",
        "        img = img.convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "        w, h = img.size\n",
        "        side = max(w, h)\n",
        "        pad_left = (side - w) // 2\n",
        "        pad_right = side - w - pad_left\n",
        "        pad_top = (side - h) // 2\n",
        "        pad_bottom = side - h - pad_top\n",
        "        img = ImageOps.expand(img, border=(pad_left, pad_top, pad_right, pad_bottom), fill=self.fill)\n",
        "        img = img.resize((self.size, self.size), Image.Resampling.BILINEAR)\n",
        "        return img\n",
        "\n",
        "class AddGaussianNoiseTensor:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, std: float):\n",
        "        self.std = float(std)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def __call__(self, x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n",
        "        if self.std <= 0:\n",
        "            return x\n",
        "        return torch.clamp(x + torch.randn_like(x) * self.std, 0.0, 1.0)\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_eval_transform(image_size: int) -> T.Compose:\n",
        "    return T.Compose([\n",
        "        SquarePadResize(image_size),\n",
        "        T.ToTensor(),\n",
        "        T.Normalize(mean=CFG.imagenet_mean, std=CFG.imagenet_std),\n",
        "    ])\n",
        "\n",
        "def deterministic_seed_for_path(path_key: str, policy_name: str, copy_idx: int, seed: int) -> int:\n",
        "    digest = __import__(\"hashlib\").sha1(f\"{path_key}_{policy_name}_{copy_idx}_{seed}\".encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()\n",
        "    return int(digest[:8], 16)\n",
        "\n",
        "def apply_gamma_jitter(img: Image.Image, gamma_delta: float) -> Image.Image:\n",
        "    if gamma_delta <= 0:\n",
        "        return img\n",
        "    gamma = 1.0 + np.random.uniform(-gamma_delta, gamma_delta)\n",
        "    arr = np.asarray(img).astype(np.float32) / 255.0\n",
        "    arr = np.clip(arr, 0.0, 1.0) ** gamma\n",
        "    arr = (np.clip(arr, 0.0, 1.0) * 255.0).astype(np.uint8)\n",
        "    return Image.fromarray(arr)\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_offline_augmenter(policy_name: str):\n",
        "    cfg = AUG_POLICIES[policy_name]\n",
        "\n",
        "    def _augment(img: Image.Image) -> Image.Image:\n",
        "        img = img.convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        if cfg[\"rotation_degrees\"] > 0 or cfg[\"translate\"] > 0 or cfg[\"scale_min\"] != 1.0 or cfg[\"scale_max\"] != 1.0:\n",
        "            angle = np.random.uniform(-cfg[\"rotation_degrees\"], cfg[\"rotation_degrees\"])\n",
        "            max_dx = cfg[\"translate\"] * img.size[0]\n",
        "            max_dy = cfg[\"translate\"] * img.size[1]\n",
        "            translations = (np.random.uniform(-max_dx, max_dx), np.random.uniform(-max_dy, max_dy))\n",
        "            scale = np.random.uniform(cfg[\"scale_min\"], cfg[\"scale_max\"])\n",
        "            img = T.functional.affine(\n",
        "                img,\n",
        "                angle=angle,\n",
        "                translate=(int(translations[0]), int(translations[1])),\n",
        "                scale=scale,\n",
        "                shear=[0.0, 0.0],\n",
        "                interpolation=T.InterpolationMode.BILINEAR,\n",
        "                fill=robust_background_color(img),\n",
        "            )\n",
        "\n",
        "        if np.random.rand() < cfg[\"hflip_p\"]:\n",
        "            img = ImageOps.mirror(img)\n",
        "\n",
        "        if any([cfg[\"brightness\"] > 0, cfg[\"contrast\"] > 0, cfg[\"saturation\"] > 0, cfg[\"hue\"] > 0]):\n",
        "            img = T.ColorJitter(\n",
        "                brightness=cfg[\"brightness\"],\n",
        "                contrast=cfg[\"contrast\"],\n",
        "                saturation=cfg[\"saturation\"],\n",
        "                hue=cfg[\"hue\"],\n",
        "            )(img)\n",
        "\n",
        "        if cfg[\"gamma_jitter\"] > 0:\n",
        "            img = apply_gamma_jitter(img, cfg[\"gamma_jitter\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "        if cfg[\"blur_p\"] > 0 and np.random.rand() < cfg[\"blur_p\"]:\n",
        "            img = img.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(radius=float(cfg[\"blur_radius\"])))\n",
        "\n",
        "        if cfg[\"grayscale_p\"] > 0 and np.random.rand() < cfg[\"grayscale_p\"]:\n",
        "            img = ImageOps.grayscale(img).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        if cfg[\"noise_std\"] > 0:\n",
        "            arr = np.asarray(img).astype(np.float32) / 255.0\n",
        "            arr = np.clip(arr + np.random.normal(0.0, cfg[\"noise_std\"], arr.shape), 0.0, 1.0)\n",
        "            img = Image.fromarray((arr * 255.0).astype(np.uint8))\n",
        "\n",
        "        return img\n",
        "\n",
        "    return _augment\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_online_train_transform(image_size: int, policy_name: str) -> T.Compose:\n",
        "    policy = AUG_POLICIES[policy_name]\n",
        "    ops: List[Any] = [SquarePadResize(image_size)]\n",
        "    if policy_name != \"none\":\n",
        "        ops.extend([\n",
        "            T.RandomApply([T.RandomRotation(degrees=policy[\"rotation_degrees\"], fill=0)], p=0.7 if policy[\"rotation_degrees\"] > 0 else 0.0),\n",
        "            T.RandomHorizontalFlip(p=policy[\"hflip_p\"]),\n",
        "            T.ColorJitter(\n",
        "                brightness=policy[\"brightness\"],\n",
        "                contrast=policy[\"contrast\"],\n",
        "                saturation=policy[\"saturation\"],\n",
        "                hue=policy[\"hue\"],\n",
        "            ) if any([policy[\"brightness\"], policy[\"contrast\"], policy[\"saturation\"], policy[\"hue\"]]) else T.Lambda(lambda x: x),\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "    ops.extend([\n",
        "        T.ToTensor(),\n",
        "        AddGaussianNoiseTensor(policy[\"noise_std\"]),\n",
        "        T.Normalize(mean=CFG.imagenet_mean, std=CFG.imagenet_std),\n",
        "    ])\n",
        "    return T.Compose(ops)\n",
        "\n",
        "def materialize_offline_aug_manifest(branch_name: str, policy_name: str, force: bool = False) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    if policy_name not in AUG_POLICIES:\n",
        "        raise KeyError(f\"Unknown augmentation policy: {policy_name}\")\n",
        "    branch_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[branch_name].copy()\n",
        "    cache_root = CFG.paths.aug_cache_root / branch_name / policy_name\n",
        "    cache_manifest_path = cache_root / \"manifest.csv\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    if cache_manifest_path.exists() and not force:\n",
        "        return pd.read_csv(cache_manifest_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "    cache_root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    # originals for all splits\n",
        "    for row in branch_df.itertuples(index=False):\n",
        "        rec = dict(row._asdict())\n",
        "        rec[\"aug_policy\"] = policy_name\n",
        "        rec[\"is_augmented\"] = False\n",
        "        rec[\"aug_copy_idx\"] = -1\n",
        "        rec[\"augmented_filepath\"] = rec[\"branch_filepath\"]\n",
        "        rows.append(rec)\n",
        "\n",
        "    copies_per_image = int(AUG_POLICIES[policy_name][\"copies_per_image\"])\n",
        "    if policy_name != \"none\" and copies_per_image > 0:\n",
        "        augmenter = build_offline_augmenter(policy_name)\n",
        "        train_rows = branch_df[branch_df[\"split_canonical\"] == \"train\"].copy()\n",
        "        for row in tqdm(train_rows.itertuples(index=False), total=len(train_rows), desc=f\"Offline aug {branch_name}/{policy_name}\"):\n",
        "            src_path = Path(row.branch_filepath)\n",
        "            for copy_idx in range(copies_per_image):\n",
        "                seed = deterministic_seed_for_path(str(row.file_sha1), policy_name, copy_idx, CFG.random_seed)\n",
        "                random.seed(seed)\n",
        "                np.random.seed(seed)\n",
        "                torch.manual_seed(seed)\n",
        "\n",
        "                dst_dir = cache_root / \"train\" / row.label\n",
        "                dst_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "                dst_path = dst_dir / f\"{Path(row.branch_filepath).stem}__aug_{policy_name}_{copy_idx:02d}.png\"\n",
        "\n",
        "                if not dst_path.exists() or force:\n",
        "                    img = Image.open(src_path).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "                    augmenter(img).save(dst_path, format=\"PNG\")\n",
        "\n",
        "                rec = dict(row._asdict())\n",
        "                rec[\"aug_policy\"] = policy_name\n",
        "                rec[\"is_augmented\"] = True\n",
        "                rec[\"aug_copy_idx\"] = int(copy_idx)\n",
        "                rec[\"augmented_filepath\"] = str(dst_path.resolve())\n",
        "                rows.append(rec)\n",
        "\n",
        "    aug_df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "    aug_df.to_csv(cache_manifest_path, index=False)\n",
        "    metadata = {\n",
        "        \"branch_name\": branch_name,\n",
        "        \"policy_name\": policy_name,\n",
        "        \"policy_cfg\": AUG_POLICIES[policy_name],\n",
        "        \"created_at\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    with open(cache_root / \"cache_metadata.json\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "        json.dump(metadata, f, indent=2)\n",
        "    return aug_df\n",
        "\n",
        "class ManifestImageDataset(torch.utils.data.Dataset):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, df: pd.DataFrame, image_path_col: str, transform: Any):\n",
        "        self.df = df.reset_index(drop=True).copy()\n",
        "        self.image_path_col = image_path_col\n",
        "        self.transform = transform\n",
        "\n",
        "    def __len__(self) -> int:\n",
        "        return len(self.df)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def __getitem__(self, idx: int):\n",
        "        row = self.df.iloc[idx]\n",
        "        img = Image.open(row[self.image_path_col]).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "        x = self.transform(img)\n",
        "        y = int(row[\"label_idx\"])\n",
        "        meta = {\n",
        "            \"filepath\": row[self.image_path_col],\n",
        "            \"source_filepath\": row[\"filepath\"],\n",
        "            \"file_sha1\": row[\"file_sha1\"],\n",
        "            \"label\": row[\"label\"],\n",
        "            \"split_canonical\": row[\"split_canonical\"],\n",
        "            \"group_id\": row[\"group_id\"],\n",
        "            \"branch_name\": row.get(\"branch_name\", \"RAW\"),\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        return x, y, meta\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_class_weight_tensor(train_df: pd.DataFrame) -> Optional[torch.Tensor]:\n",
        "    counts = train_df[\"label_idx\"].value_counts().reindex(list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes)), fill_value=0).astype(float)\n",
        "    if counts.min() <= 0:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    imbalance_ratio = counts.max() / counts.min()\n",
        "    if imbalance_ratio < CFG.imbalance_ratio_trigger or not CFG.use_class_weights_when_imbalanced:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    weights = counts.sum() / (len(counts) * counts)\n",
        "    return torch.tensor(weights.values, dtype=torch.float32)\n",
        "\n",
        "def maybe_build_weighted_sampler(train_df: pd.DataFrame) -> Optional[torch.utils.data.WeightedRandomSampler]:\n",
        "    counts = train_df[\"label_idx\"].value_counts().reindex(list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes)), fill_value=0).astype(float)\n",
        "    if counts.min() <= 0:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    imbalance_ratio = counts.max() / counts.min()\n",
        "    if imbalance_ratio < CFG.imbalance_ratio_trigger:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    sample_weights = train_df[\"label_idx\"].map(lambda idx: 1.0 / counts.loc[idx]).values.astype(np.float64)\n",
        "    return torch.utils.data.WeightedRandomSampler(\n",
        "        weights=torch.as_tensor(sample_weights, dtype=torch.double),\n",
        "        num_samples=len(sample_weights),\n",
        "        replacement=True,\n",
        "    )\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "7d625174",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7d625174"
      },
      "source": [
        "## SECTION I + J — Experiment specs, model builders, and trainer wrappers\n",
        "\n",
        "The benchmark supports three core model families:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **old checkpoint transfer** using the provided fruit fly model\n",
        "- **generic pretrained baseline** using stable torchvision classifiers\n",
        "- **scratch baseline** using the same backbone families without pretrained weights\n",
        "\n",
        "The training loop is a custom PyTorch loop. This avoids the brittle trainer interactions that often appear when mixing custom dataset logic, branch-specific preprocessing, and non-native backbones in a single external training API.\n",
        "\n",
        "The notebook still uses the old checkpoint directly, but all benchmark training is controlled by explicit code here.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "b5f809da",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b5f809da"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION I + J — Experiment specs, model factories, training loop, checkpointing\n",
        "\n",
        "@dataclass\n",
        "class ExperimentSpec:\n",
        "    run_name: str\n",
        "    family: str\n",
        "    architecture: str\n",
        "    init_mode: str\n",
        "    branch_name: str\n",
        "    aug_policy: str\n",
        "    image_size: int\n",
        "    batch_size: int\n",
        "    epochs: int\n",
        "    patience: int\n",
        "    lr: float\n",
        "    weight_decay: float\n",
        "    optimizer_name: str = \"AdamW\"\n",
        "    dropout: float = 0.0\n",
        "    label_smoothing: float = 0.0\n",
        "    freeze_backbone_epochs: int = 0\n",
        "    stronger_regularization: bool = False\n",
        "    class_balancing: str = \"auto\"  # auto | class_weight | weighted_sampler | none\n",
        "    loss_name: str = \"ce\"          # ce | focal\n",
        "    focal_gamma: float = 1.5\n",
        "    notes: str = \"\"\n",
        "    seed: int = 1337\n",
        "    use_offline_aug_cache: bool = True\n",
        "    use_online_aug: bool = False\n",
        "    final_retrain: bool = False\n",
        "\n",
        "def spec_to_recipe_key(spec: ExperimentSpec) -> str:\n",
        "    fields = [\n",
        "        spec.family, spec.architecture, spec.init_mode, spec.branch_name, spec.aug_policy,\n",
        "        f\"img{spec.image_size}\", f\"lr{spec.lr}\", f\"wd{spec.weight_decay}\",\n",
        "        f\"drop{spec.dropout}\", f\"ls{spec.label_smoothing}\", f\"freeze{spec.freeze_backbone_epochs}\",\n",
        "        spec.class_balancing, spec.loss_name,\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    return \"__\".join([normalize_token(x) for x in fields])\n",
        "\n",
        "def save_json(path: Path, obj: Any) -> None:\n",
        "    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    with open(path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "        json.dump(obj, f, indent=2, default=str)\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_json(path: Path) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    return json.loads(Path(path).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "def get_run_dir(spec: ExperimentSpec) -> Path:\n",
        "    return CFG.paths.experiment_root / spec.run_name\n",
        "\n",
        "def replace_last_linear_in_module(module: nn.Module, out_features: int) -> bool:\n",
        "    named = list(module.named_modules())\n",
        "    for name, submodule in reversed(named):\n",
        "        if isinstance(submodule, nn.Linear):\n",
        "            parent = module\n",
        "            parent_name = name.rsplit(\".\", 1)[0] if \".\" in name else \"\"\n",
        "            if parent_name:\n",
        "                for token in parent_name.split(\".\"):\n",
        "                    parent = getattr(parent, token)\n",
        "            last_name = name.split(\".\")[-1]\n",
        "            new_layer = nn.Linear(submodule.in_features, out_features)\n",
        "            setattr(parent, last_name, new_layer)\n",
        "            return True\n",
        "    return False\n",
        "\n",
        "def try_wrap_classifier_with_dropout(module: nn.Module, p: float) -> None:\n",
        "    if p <= 0:\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    if hasattr(module, \"fc\") and isinstance(module.fc, nn.Linear):\n",
        "        module.fc = nn.Sequential(nn.Dropout(p), module.fc)\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    if hasattr(module, \"classifier\"):\n",
        "        classifier = getattr(module, \"classifier\")\n",
        "        if isinstance(classifier, nn.Linear):\n",
        "            setattr(module, \"classifier\", nn.Sequential(nn.Dropout(p), classifier))\n",
        "            return\n",
        "        if isinstance(classifier, nn.Sequential):\n",
        "            layers = list(classifier.children())\n",
        "            if layers and isinstance(layers[-1], nn.Linear):\n",
        "                layers.insert(len(layers) - 1, nn.Dropout(p))\n",
        "                setattr(module, \"classifier\", nn.Sequential(*layers))\n",
        "                return\n",
        "    # Generic fallback: wrap the final linear inside its parent.\n",
        "    named = list(module.named_modules())\n",
        "    for name, submodule in reversed(named):\n",
        "        if isinstance(submodule, nn.Linear):\n",
        "            parent = module\n",
        "            parent_name = name.rsplit(\".\", 1)[0] if \".\" in name else \"\"\n",
        "            if parent_name:\n",
        "                for token in parent_name.split(\".\"):\n",
        "                    parent = getattr(parent, token)\n",
        "            last_name = name.split(\".\")[-1]\n",
        "            setattr(parent, last_name, nn.Sequential(nn.Dropout(p), submodule))\n",
        "            return\n",
        "\n",
        "def infer_model_family_for_bundle(spec: ExperimentSpec) -> str:\n",
        "    return spec.family\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_torchvision_model(architecture: str, num_classes: int, pretrained: bool, dropout: float) -> nn.Module:\n",
        "    arch = architecture.lower()\n",
        "    if arch == \"resnet18\":\n",
        "        weights = torchvision.models.ResNet18_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1 if pretrained else None\n",
        "        model = torchvision.models.resnet18(weights=weights)\n",
        "        model.fc = nn.Linear(model.fc.in_features, num_classes)\n",
        "    elif arch == \"efficientnet_b0\":\n",
        "        weights = torchvision.models.EfficientNet_B0_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1 if pretrained else None\n",
        "        model = torchvision.models.efficientnet_b0(weights=weights)\n",
        "        in_features = model.classifier[-1].in_features\n",
        "        model.classifier[-1] = nn.Linear(in_features, num_classes)\n",
        "    elif arch == \"mobilenet_v3_small\":\n",
        "        weights = torchvision.models.MobileNet_V3_Small_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1 if pretrained else None\n",
        "        model = torchvision.models.mobilenet_v3_small(weights=weights)\n",
        "        in_features = model.classifier[-1].in_features\n",
        "        model.classifier[-1] = nn.Linear(in_features, num_classes)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        raise KeyError(f\"Unsupported torchvision architecture: {architecture}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    try_wrap_classifier_with_dropout(model, dropout)\n",
        "    return model\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_ultralytics_model(architecture_or_ckpt: str, num_classes: int, dropout: float) -> nn.Module:\n",
        "    yolo = YOLO(architecture_or_ckpt)\n",
        "    model = yolo.model\n",
        "    # Ensure the final classifier head matches the target class count.\n",
        "    ok = replace_last_linear_in_module(model, num_classes)\n",
        "    if not ok:\n",
        "        raise RuntimeError(f\"Could not replace the classifier head for Ultralytics model: {architecture_or_ckpt}\")\n",
        "    try_wrap_classifier_with_dropout(model, dropout)\n",
        "    if hasattr(model, \"names\"):\n",
        "        model.names = {i: name for i, name in enumerate(CFG.class_names)}\n",
        "    return model\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_model_from_spec(spec: ExperimentSpec) -> nn.Module:\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"old_checkpoint\":\n",
        "        if CFG.old_model_path is None or not Path(CFG.old_model_path).exists():\n",
        "            raise FileNotFoundError(\"Old checkpoint path is not available.\")\n",
        "        return build_ultralytics_model(str(CFG.old_model_path), num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"generic_pretrained\":\n",
        "        return build_torchvision_model(spec.architecture, num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, pretrained=True, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"generic_pretrained_2\":\n",
        "        return build_torchvision_model(spec.architecture, num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, pretrained=True, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"scratch_yolo\":\n",
        "        return build_ultralytics_model(spec.architecture, num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"scratch_torchvision\":\n",
        "        return build_torchvision_model(spec.architecture, num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, pretrained=False, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    raise KeyError(f\"Unknown spec.family: {spec.family}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def freeze_backbone(model: nn.Module, spec: ExperimentSpec) -> None:\n",
        "    for param in model.parameters():\n",
        "        param.requires_grad = False\n",
        "\n",
        "    if hasattr(model, \"fc\"):\n",
        "        for param in model.fc.parameters():\n",
        "            param.requires_grad = True\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    if hasattr(model, \"classifier\"):\n",
        "        classifier = getattr(model, \"classifier\")\n",
        "        for param in classifier.parameters():\n",
        "            param.requires_grad = True\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    if hasattr(model, \"model\") and isinstance(model.model, (nn.ModuleList, list)) and len(model.model) > 0:\n",
        "        for param in model.model[-1].parameters():\n",
        "            param.requires_grad = True\n",
        "        return\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Fallback: unfreeze last linear layer only.\n",
        "    for name, submodule in reversed(list(model.named_modules())):\n",
        "        if isinstance(submodule, nn.Linear):\n",
        "            for param in submodule.parameters():\n",
        "                param.requires_grad = True\n",
        "            return\n",
        "\n",
        "def unfreeze_all(model: nn.Module) -> None:\n",
        "    for param in model.parameters():\n",
        "        param.requires_grad = True\n",
        "\n",
        "def extract_logits(output: Any) -> torch.Tensor:\n",
        "    if isinstance(output, dict):\n",
        "        if \"logits\" in output:\n",
        "            output = output[\"logits\"]\n",
        "        elif \"preds\" in output:\n",
        "            output = output[\"preds\"]\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            raise TypeError(f\"Unsupported dict output keys: {list(output.keys())}\")\n",
        "    if isinstance(output, (list, tuple)):\n",
        "        output = output[0]\n",
        "    if not isinstance(output, torch.Tensor):\n",
        "        raise TypeError(f\"Expected tensor-like model output, got: {type(output)}\")\n",
        "    if output.ndim > 2:\n",
        "        output = output.squeeze(-1).squeeze(-1)\n",
        "    output = output.float()\n",
        "    if tensor_looks_like_probabilities(output):\n",
        "        output = torch.log(torch.clamp(output, 1e-6, 1.0))\n",
        "    return output\n",
        "\n",
        "def tensor_looks_like_probabilities(x: torch.Tensor, tol: float = 1e-3) -> bool:\n",
        "    if x.ndim != 2:\n",
        "        return False\n",
        "    if torch.any(x < -tol) or torch.any(x > 1.0 + tol):\n",
        "        return False\n",
        "    row_sums = x.sum(dim=1)\n",
        "    return bool(torch.all(torch.abs(row_sums - 1.0) < 5 * tol).item())\n",
        "\n",
        "class FocalLoss(nn.Module):\n",
        "    def __init__(self, gamma: float = 1.5, weight: Optional[torch.Tensor] = None):\n",
        "        super().__init__()\n",
        "        self.gamma = gamma\n",
        "        self.weight = weight\n",
        "\n",
        "    def forward(self, logits: torch.Tensor, targets: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n",
        "        log_probs = F.log_softmax(logits, dim=1)\n",
        "        probs = log_probs.exp()\n",
        "        target_log_probs = log_probs.gather(1, targets[:, None]).squeeze(1)\n",
        "        target_probs = probs.gather(1, targets[:, None]).squeeze(1)\n",
        "        focal_factor = (1.0 - target_probs).pow(self.gamma)\n",
        "        loss = -focal_factor * target_log_probs\n",
        "        if self.weight is not None:\n",
        "            class_weights = self.weight.to(logits.device).gather(0, targets)\n",
        "            loss = loss * class_weights\n",
        "        return loss.mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_loss_function(spec: ExperimentSpec, class_weight_tensor: Optional[torch.Tensor]) -> nn.Module:\n",
        "    if spec.loss_name == \"focal\":\n",
        "        return FocalLoss(gamma=spec.focal_gamma, weight=class_weight_tensor)\n",
        "    return nn.CrossEntropyLoss(\n",
        "        weight=class_weight_tensor,\n",
        "        label_smoothing=float(spec.label_smoothing),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_optimizer(model: nn.Module, spec: ExperimentSpec) -> torch.optim.Optimizer:\n",
        "    params = [p for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad]\n",
        "    if spec.optimizer_name.lower() == \"adamw\":\n",
        "        return torch.optim.AdamW(params, lr=spec.lr, weight_decay=spec.weight_decay)\n",
        "    if spec.optimizer_name.lower() == \"sgd\":\n",
        "        return torch.optim.SGD(params, lr=spec.lr, momentum=0.9, nesterov=True, weight_decay=spec.weight_decay)\n",
        "    raise KeyError(f\"Unknown optimizer_name: {spec.optimizer_name}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_scheduler(optimizer: torch.optim.Optimizer, total_epochs: int):\n",
        "    if CFG.scheduler_name.lower() == \"cosine\":\n",
        "        return torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=max(1, total_epochs))\n",
        "    return torch.optim.lr_scheduler.StepLR(optimizer, step_size=max(1, total_epochs // 3), gamma=0.2)\n",
        "\n",
        "def get_device_string_for_autocast(device: str) -> str:\n",
        "    if device.startswith(\"cuda\"):\n",
        "        return \"cuda\"\n",
        "    if device.startswith(\"mps\"):\n",
        "        return \"cpu\"  # MPS autocast is less reliable; keep it conservative.\n",
        "    return \"cpu\"\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_probabilities_from_logits(logits: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n",
        "    if tensor_looks_like_probabilities(logits):\n",
        "        probs = logits\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        probs = logits.softmax(dim=1)\n",
        "    return probs\n",
        "\n",
        "def train_one_epoch(\n",
        "    model: nn.Module,\n",
        "    loader: torch.utils.data.DataLoader,\n",
        "    optimizer: torch.optim.Optimizer,\n",
        "    loss_fn: nn.Module,\n",
        "    device: str,\n",
        "    scaler: Optional[torch.cuda.amp.GradScaler] = None,\n",
        "    max_grad_norm: Optional[float] = None,\n",
        ") -> Dict[str, float]:\n",
        "    model.train()\n",
        "    losses = []\n",
        "    correct = 0\n",
        "    total = 0\n",
        "    device_type = get_device_string_for_autocast(device)\n",
        "    use_amp_here = bool(CFG.use_amp and device.startswith(\"cuda\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "    for batch_x, batch_y, _ in tqdm(loader, desc=\"train\", leave=False):\n",
        "        batch_x = batch_x.to(device, non_blocking=device.startswith(\"cuda\"))\n",
        "        batch_y = batch_y.to(device, non_blocking=device.startswith(\"cuda\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n",
        "        if use_amp_here and scaler is not None:\n",
        "            with torch.autocast(device_type=device_type, dtype=torch.float16):\n",
        "                logits = extract_logits(model(batch_x))\n",
        "                loss = loss_fn(logits, batch_y)\n",
        "            scaler.scale(loss).backward()\n",
        "            if max_grad_norm is not None:\n",
        "                scaler.unscale_(optimizer)\n",
        "                nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), max_grad_norm)\n",
        "            scaler.step(optimizer)\n",
        "            scaler.update()\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            logits = extract_logits(model(batch_x))\n",
        "            loss = loss_fn(logits, batch_y)\n",
        "            loss.backward()\n",
        "            if max_grad_norm is not None:\n",
        "                nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), max_grad_norm)\n",
        "            optimizer.step()\n",
        "\n",
        "        losses.append(float(loss.detach().cpu().item()))\n",
        "        probs = compute_probabilities_from_logits(logits.detach())\n",
        "        preds = probs.argmax(dim=1)\n",
        "        correct += int((preds == batch_y).sum().item())\n",
        "        total += int(batch_y.numel())\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"train_loss\": float(np.mean(losses)) if losses else float(\"nan\"),\n",
        "        \"train_accuracy\": float(correct / max(1, total)),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "def predict_with_model(\n",
        "    model: nn.Module,\n",
        "    loader: torch.utils.data.DataLoader,\n",
        "    device: str,\n",
        "    temperature: float = 1.0,\n",
        "    tta_views: Optional[Tuple[str, ...]] = None,\n",
        ") -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    records: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    def apply_tta_view(batch: torch.Tensor, view_name: str) -> torch.Tensor:\n",
        "        if view_name == \"identity\":\n",
        "            return batch\n",
        "        if view_name == \"hflip\":\n",
        "            return torch.flip(batch, dims=[3])\n",
        "        if view_name == \"rot_pos\":\n",
        "            return T.functional.rotate(batch, angle=3.0)\n",
        "        if view_name == \"rot_neg\":\n",
        "            return T.functional.rotate(batch, angle=-3.0)\n",
        "        raise KeyError(f\"Unknown TTA view: {view_name}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    with torch.inference_mode():\n",
        "        for batch_x, batch_y, batch_meta in tqdm(loader, desc=\"predict\", leave=False):\n",
        "            batch_x = batch_x.to(device, non_blocking=device.startswith(\"cuda\"))\n",
        "            logits_accum = []\n",
        "            if tta_views:\n",
        "                for view_name in tta_views:\n",
        "                    view_x = apply_tta_view(batch_x, view_name)\n",
        "                    view_logits = extract_logits(model(view_x))\n",
        "                    logits_accum.append(view_logits)\n",
        "                logits = torch.stack(logits_accum, dim=0).mean(dim=0)\n",
        "                tta_var = torch.stack([compute_probabilities_from_logits(v) for v in logits_accum], dim=0).var(dim=0).mean(dim=1)\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                logits = extract_logits(model(batch_x))\n",
        "                tta_var = torch.zeros(logits.shape[0], device=logits.device)\n",
        "\n",
        "            logits = logits / float(max(1e-6, temperature))\n",
        "            probs = compute_probabilities_from_logits(logits)\n",
        "            conf, preds = probs.max(dim=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "            for i in range(len(batch_y)):\n",
        "                rec = {\n",
        "                    \"filepath\": batch_meta[\"filepath\"][i] if isinstance(batch_meta[\"filepath\"], list) else batch_meta[\"filepath\"],\n",
        "                    \"source_filepath\": batch_meta[\"source_filepath\"][i] if isinstance(batch_meta[\"source_filepath\"], list) else batch_meta[\"source_filepath\"],\n",
        "                    \"file_sha1\": batch_meta[\"file_sha1\"][i] if isinstance(batch_meta[\"file_sha1\"], list) else batch_meta[\"file_sha1\"],\n",
        "                    \"label_true_idx\": int(batch_y[i].item()),\n",
        "                    \"label_true\": CFG.class_names[int(batch_y[i].item())],\n",
        "                    \"pred_idx\": int(preds[i].item()),\n",
        "                    \"pred_label\": CFG.class_names[int(preds[i].item())],\n",
        "                    \"confidence\": float(conf[i].item()),\n",
        "                    \"tta_variance\": float(tta_var[i].item()),\n",
        "                }\n",
        "                for class_idx, class_name in enumerate(CFG.class_names):\n",
        "                    rec[f\"logit_{class_name}\"] = float(logits[i, class_idx].detach().cpu().item())\n",
        "                    rec[f\"prob_{class_name}\"] = float(probs[i, class_idx].detach().cpu().item())\n",
        "                rec[\"is_correct\"] = rec[\"label_true_idx\"] == rec[\"pred_idx\"]\n",
        "                records.append(rec)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(records)\n",
        "\n",
        "def save_training_history(history_rows: List[Dict[str, Any]], run_dir: Path) -> None:\n",
        "    hist_df = pd.DataFrame(history_rows)\n",
        "    hist_df.to_csv(run_dir / \"history.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "    if hist_df.empty:\n",
        "        return\n",
        "\n",
        "    plt.figure(figsize=(7, 4), dpi=140)\n",
        "    plt.plot(hist_df[\"epoch\"], hist_df[\"train_loss\"], marker=\"o\", label=\"train_loss\")\n",
        "    if \"valid_macro_f1\" in hist_df.columns:\n",
        "        plt.plot(hist_df[\"epoch\"], hist_df[\"valid_macro_f1\"], marker=\"o\", label=\"valid_macro_f1\")\n",
        "    plt.xlabel(\"Epoch\")\n",
        "    plt.ylabel(\"Metric\")\n",
        "    plt.title(\"Training curve\")\n",
        "    plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "    plt.legend()\n",
        "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "    plt.savefig(run_dir / \"training_curve.png\")\n",
        "    plt.close()\n",
        "\n",
        "def bundle_checkpoint_path(run_dir: Path, kind: str = \"best\") -> Path:\n",
        "    return run_dir / \"weights\" / f\"{kind}.pt\"\n",
        "\n",
        "def save_model_bundle(path: Path, model: nn.Module, spec: ExperimentSpec, extra: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> None:\n",
        "    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    bundle = {\n",
        "        \"state_dict\": model.state_dict(),\n",
        "        \"spec\": asdict(spec),\n",
        "        \"class_names\": CFG.class_names,\n",
        "        \"created_at\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n",
        "        \"family\": infer_model_family_for_bundle(spec),\n",
        "        \"extra\": extra or {},\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    torch.save(bundle, path)\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_model_bundle(path: Path) -> Tuple[nn.Module, ExperimentSpec, Dict[str, Any]]:\n",
        "    bundle = torch.load(path, map_location=\"cpu\")\n",
        "    if not isinstance(bundle, dict) or \"state_dict\" not in bundle or \"spec\" not in bundle:\n",
        "        raise ValueError(f\"File does not look like a custom notebook bundle: {path}\")\n",
        "    spec = ExperimentSpec(**bundle[\"spec\"])\n",
        "    model = build_model_from_spec(spec)\n",
        "    model.load_state_dict(bundle[\"state_dict\"], strict=True)\n",
        "    model.eval()\n",
        "    return model, spec, bundle.get(\"extra\", {})\n",
        "\n",
        "def prepare_manifests_for_spec(spec: ExperimentSpec, combine_train_valid: bool = False) -> Tuple[pd.DataFrame, pd.DataFrame, pd.DataFrame]:\n",
        "    if spec.branch_name not in BRANCH_MANIFESTS:\n",
        "        raise KeyError(f\"Branch not materialized: {spec.branch_name}\")\n",
        "    branch_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    if spec.use_offline_aug_cache and not spec.use_online_aug:\n",
        "        train_aug_df = materialize_offline_aug_manifest(\n",
        "            spec.branch_name,\n",
        "            spec.aug_policy,\n",
        "            force=CFG.force_regenerate_aug_cache,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        train_df = train_aug_df[train_aug_df[\"split_canonical\"] == \"train\"].copy()\n",
        "        if combine_train_valid:\n",
        "            valid_aug_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name].copy()\n",
        "            valid_aug_df = valid_aug_df[valid_aug_df[\"split_canonical\"] == \"valid\"].copy()\n",
        "            valid_aug_df[\"aug_policy\"] = spec.aug_policy\n",
        "            valid_aug_df[\"is_augmented\"] = False\n",
        "            valid_aug_df[\"aug_copy_idx\"] = -1\n",
        "            valid_aug_df[\"augmented_filepath\"] = valid_aug_df[\"branch_filepath\"]\n",
        "            train_df = pd.concat([train_df, valid_aug_df], ignore_index=True)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        train_df = branch_df[branch_df[\"split_canonical\"] == \"train\"].copy()\n",
        "        if combine_train_valid:\n",
        "            train_df = branch_df[branch_df[\"split_canonical\"].isin([\"train\", \"valid\"])].copy()\n",
        "        train_df[\"augmented_filepath\"] = train_df[\"branch_filepath\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    valid_df = branch_df[branch_df[\"split_canonical\"] == \"valid\"].copy()\n",
        "    test_df = branch_df[branch_df[\"split_canonical\"] == \"test\"].copy()\n",
        "    return train_df.reset_index(drop=True), valid_df.reset_index(drop=True), test_df.reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_dataloaders_for_spec(spec: ExperimentSpec, combine_train_valid: bool = False) -> Tuple[Any, Any, Any, Optional[torch.Tensor], Optional[torch.utils.data.WeightedRandomSampler]]:\n",
        "    train_df, valid_df, test_df = prepare_manifests_for_spec(spec, combine_train_valid=combine_train_valid)\n",
        "    if spec.use_online_aug:\n",
        "        train_transform = build_online_train_transform(spec.image_size, spec.aug_policy)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        train_transform = build_eval_transform(spec.image_size)\n",
        "    eval_transform = build_eval_transform(spec.image_size)\n",
        "\n",
        "    train_ds = ManifestImageDataset(train_df, image_path_col=\"augmented_filepath\", transform=train_transform)\n",
        "    valid_ds = ManifestImageDataset(valid_df, image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\", transform=eval_transform)\n",
        "    test_ds = ManifestImageDataset(test_df, image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\", transform=eval_transform)\n",
        "\n",
        "    class_weight_tensor = compute_class_weight_tensor(train_df)\n",
        "    weighted_sampler = None\n",
        "    if spec.class_balancing in {\"auto\", \"weighted_sampler\"} and (CFG.weighted_sampler_in_advanced_mode or spec.class_balancing == \"weighted_sampler\"):\n",
        "        weighted_sampler = maybe_build_weighted_sampler(train_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "    train_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(\n",
        "        train_ds,\n",
        "        batch_size=spec.batch_size,\n",
        "        shuffle=(weighted_sampler is None),\n",
        "        sampler=weighted_sampler,\n",
        "        num_workers=CFG.num_workers,\n",
        "        pin_memory=CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    valid_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(\n",
        "        valid_ds,\n",
        "        batch_size=CFG.eval_batch_size,\n",
        "        shuffle=False,\n",
        "        num_workers=CFG.num_workers,\n",
        "        pin_memory=CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    test_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(\n",
        "        test_ds,\n",
        "        batch_size=CFG.eval_batch_size,\n",
        "        shuffle=False,\n",
        "        num_workers=CFG.num_workers,\n",
        "        pin_memory=CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return train_loader, valid_loader, test_loader, class_weight_tensor, weighted_sampler\n",
        "\n",
        "def run_training_experiment(spec: ExperimentSpec) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    run_dir = get_run_dir(spec)\n",
        "    run_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    save_json(run_dir / \"spec.json\", asdict(spec))\n",
        "    status_path = run_dir / \"status.json\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    if status_path.exists():\n",
        "        status = load_json(status_path)\n",
        "        if status.get(\"status\") == \"success\" and (run_dir / \"metrics_summary.json\").exists():\n",
        "            print(f\"Skipping completed run: {spec.run_name}\")\n",
        "            return status\n",
        "\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        seed_everything(spec.seed, deterministic=CFG.deterministic)\n",
        "        model = build_model_from_spec(spec).to(CFG.device)\n",
        "        train_loader, valid_loader, test_loader, class_weight_tensor, weighted_sampler = build_dataloaders_for_spec(spec)\n",
        "\n",
        "        loss_fn = build_loss_function(\n",
        "            spec,\n",
        "            class_weight_tensor.to(CFG.device) if class_weight_tensor is not None and spec.class_balancing in {\"auto\", \"class_weight\"} else None,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "\n",
        "        if spec.freeze_backbone_epochs > 0:\n",
        "            freeze_backbone(model, spec)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            unfreeze_all(model)\n",
        "\n",
        "        optimizer = build_optimizer(model, spec)\n",
        "        scheduler = build_scheduler(optimizer, total_epochs=spec.epochs)\n",
        "        scaler = torch.cuda.amp.GradScaler(enabled=(CFG.use_amp and CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\")))\n",
        "\n",
        "        history_rows: List[Dict[str, Any]] = []\n",
        "        best_metric = -float(\"inf\")\n",
        "        best_epoch = -1\n",
        "        epochs_without_improvement = 0\n",
        "\n",
        "        for epoch in range(1, spec.epochs + 1):\n",
        "            if epoch == spec.freeze_backbone_epochs + 1 and spec.freeze_backbone_epochs > 0:\n",
        "                unfreeze_all(model)\n",
        "                optimizer = build_optimizer(model, spec)\n",
        "                scheduler = build_scheduler(optimizer, total_epochs=max(1, spec.epochs - epoch + 1))\n",
        "\n",
        "            train_stats = train_one_epoch(\n",
        "                model,\n",
        "                train_loader,\n",
        "                optimizer,\n",
        "                loss_fn,\n",
        "                device=CFG.device,\n",
        "                scaler=scaler,\n",
        "                max_grad_norm=CFG.max_grad_norm,\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            valid_pred_df = predict_with_model(model, valid_loader, device=CFG.device)\n",
        "            valid_metric = float(f1_score(valid_pred_df[\"label_true_idx\"], valid_pred_df[\"pred_idx\"], average=\"macro\", zero_division=0))\n",
        "\n",
        "            hist_row = {\n",
        "                \"epoch\": epoch,\n",
        "                **train_stats,\n",
        "                \"valid_macro_f1\": valid_metric,\n",
        "                \"valid_accuracy\": float(accuracy_score(valid_pred_df[\"label_true_idx\"], valid_pred_df[\"pred_idx\"])),\n",
        "            }\n",
        "            history_rows.append(hist_row)\n",
        "\n",
        "            if valid_metric > best_metric:\n",
        "                best_metric = valid_metric\n",
        "                best_epoch = epoch\n",
        "                epochs_without_improvement = 0\n",
        "                save_model_bundle(bundle_checkpoint_path(run_dir, \"best\"), model, spec, extra={\"best_epoch\": epoch})\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                epochs_without_improvement += 1\n",
        "\n",
        "            save_model_bundle(bundle_checkpoint_path(run_dir, \"last\"), model, spec, extra={\"epoch\": epoch})\n",
        "            scheduler.step()\n",
        "\n",
        "            print(f\"Epoch {epoch:03d} | train_loss={train_stats['train_loss']:.4f} | train_acc={train_stats['train_accuracy']:.3f} | valid_macro_f1={valid_metric:.3f}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "            if epochs_without_improvement >= spec.patience:\n",
        "                print(f\"Early stopping at epoch {epoch} with best_epoch={best_epoch} and best_valid_macro_f1={best_metric:.4f}\")\n",
        "                break\n",
        "\n",
        "        save_training_history(history_rows, run_dir)\n",
        "\n",
        "        status = {\n",
        "            \"status\": \"trained\",\n",
        "            \"run_name\": spec.run_name,\n",
        "            \"best_epoch\": best_epoch,\n",
        "            \"best_metric\": best_metric,\n",
        "            \"bundle_best\": str(bundle_checkpoint_path(run_dir, \"best\").resolve()),\n",
        "            \"bundle_last\": str(bundle_checkpoint_path(run_dir, \"last\").resolve()),\n",
        "            \"history_csv\": str((run_dir / \"history.csv\").resolve()),\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        save_json(status_path, status)\n",
        "        return status\n",
        "\n",
        "    except Exception as exc:\n",
        "        err_text = traceback.format_exc()\n",
        "        (run_dir / \"error.txt\").write_text(err_text, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "        status = {\n",
        "            \"status\": \"failed\",\n",
        "            \"run_name\": spec.run_name,\n",
        "            \"error\": str(exc),\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        save_json(status_path, status)\n",
        "        print_rule(f\"RUN FAILED — {spec.run_name}\")\n",
        "        print(err_text)\n",
        "        return status\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "93e2f2a6",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "93e2f2a6"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# PATCH — Preserve old-checkpoint classifier weights when class count already matches\n",
        "\n",
        "def _find_last_linear(module: nn.Module) -> Optional[nn.Linear]:\n",
        "    for submodule in reversed(list(module.modules())):\n",
        "        if isinstance(submodule, nn.Linear):\n",
        "            return submodule\n",
        "    return None\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_ultralytics_model(architecture_or_ckpt: str, num_classes: int, dropout: float) -> nn.Module:\n",
        "    yolo = YOLO(architecture_or_ckpt)\n",
        "    model = yolo.model\n",
        "    last_linear = _find_last_linear(model)\n",
        "    if last_linear is None:\n",
        "        raise RuntimeError(f\"Could not locate a final Linear layer for Ultralytics model: {architecture_or_ckpt}\")\n",
        "    if int(last_linear.out_features) != int(num_classes):\n",
        "        ok = replace_last_linear_in_module(model, num_classes)\n",
        "        if not ok:\n",
        "            raise RuntimeError(f\"Could not replace the classifier head for Ultralytics model: {architecture_or_ckpt}\")\n",
        "    try_wrap_classifier_with_dropout(model, dropout)\n",
        "    if hasattr(model, \"names\"):\n",
        "        model.names = {i: name for i, name in enumerate(CFG.class_names)}\n",
        "    return model\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_model_from_spec(spec: ExperimentSpec) -> nn.Module:\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"old_checkpoint\":\n",
        "        if CFG.old_model_path is None or not Path(CFG.old_model_path).exists():\n",
        "            raise FileNotFoundError(\"Old checkpoint path is not available.\")\n",
        "        return build_ultralytics_model(str(CFG.old_model_path), num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"generic_pretrained\":\n",
        "        return build_torchvision_model(spec.architecture, num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, pretrained=True, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"generic_pretrained_2\":\n",
        "        return build_torchvision_model(spec.architecture, num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, pretrained=True, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"scratch_yolo\":\n",
        "        return build_ultralytics_model(spec.architecture, num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    if spec.family == \"scratch_torchvision\":\n",
        "        return build_torchvision_model(spec.architecture, num_classes=CFG.expected_num_classes, pretrained=False, dropout=spec.dropout)\n",
        "    raise KeyError(f\"Unknown spec.family: {spec.family}\")\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cf251d19",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cf251d19"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# PATCH — avoid double balancing; auto uses class-weighted loss, explicit weighted_sampler uses sampler\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_dataloaders_for_spec(spec: ExperimentSpec, combine_train_valid: bool = False) -> Tuple[Any, Any, Any, Optional[torch.Tensor], Optional[torch.utils.data.WeightedRandomSampler]]:\n",
        "    train_df, valid_df, test_df = prepare_manifests_for_spec(spec, combine_train_valid=combine_train_valid)\n",
        "    if spec.use_online_aug:\n",
        "        train_transform = build_online_train_transform(spec.image_size, spec.aug_policy)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        train_transform = build_eval_transform(spec.image_size)\n",
        "    eval_transform = build_eval_transform(spec.image_size)\n",
        "\n",
        "    train_ds = ManifestImageDataset(train_df, image_path_col=\"augmented_filepath\", transform=train_transform)\n",
        "    valid_ds = ManifestImageDataset(valid_df, image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\", transform=eval_transform)\n",
        "    test_ds = ManifestImageDataset(test_df, image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\", transform=eval_transform)\n",
        "\n",
        "    class_weight_tensor = compute_class_weight_tensor(train_df)\n",
        "    weighted_sampler = None\n",
        "    if spec.class_balancing == \"weighted_sampler\":\n",
        "        weighted_sampler = maybe_build_weighted_sampler(train_df)\n",
        "        class_weight_tensor = None\n",
        "    elif spec.class_balancing == \"none\":\n",
        "        class_weight_tensor = None\n",
        "\n",
        "    train_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(\n",
        "        train_ds,\n",
        "        batch_size=spec.batch_size,\n",
        "        shuffle=(weighted_sampler is None),\n",
        "        sampler=weighted_sampler,\n",
        "        num_workers=CFG.num_workers,\n",
        "        pin_memory=CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    valid_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(\n",
        "        valid_ds,\n",
        "        batch_size=CFG.eval_batch_size,\n",
        "        shuffle=False,\n",
        "        num_workers=CFG.num_workers,\n",
        "        pin_memory=CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    test_loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(\n",
        "        test_ds,\n",
        "        batch_size=CFG.eval_batch_size,\n",
        "        shuffle=False,\n",
        "        num_workers=CFG.num_workers,\n",
        "        pin_memory=CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return train_loader, valid_loader, test_loader, class_weight_tensor, weighted_sampler\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "93b1fb1b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "93b1fb1b"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# PATCH — torchvision pretrained download fallback\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_torchvision_model(architecture: str, num_classes: int, pretrained: bool, dropout: float) -> nn.Module:\n",
        "    arch = architecture.lower()\n",
        "    def _safe_construct(builder, weights_obj):\n",
        "        if pretrained:\n",
        "            try:\n",
        "                return builder(weights=weights_obj)\n",
        "            except Exception as exc:\n",
        "                print(f\"WARNING: pretrained weights unavailable for {architecture}, falling back to random init. Reason: {exc}\")\n",
        "                return builder(weights=None)\n",
        "        return builder(weights=None)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if arch == \"resnet18\":\n",
        "        model = _safe_construct(torchvision.models.resnet18, torchvision.models.ResNet18_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1)\n",
        "        model.fc = nn.Linear(model.fc.in_features, num_classes)\n",
        "    elif arch == \"efficientnet_b0\":\n",
        "        model = _safe_construct(torchvision.models.efficientnet_b0, torchvision.models.EfficientNet_B0_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1)\n",
        "        in_features = model.classifier[-1].in_features\n",
        "        model.classifier[-1] = nn.Linear(in_features, num_classes)\n",
        "    elif arch == \"mobilenet_v3_small\":\n",
        "        model = _safe_construct(torchvision.models.mobilenet_v3_small, torchvision.models.MobileNet_V3_Small_Weights.IMAGENET1K_V1)\n",
        "        in_features = model.classifier[-1].in_features\n",
        "        model.classifier[-1] = nn.Linear(in_features, num_classes)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        raise KeyError(f\"Unsupported torchvision architecture: {architecture}\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    try_wrap_classifier_with_dropout(model, dropout)\n",
        "    return model\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "e69376e9",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "e69376e9"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section K, L, M — Testing and Evaluating Our Models\n",
        "\n",
        "How do we know if a model is actually good? We track a bunch of metrics:\n",
        "- **Accuracy**: How many did it get right?\n",
        "- **Macro F1**: A balanced score that makes sure we are doing well on *both* males and females, even if one is more common.\n",
        "- **Confusion Matrices**: A visual grid showing what the model got confused by.\n",
        "- **Calibration**: If the model says it's 90% sure, is it actually right 90% of the time?\n",
        "\n",
        "We also create **Challenge Suites**—we take the test images and purposefully make them dark, blurry, or noisy to see if the model falls apart."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "d72d7f45",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d72d7f45"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION K + L + M — Metrics, calibration, threshold sweeps, challenge suites, and evaluation\n",
        "\n",
        "def expected_calibration_error(y_true: np.ndarray, probs: np.ndarray, n_bins: int = 15) -> float:\n",
        "    confidences = probs.max(axis=1)\n",
        "    predictions = probs.argmax(axis=1)\n",
        "    correctness = (predictions == y_true).astype(float)\n",
        "    bins = np.linspace(0.0, 1.0, n_bins + 1)\n",
        "    ece = 0.0\n",
        "    for i in range(n_bins):\n",
        "        lo, hi = bins[i], bins[i + 1]\n",
        "        mask = (confidences >= lo) & (confidences < hi if i < n_bins - 1 else confidences <= hi)\n",
        "        if mask.sum() == 0:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        bin_acc = correctness[mask].mean()\n",
        "        bin_conf = confidences[mask].mean()\n",
        "        ece += (mask.mean()) * abs(bin_acc - bin_conf)\n",
        "    return float(ece)\n",
        "\n",
        "def safe_binary_metrics(y_true: np.ndarray, probs_pos: np.ndarray) -> Dict[str, float]:\n",
        "    out = {\"roc_auc\": float(\"nan\"), \"pr_auc\": float(\"nan\"), \"brier_score\": float(\"nan\"), \"log_loss\": float(\"nan\")}\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        if len(np.unique(y_true)) == 2:\n",
        "            out[\"roc_auc\"] = float(roc_auc_score(y_true, probs_pos))\n",
        "            out[\"pr_auc\"] = float(average_precision_score(y_true, probs_pos))\n",
        "            out[\"brier_score\"] = float(np.mean((probs_pos - y_true) ** 2))\n",
        "            out[\"log_loss\"] = float(log_loss(y_true, np.clip(probs_pos, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)))\n",
        "    except Exception:\n",
        "        pass\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_prediction_metrics(pred_df: pd.DataFrame) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    y_true = pred_df[\"label_true_idx\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "    y_pred = pred_df[\"pred_idx\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "    probs = pred_df[[f\"prob_{name}\" for name in CFG.class_names]].to_numpy()\n",
        "    precision, recall, f1_vals, support = precision_recall_fscore_support(\n",
        "        y_true,\n",
        "        y_pred,\n",
        "        labels=list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes)),\n",
        "        zero_division=0,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    per_class = {\n",
        "        CFG.class_names[i]: {\n",
        "            \"precision\": float(precision[i]),\n",
        "            \"recall\": float(recall[i]),\n",
        "            \"f1\": float(f1_vals[i]),\n",
        "            \"support\": int(support[i]),\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        for i in range(CFG.expected_num_classes)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    extra_binary = safe_binary_metrics(y_true, probs[:, 1]) if CFG.expected_num_classes == 2 else {}\n",
        "    metrics = {\n",
        "        \"accuracy\": float(accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred)),\n",
        "        \"balanced_accuracy\": float(balanced_accuracy_score(y_true, y_pred)) if len(np.unique(y_true)) > 1 else float(\"nan\"),\n",
        "        \"macro_f1\": float(f1_score(y_true, y_pred, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0)),\n",
        "        \"worst_class_recall\": float(np.min(recall)) if len(recall) else float(\"nan\"),\n",
        "        \"ece\": expected_calibration_error(y_true, probs, n_bins=CFG.ece_bins),\n",
        "        \"confusion_matrix_raw\": confusion_matrix(y_true, y_pred, labels=list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes))).tolist(),\n",
        "        \"confusion_matrix_normalized\": confusion_matrix(y_true, y_pred, labels=list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes)), normalize=\"true\").tolist(),\n",
        "        \"classification_report\": classification_report(\n",
        "            y_true,\n",
        "            y_pred,\n",
        "            labels=list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes)),\n",
        "            target_names=CFG.class_names,\n",
        "            output_dict=True,\n",
        "            zero_division=0,\n",
        "        ),\n",
        "        \"per_class\": per_class,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    metrics.update(extra_binary)\n",
        "    return metrics\n",
        "\n",
        "def compute_threshold_sweep(pred_df: pd.DataFrame, thresholds: Sequence[float]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    y_true = pred_df[\"label_true_idx\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "    y_pred = pred_df[\"pred_idx\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "    confidence = pred_df[\"confidence\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "    probs = pred_df[[f\"prob_{name}\" for name in CFG.class_names]].to_numpy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    for thr in thresholds:\n",
        "        keep = confidence >= thr\n",
        "        abstain_count = int((~keep).sum())\n",
        "        coverage = float(keep.mean()) if len(keep) else 0.0\n",
        "        overall_acc = float((((y_pred == y_true) & keep).sum()) / max(1, len(y_true)))\n",
        "\n",
        "        if keep.sum() > 0:\n",
        "            yt = y_true[keep]\n",
        "            yp = y_pred[keep]\n",
        "            conf_probs = probs[keep]\n",
        "            macro_f1 = float(f1_score(yt, yp, average=\"macro\", zero_division=0))\n",
        "            bal_acc = float(balanced_accuracy_score(yt, yp)) if len(np.unique(yt)) > 1 else float(\"nan\")\n",
        "            worst_recall = float(np.min(precision_recall_fscore_support(yt, yp, labels=list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes)), zero_division=0)[1]))\n",
        "            confident_acc = float(accuracy_score(yt, yp))\n",
        "            confident_ece = expected_calibration_error(yt, conf_probs, n_bins=CFG.ece_bins)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            macro_f1 = float(\"nan\")\n",
        "            bal_acc = float(\"nan\")\n",
        "            worst_recall = float(\"nan\")\n",
        "            confident_acc = float(\"nan\")\n",
        "            confident_ece = float(\"nan\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        rows.append({\n",
        "            \"threshold\": float(thr),\n",
        "            \"coverage\": coverage,\n",
        "            \"abstained_images\": abstain_count,\n",
        "            \"overall_accuracy_including_abstentions_as_wrong\": overall_acc,\n",
        "            \"confident_accuracy\": confident_acc,\n",
        "            \"confident_macro_f1\": macro_f1,\n",
        "            \"confident_balanced_accuracy\": bal_acc,\n",
        "            \"confident_worst_class_recall\": worst_recall,\n",
        "            \"confident_ece\": confident_ece,\n",
        "        })\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "\n",
        "def choose_recommended_threshold(sweep_df: pd.DataFrame, min_coverage: float = 0.80) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    work = sweep_df.copy()\n",
        "    eligible = work[work[\"coverage\"] >= min_coverage].copy()\n",
        "    if eligible.empty:\n",
        "        eligible = work.copy()\n",
        "    best_macro = eligible.sort_values(\n",
        "        by=[\"confident_macro_f1\", \"confident_balanced_accuracy\", \"coverage\"],\n",
        "        ascending=[False, False, False],\n",
        "        na_position=\"last\",\n",
        "    ).iloc[0].to_dict()\n",
        "    best_overall = work.sort_values(\n",
        "        by=[\"overall_accuracy_including_abstentions_as_wrong\", \"coverage\"],\n",
        "        ascending=[False, False],\n",
        "        na_position=\"last\",\n",
        "    ).iloc[0].to_dict()\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"best_threshold_by_macro_f1\": best_macro,\n",
        "        \"best_threshold_by_overall_accuracy\": best_overall,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "def plot_confusion(cm: np.ndarray, out_path: Path, title: str, normalized: bool = False) -> None:\n",
        "    plt.figure(figsize=(5.2, 4.5), dpi=140)\n",
        "    sns.heatmap(\n",
        "        cm,\n",
        "        annot=True,\n",
        "        fmt=\".2f\" if normalized else \"d\",\n",
        "        cmap=\"Blues\",\n",
        "        xticklabels=CFG.class_names,\n",
        "        yticklabels=CFG.class_names,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    plt.xlabel(\"Predicted\")\n",
        "    plt.ylabel(\"True\")\n",
        "    plt.title(title)\n",
        "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "    plt.savefig(out_path)\n",
        "    plt.close()\n",
        "\n",
        "def plot_reliability(pred_df: pd.DataFrame, out_path: Path, title: str) -> None:\n",
        "    y_true = pred_df[\"label_true_idx\"].to_numpy()\n",
        "    probs = pred_df[[f\"prob_{name}\" for name in CFG.class_names]].to_numpy()\n",
        "    confidences = probs.max(axis=1)\n",
        "    predictions = probs.argmax(axis=1)\n",
        "    correctness = (predictions == y_true).astype(int)\n",
        "    frac_pos, mean_pred = calibration_curve(correctness, confidences, n_bins=CFG.ece_bins, strategy=\"uniform\")\n",
        "    plt.figure(figsize=(5.0, 4.5), dpi=140)\n",
        "    plt.plot([0, 1], [0, 1], \"--\", color=\"gray\", linewidth=1)\n",
        "    plt.plot(mean_pred, frac_pos, marker=\"o\")\n",
        "    plt.xlabel(\"Mean predicted confidence\")\n",
        "    plt.ylabel(\"Empirical accuracy\")\n",
        "    plt.title(title)\n",
        "    plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "    plt.savefig(out_path)\n",
        "    plt.close()\n",
        "\n",
        "def plot_threshold_sweep(sweep_df: pd.DataFrame, out_dir: Path, split_name: str) -> None:\n",
        "    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    for y_col, title, fname in [\n",
        "        (\"coverage\", \"Coverage vs threshold\", \"coverage_vs_threshold.png\"),\n",
        "        (\"overall_accuracy_including_abstentions_as_wrong\", \"Overall accuracy vs threshold\", \"overall_accuracy_vs_threshold.png\"),\n",
        "        (\"confident_macro_f1\", \"Confident macro F1 vs threshold\", \"macro_f1_vs_threshold.png\"),\n",
        "        (\"confident_accuracy\", \"Confident accuracy vs threshold\", \"confident_accuracy_vs_threshold.png\"),\n",
        "    ]:\n",
        "        plt.figure(figsize=(6.5, 4.0), dpi=140)\n",
        "        plt.plot(sweep_df[\"threshold\"], sweep_df[y_col], marker=\"o\")\n",
        "        plt.xlabel(\"Confidence threshold\")\n",
        "        plt.ylabel(y_col)\n",
        "        plt.title(f\"{split_name} — {title}\")\n",
        "        plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "        plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "        plt.savefig(out_dir / fname)\n",
        "        plt.close()\n",
        "\n",
        "def plot_misclassification_gallery(pred_df: pd.DataFrame, out_path: Path, title: str, max_items: int = 24) -> None:\n",
        "    mis_df = pred_df[~pred_df[\"is_correct\"]].copy().sort_values(\"confidence\", ascending=False).head(max_items)\n",
        "    if mis_df.empty:\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    cols = 4\n",
        "    rows = math.ceil(len(mis_df) / cols)\n",
        "    fig, axes = plt.subplots(rows, cols, figsize=(4 * cols, 3.2 * rows), dpi=140)\n",
        "    axes = np.array(axes).reshape(-1)\n",
        "    for ax in axes:\n",
        "        ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "    for ax, row in zip(axes, mis_df.itertuples(index=False)):\n",
        "        img = Image.open(row.filepath).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "        ax.imshow(img)\n",
        "        ax.set_title(f\"true={row.label_true} | pred={row.pred_label}\\nconf={row.confidence:.3f}\", fontsize=9)\n",
        "        ax.axis(\"off\")\n",
        "    plt.suptitle(title)\n",
        "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "    plt.savefig(out_path)\n",
        "    plt.close()\n",
        "\n",
        "def summarize_prediction_artifacts(pred_df: pd.DataFrame, out_dir: Path, split_name: str, prefix: str = \"\") -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    pred_path = out_dir / f\"{prefix}predictions.csv\"\n",
        "    pred_df.to_csv(pred_path, index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "    metrics = compute_prediction_metrics(pred_df)\n",
        "    sweep_df = compute_threshold_sweep(pred_df, CFG.confidence_thresholds)\n",
        "    sweep_path = out_dir / f\"{prefix}threshold_sweep.csv\"\n",
        "    sweep_df.to_csv(sweep_path, index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "    chosen_thresholds = choose_recommended_threshold(sweep_df, min_coverage=CFG.threshold_min_coverage)\n",
        "\n",
        "    plot_confusion(np.asarray(metrics[\"confusion_matrix_raw\"]), out_dir / f\"{prefix}confusion_raw.png\", f\"{split_name} confusion (raw)\", normalized=False)\n",
        "    plot_confusion(np.asarray(metrics[\"confusion_matrix_normalized\"]), out_dir / f\"{prefix}confusion_normalized.png\", f\"{split_name} confusion (normalized)\", normalized=True)\n",
        "    plot_reliability(pred_df, out_dir / f\"{prefix}reliability.png\", f\"{split_name} reliability\")\n",
        "    plot_threshold_sweep(sweep_df, out_dir, split_name=f\"{split_name}{prefix}\")\n",
        "    if CFG.show_misclassified_examples:\n",
        "        plot_misclassification_gallery(pred_df, out_dir / f\"{prefix}misclassified_gallery.png\", title=f\"{split_name} misclassified gallery\", max_items=CFG.num_misclassified_to_show)\n",
        "\n",
        "    high_conf_wrong = pred_df[(~pred_df[\"is_correct\"]) & (pred_df[\"confidence\"] >= 0.80)].copy()\n",
        "    low_conf_correct = pred_df[(pred_df[\"is_correct\"]) & (pred_df[\"confidence\"] < 0.55)].copy()\n",
        "    high_conf_wrong.to_csv(out_dir / f\"{prefix}high_confidence_errors.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "    low_conf_correct.to_csv(out_dir / f\"{prefix}low_confidence_correct.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "    summary = {\n",
        "        \"split_name\": split_name,\n",
        "        \"n_images\": int(len(pred_df)),\n",
        "        \"metrics\": metrics,\n",
        "        \"recommended_thresholds\": chosen_thresholds,\n",
        "        \"n_errors\": int((~pred_df[\"is_correct\"]).sum()),\n",
        "        \"n_high_confidence_errors\": int(len(high_conf_wrong)),\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    save_json(out_dir / f\"{prefix}summary.json\", summary)\n",
        "    return summary\n",
        "\n",
        "def fit_temperature_from_logits(pred_df: pd.DataFrame) -> float:\n",
        "    logits = pred_df[[f\"logit_{name}\" for name in CFG.class_names]].to_numpy(dtype=np.float64)\n",
        "    y_true = pred_df[\"label_true_idx\"].to_numpy(dtype=np.int64)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def objective(log_t: np.ndarray) -> float:\n",
        "        temp = float(np.exp(log_t[0]))\n",
        "        scaled = logits / temp\n",
        "        probs = softmax(scaled, axis=1)\n",
        "        return float(log_loss(y_true, probs, labels=list(range(CFG.expected_num_classes))))\n",
        "\n",
        "    result = minimize(objective, x0=np.array([0.0], dtype=np.float64), method=\"L-BFGS-B\", bounds=[(-3.0, 3.0)])\n",
        "    if not result.success:\n",
        "        return 1.0\n",
        "    return float(np.exp(result.x[0]))\n",
        "\n",
        "CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS: Dict[str, Any] = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "def _noise_image(img: Image.Image, std: float) -> Image.Image:\n",
        "    arr = np.asarray(img.convert(\"RGB\")).astype(np.float32) / 255.0\n",
        "    arr = np.clip(arr + np.random.normal(0.0, std, arr.shape), 0.0, 1.0)\n",
        "    return Image.fromarray((arr * 255.0).astype(np.uint8))\n",
        "\n",
        "def _jpeg_recompress(img: Image.Image, quality: int) -> Image.Image:\n",
        "    import io\n",
        "    buf = io.BytesIO()\n",
        "    img.save(buf, format=\"JPEG\", quality=quality)\n",
        "    buf.seek(0)\n",
        "    return Image.open(buf).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "\n",
        "def register_challenge_transforms():\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"brightness_down\"] = lambda img: ImageEnhance.Brightness(img).enhance(0.78)\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"brightness_up\"] = lambda img: ImageEnhance.Brightness(img).enhance(1.18)\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"contrast_low\"] = lambda img: ImageEnhance.Contrast(img).enhance(0.72)\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"gaussian_blur\"] = lambda img: img.filter(ImageFilter.GaussianBlur(radius=1.2))\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"gaussian_noise\"] = lambda img: _noise_image(img, std=0.03)\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"desaturate\"] = lambda img: ImageEnhance.Color(img).enhance(0.25)\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"jpeg_compression\"] = lambda img: _jpeg_recompress(img, quality=28)\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"crop_shift\"] = lambda img: T.functional.affine(\n",
        "        img, angle=0.0, translate=(int(0.03 * img.size[0]), int(0.03 * img.size[1])), scale=1.0, shear=[0.0, 0.0], fill=robust_background_color(img)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"sharpness_down\"] = lambda img: ImageEnhance.Sharpness(img).enhance(0.45)\n",
        "    CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[\"grayscale_mix\"] = lambda img: ImageOps.grayscale(img).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "\n",
        "register_challenge_transforms()\n",
        "\n",
        "def materialize_challenge_manifest(branch_name: str, split_name: str, suite_name: str, force: bool = False) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    if suite_name not in CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS:\n",
        "        raise KeyError(f\"Unknown challenge suite: {suite_name}\")\n",
        "    branch_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[branch_name].copy()\n",
        "    subset = branch_df[branch_df[\"split_canonical\"] == split_name].copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "    suite_root = CFG.paths.challenge_root / split_name / suite_name / branch_name\n",
        "    manifest_path = suite_root / \"manifest.csv\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    if manifest_path.exists() and not force:\n",
        "        return pd.read_csv(manifest_path)\n",
        "\n",
        "    suite_root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    transform = CHALLENGE_TRANSFORMS[suite_name]\n",
        "\n",
        "    for row in tqdm(subset.itertuples(index=False), total=len(subset), desc=f\"Challenge {split_name}/{suite_name}/{branch_name}\"):\n",
        "        src_path = Path(row.branch_filepath)\n",
        "        dst_dir = suite_root / row.label\n",
        "        dst_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "        dst_path = dst_dir / f\"{Path(row.branch_filepath).stem}__{suite_name}.png\"\n",
        "\n",
        "        if not dst_path.exists() or force:\n",
        "            img = Image.open(src_path).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "            random.seed(deterministic_seed_for_path(row.file_sha1, suite_name, 0, CFG.random_seed))\n",
        "            np.random.seed(deterministic_seed_for_path(row.file_sha1, suite_name, 1, CFG.random_seed))\n",
        "            out = transform(img)\n",
        "            out.save(dst_path, format=\"PNG\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        rec = dict(row._asdict())\n",
        "        rec[\"challenge_suite\"] = suite_name\n",
        "        rec[\"challenge_filepath\"] = str(dst_path.resolve())\n",
        "        rows.append(rec)\n",
        "\n",
        "    challenge_df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "    challenge_df.to_csv(manifest_path, index=False)\n",
        "    return challenge_df\n",
        "\n",
        "def evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "    bundle_path: Path,\n",
        "    df: pd.DataFrame,\n",
        "    image_path_col: str,\n",
        "    image_size: int,\n",
        "    out_dir: Path,\n",
        "    split_name: str,\n",
        "    use_temperature: Optional[float] = None,\n",
        "    tta_views: Optional[Tuple[str, ...]] = None,\n",
        "    prefix: str = \"\",\n",
        ") -> Tuple[pd.DataFrame, Dict[str, Any]]:\n",
        "    model, spec, extra = load_model_bundle(bundle_path)\n",
        "    model = model.to(CFG.device)\n",
        "    transform = build_eval_transform(image_size)\n",
        "    ds = ManifestImageDataset(df, image_path_col=image_path_col, transform=transform)\n",
        "    loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(\n",
        "        ds,\n",
        "        batch_size=CFG.eval_batch_size,\n",
        "        shuffle=False,\n",
        "        num_workers=CFG.num_workers,\n",
        "        pin_memory=CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    pred_df = predict_with_model(model, loader, device=CFG.device, temperature=(use_temperature or 1.0), tta_views=tta_views)\n",
        "    summary = summarize_prediction_artifacts(pred_df, out_dir=out_dir, split_name=split_name, prefix=prefix)\n",
        "    del model\n",
        "    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
        "        torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n",
        "    return pred_df, summary\n",
        "\n",
        "def evaluate_native_old_checkpoint_on_manifest(df: pd.DataFrame, image_path_col: str, out_dir: Path, split_name: str) -> Tuple[pd.DataFrame, Dict[str, Any]]:\n",
        "    model = YOLO(str(CFG.old_model_path))\n",
        "    transform = build_eval_transform(CFG.image_size)\n",
        "    ds = ManifestImageDataset(df, image_path_col=image_path_col, transform=transform)\n",
        "    loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(\n",
        "        ds,\n",
        "        batch_size=CFG.eval_batch_size,\n",
        "        shuffle=False,\n",
        "        num_workers=CFG.num_workers,\n",
        "        pin_memory=CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    net = model.model.to(CFG.device)\n",
        "    net.eval()\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    with torch.inference_mode():\n",
        "        for batch_x, batch_y, batch_meta in tqdm(loader, desc=f\"baseline {split_name}\", leave=False):\n",
        "            batch_x = batch_x.to(CFG.device)\n",
        "            logits = extract_logits(net(batch_x))\n",
        "            probs = compute_probabilities_from_logits(logits)\n",
        "            conf, preds = probs.max(dim=1)\n",
        "            for i in range(len(batch_y)):\n",
        "                rec = {\n",
        "                    \"filepath\": batch_meta[\"filepath\"][i] if isinstance(batch_meta[\"filepath\"], list) else batch_meta[\"filepath\"],\n",
        "                    \"source_filepath\": batch_meta[\"source_filepath\"][i] if isinstance(batch_meta[\"source_filepath\"], list) else batch_meta[\"source_filepath\"],\n",
        "                    \"file_sha1\": batch_meta[\"file_sha1\"][i] if isinstance(batch_meta[\"file_sha1\"], list) else batch_meta[\"file_sha1\"],\n",
        "                    \"label_true_idx\": int(batch_y[i].item()),\n",
        "                    \"label_true\": CFG.class_names[int(batch_y[i].item())],\n",
        "                    \"pred_idx\": int(preds[i].item()),\n",
        "                    \"pred_label\": CFG.class_names[int(preds[i].item())],\n",
        "                    \"confidence\": float(conf[i].item()),\n",
        "                    \"tta_variance\": 0.0,\n",
        "                }\n",
        "                for class_idx, class_name in enumerate(CFG.class_names):\n",
        "                    rec[f\"logit_{class_name}\"] = float(logits[i, class_idx].detach().cpu().item())\n",
        "                    rec[f\"prob_{class_name}\"] = float(probs[i, class_idx].detach().cpu().item())\n",
        "                rec[\"is_correct\"] = rec[\"label_true_idx\"] == rec[\"pred_idx\"]\n",
        "                rows.append(rec)\n",
        "    pred_df = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "    summary = summarize_prediction_artifacts(pred_df, out_dir=out_dir, split_name=split_name)\n",
        "    return pred_df, summary\n",
        "\n",
        "def summarize_challenge_results(pristine_summary: Dict[str, Any], suite_summaries: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    base_macro = pristine_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"]\n",
        "    base_bal = pristine_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"]\n",
        "    base_worst = pristine_summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"]\n",
        "    for suite_name, summary in suite_summaries.items():\n",
        "        rows.append({\n",
        "            \"challenge_suite\": suite_name,\n",
        "            \"macro_f1\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "            \"balanced_accuracy\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "            \"worst_class_recall\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "            \"macro_f1_delta_vs_pristine\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"] - base_macro,\n",
        "            \"balanced_accuracy_delta_vs_pristine\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"] - base_bal,\n",
        "            \"worst_class_recall_delta_vs_pristine\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"] - base_worst,\n",
        "        })\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "\n",
        "def evaluate_challenge_suites_for_bundle(\n",
        "    bundle_path: Path,\n",
        "    branch_name: str,\n",
        "    split_name: str,\n",
        "    suite_names: Sequence[str],\n",
        "    out_dir: Path,\n",
        "    image_size: int,\n",
        "    temperature: Optional[float] = None,\n",
        "    tta_views: Optional[Tuple[str, ...]] = None,\n",
        ") -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    suite_summaries: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]] = {}\n",
        "    for suite_name in suite_names:\n",
        "        challenge_df = materialize_challenge_manifest(\n",
        "            branch_name=branch_name,\n",
        "            split_name=split_name,\n",
        "            suite_name=suite_name,\n",
        "            force=CFG.force_regenerate_challenge_copies,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        _, summary = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "            bundle_path=bundle_path,\n",
        "            df=challenge_df,\n",
        "            image_path_col=\"challenge_filepath\",\n",
        "            image_size=image_size,\n",
        "            out_dir=out_dir / suite_name,\n",
        "            split_name=f\"{split_name}_{suite_name}\",\n",
        "            use_temperature=temperature,\n",
        "            tta_views=tta_views,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        suite_summaries[suite_name] = summary\n",
        "    if not suite_summaries:\n",
        "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "    pristine_summary = {\"metrics\": {\"macro_f1\": float(\"nan\"), \"balanced_accuracy\": float(\"nan\"), \"worst_class_recall\": float(\"nan\")}}\n",
        "    summary_df = pd.DataFrame([\n",
        "        {\n",
        "            \"challenge_suite\": suite_name,\n",
        "            \"macro_f1\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "            \"balanced_accuracy\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "            \"worst_class_recall\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        for suite_name, summary in suite_summaries.items()\n",
        "    ])\n",
        "    summary_df.to_csv(out_dir / \"challenge_suite_metrics.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "    return summary_df\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "1f96928b",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1f96928b"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section N (Part 1) — Testing the Original Model\n",
        "\n",
        "Before we train any new AI, we need to test the *existing* model on our new data. This gives us our baseline score. If our newly trained models can't beat this score, we know we did something wrong!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "c573d500",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c573d500"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION N (part 1) — Evaluate the old checkpoint before any retraining\n",
        "\n",
        "if CFG.old_model_path is None:\n",
        "    raise FileNotFoundError(\n",
        "        \"No old checkpoint was discovered. Place newone.pt in the working directory, /content, or /mnt/data, \"\n",
        "        \"or set CFG.old_model_path explicitly in the config cell.\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "RAW_BRANCH_DF = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[\"RAW\"].copy()\n",
        "RAW_VALID_DF = RAW_BRANCH_DF[RAW_BRANCH_DF[\"split_canonical\"] == \"valid\"].copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "RAW_TEST_DF = RAW_BRANCH_DF[RAW_BRANCH_DF[\"split_canonical\"] == \"test\"].copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "with timed_block(\"Old checkpoint baseline on pristine validation\"):\n",
        "    baseline_valid_pred_df, baseline_valid_summary = evaluate_native_old_checkpoint_on_manifest(\n",
        "        RAW_VALID_DF,\n",
        "        image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\",\n",
        "        out_dir=CFG.paths.baseline_root / \"valid_pristine\",\n",
        "        split_name=\"valid_pristine\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "with timed_block(\"Old checkpoint baseline on pristine sacred holdout\"):\n",
        "    baseline_test_pred_df, baseline_test_summary = evaluate_native_old_checkpoint_on_manifest(\n",
        "        RAW_TEST_DF,\n",
        "        image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\",\n",
        "        out_dir=CFG.paths.baseline_root / \"test_pristine\",\n",
        "        split_name=\"test_pristine\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "baseline_temperature = fit_temperature_from_logits(baseline_valid_pred_df) if CFG.run_temperature_scaling else 1.0\n",
        "save_json(CFG.paths.baseline_root / \"temperature_scaling.json\", {\"temperature\": baseline_temperature})\n",
        "\n",
        "old_baseline_record = {\n",
        "    \"run_name\": \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\",\n",
        "    \"status\": \"success\",\n",
        "    \"family\": \"old_checkpoint\",\n",
        "    \"architecture\": str(CFG.old_model_path.name),\n",
        "    \"init_mode\": \"eval_only\",\n",
        "    \"branch_name\": \"RAW\",\n",
        "    \"aug_policy\": \"none\",\n",
        "    \"image_size\": CFG.image_size,\n",
        "    \"batch_size\": CFG.batch_size,\n",
        "    \"epochs\": 0,\n",
        "    \"patience\": 0,\n",
        "    \"lr\": None,\n",
        "    \"weight_decay\": None,\n",
        "    \"dropout\": 0.0,\n",
        "    \"label_smoothing\": 0.0,\n",
        "    \"freeze_backbone_epochs\": 0,\n",
        "    \"seed\": CFG.random_seed,\n",
        "    \"notes\": \"Direct portability baseline of the provided checkpoint on the new setup.\",\n",
        "    \"valid_summary_path\": str((CFG.paths.baseline_root / \"valid_pristine\" / \"summary.json\").resolve()),\n",
        "    \"test_summary_path\": str((CFG.paths.baseline_root / \"test_pristine\" / \"summary.json\").resolve()),\n",
        "    \"valid_macro_f1\": baseline_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "    \"valid_balanced_accuracy\": baseline_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "    \"valid_worst_class_recall\": baseline_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "    \"valid_ece\": baseline_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "    \"test_macro_f1\": baseline_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "    \"test_balanced_accuracy\": baseline_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "    \"test_worst_class_recall\": baseline_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "    \"test_ece\": baseline_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "    \"recommended_threshold\": baseline_valid_summary[\"recommended_thresholds\"][\"best_threshold_by_macro_f1\"][\"threshold\"],\n",
        "    \"temperature\": baseline_temperature,\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "save_json(CFG.paths.baseline_root / \"baseline_record.json\", old_baseline_record)\n",
        "\n",
        "print_rule(\"OLD CHECKPOINT BASELINE\")\n",
        "print(json.dumps({\n",
        "    \"old_model_path\": str(CFG.old_model_path),\n",
        "    \"valid_macro_f1\": baseline_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "    \"valid_balanced_accuracy\": baseline_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "    \"test_macro_f1\": baseline_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "    \"test_balanced_accuracy\": baseline_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "    \"baseline_temperature\": baseline_temperature,\n",
        "}, indent=2))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "df54fc7e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "df54fc7e"
      },
      "source": [
        "## SECTION I (part 2) — Experiment grid construction\n",
        "\n",
        "The core benchmark grid covers:\n",
        "\n",
        "### Baseline\n",
        "- old checkpoint eval only\n",
        "\n",
        "### Old checkpoint family\n",
        "- no augmentation\n",
        "- light augmentation\n",
        "- medium augmentation\n",
        "- medium + low LR\n",
        "- medium + freeze/unfreeze warmup\n",
        "- medium + alternate image size\n",
        "- medium + dropout\n",
        "- medium + label smoothing / stronger weight decay\n",
        "\n",
        "### Generic pretrained family\n",
        "- no augmentation\n",
        "- light augmentation\n",
        "- medium augmentation\n",
        "- medium + low LR\n",
        "- medium + freeze/unfreeze warmup\n",
        "- medium + alternate image size\n",
        "- medium + dropout\n",
        "- medium + label smoothing / stronger weight decay\n",
        "\n",
        "### Scratch family\n",
        "- no augmentation\n",
        "- light augmentation\n",
        "- medium augmentation\n",
        "- medium + longer schedule\n",
        "- medium + alternate image size\n",
        "- medium + stronger regularization\n",
        "\n",
        "In FULL / MOONSHOT mode the notebook can also add:\n",
        "- a second backbone family\n",
        "- multi-seed follow-up\n",
        "- branch comparisons for top recipes\n",
        "- TTA and ensembling\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "de1ff72e",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "de1ff72e"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION I (part 2) — Build experiment specs and run the core benchmark\n",
        "\n",
        "def make_spec(\n",
        "    run_name: str,\n",
        "    family: str,\n",
        "    architecture: str,\n",
        "    init_mode: str,\n",
        "    branch_name: str = \"RAW\",\n",
        "    aug_policy: str = \"none\",\n",
        "    image_size: Optional[int] = None,\n",
        "    batch_size: Optional[int] = None,\n",
        "    epochs: Optional[int] = None,\n",
        "    patience: Optional[int] = None,\n",
        "    lr: Optional[float] = None,\n",
        "    weight_decay: Optional[float] = None,\n",
        "    dropout: float = 0.0,\n",
        "    label_smoothing: float = 0.0,\n",
        "    freeze_backbone_epochs: int = 0,\n",
        "    stronger_regularization: bool = False,\n",
        "    class_balancing: str = \"auto\",\n",
        "    loss_name: str = \"ce\",\n",
        "    focal_gamma: float = 1.5,\n",
        "    notes: str = \"\",\n",
        "    seed: Optional[int] = None,\n",
        "    use_offline_aug_cache: bool = True,\n",
        "    use_online_aug: bool = False,\n",
        "    final_retrain: bool = False,\n",
        ") -> ExperimentSpec:\n",
        "    return ExperimentSpec(\n",
        "        run_name=run_name,\n",
        "        family=family,\n",
        "        architecture=architecture,\n",
        "        init_mode=init_mode,\n",
        "        branch_name=branch_name,\n",
        "        aug_policy=aug_policy,\n",
        "        image_size=int(image_size or CFG.image_size),\n",
        "        batch_size=int(batch_size or CFG.batch_size),\n",
        "        epochs=int(epochs or CFG.epochs),\n",
        "        patience=int(patience or CFG.patience),\n",
        "        lr=float(lr or CFG.lr),\n",
        "        weight_decay=float(weight_decay or CFG.weight_decay),\n",
        "        optimizer_name=CFG.optimizer_name,\n",
        "        dropout=float(dropout),\n",
        "        label_smoothing=float(label_smoothing),\n",
        "        freeze_backbone_epochs=int(freeze_backbone_epochs),\n",
        "        stronger_regularization=bool(stronger_regularization),\n",
        "        class_balancing=class_balancing,\n",
        "        loss_name=loss_name,\n",
        "        focal_gamma=float(focal_gamma),\n",
        "        notes=notes,\n",
        "        seed=int(seed or CFG.random_seed),\n",
        "        use_offline_aug_cache=bool(use_offline_aug_cache),\n",
        "        use_online_aug=bool(use_online_aug),\n",
        "        final_retrain=bool(final_retrain),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_core_experiment_specs() -> List[ExperimentSpec]:\n",
        "    specs: List[ExperimentSpec] = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Old checkpoint family.\n",
        "    specs.extend([\n",
        "        make_spec(\"b_old_none\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"none\", notes=\"Old checkpoint + no augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"c_old_light\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"light\", notes=\"Old checkpoint + light augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"d_old_medium\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"medium\", notes=\"Old checkpoint + medium augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"e_old_medium_low_lr\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"medium\", lr=CFG.low_lr, notes=\"Old checkpoint + medium augmentation + lower LR.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"f_old_medium_freeze_unfreeze\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"medium\", freeze_backbone_epochs=CFG.warmup_freeze_epochs, notes=\"Old checkpoint + medium augmentation + freeze/unfreeze warmup.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"g_old_medium_alt_img\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"medium\", image_size=CFG.alt_image_size, notes=\"Old checkpoint + medium augmentation + alternate image size.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"h_old_medium_dropout\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"medium\", dropout=CFG.stronger_dropout, notes=\"Old checkpoint + medium augmentation + dropout.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"i_old_medium_label_smooth_wd\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"medium\", label_smoothing=CFG.stronger_label_smoothing, weight_decay=CFG.strong_weight_decay, notes=\"Old checkpoint + medium augmentation + label smoothing and stronger weight decay.\"),\n",
        "    ])\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Generic pretrained family.\n",
        "    specs.extend([\n",
        "        make_spec(\"j_pretrained_none\", family=\"generic_pretrained\", architecture=\"resnet18\", init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"none\", notes=\"Generic pretrained ResNet18 + no augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"k_pretrained_light\", family=\"generic_pretrained\", architecture=\"resnet18\", init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"light\", notes=\"Generic pretrained ResNet18 + light augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"l_pretrained_medium\", family=\"generic_pretrained\", architecture=\"resnet18\", init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"medium\", notes=\"Generic pretrained ResNet18 + medium augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"m_pretrained_medium_low_lr\", family=\"generic_pretrained\", architecture=\"resnet18\", init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"medium\", lr=CFG.low_lr, notes=\"Generic pretrained ResNet18 + medium augmentation + lower LR.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"n_pretrained_medium_freeze_unfreeze\", family=\"generic_pretrained\", architecture=\"resnet18\", init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"medium\", freeze_backbone_epochs=CFG.warmup_freeze_epochs, notes=\"Generic pretrained ResNet18 + medium augmentation + freeze/unfreeze warmup.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"o_pretrained_medium_alt_img\", family=\"generic_pretrained\", architecture=\"resnet18\", init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"medium\", image_size=CFG.alt_image_size, notes=\"Generic pretrained ResNet18 + medium augmentation + alternate image size.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"p_pretrained_medium_dropout\", family=\"generic_pretrained\", architecture=\"resnet18\", init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"medium\", dropout=CFG.stronger_dropout, notes=\"Generic pretrained ResNet18 + medium augmentation + dropout.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"q_pretrained_medium_label_smooth_wd\", family=\"generic_pretrained\", architecture=\"resnet18\", init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"medium\", label_smoothing=CFG.stronger_label_smoothing, weight_decay=CFG.strong_weight_decay, notes=\"Generic pretrained ResNet18 + medium augmentation + label smoothing and stronger weight decay.\"),\n",
        "    ])\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Scratch family.\n",
        "    specs.extend([\n",
        "        make_spec(\"r_scratch_none\", family=\"scratch_yolo\", architecture=\"yolo26n-cls.yaml\", init_mode=\"scratch\", aug_policy=\"none\", epochs=CFG.scratch_epochs, notes=\"Scratch YOLO26n-cls + no augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"s_scratch_light\", family=\"scratch_yolo\", architecture=\"yolo26n-cls.yaml\", init_mode=\"scratch\", aug_policy=\"light\", epochs=CFG.scratch_epochs, notes=\"Scratch YOLO26n-cls + light augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"t_scratch_medium\", family=\"scratch_yolo\", architecture=\"yolo26n-cls.yaml\", init_mode=\"scratch\", aug_policy=\"medium\", epochs=CFG.scratch_epochs, notes=\"Scratch YOLO26n-cls + medium augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"u_scratch_medium_longer\", family=\"scratch_yolo\", architecture=\"yolo26n-cls.yaml\", init_mode=\"scratch\", aug_policy=\"medium\", epochs=max(CFG.scratch_epochs, CFG.epochs + 15), patience=CFG.patience + 3, notes=\"Scratch YOLO26n-cls + medium augmentation + longer schedule.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"v_scratch_medium_alt_img\", family=\"scratch_yolo\", architecture=\"yolo26n-cls.yaml\", init_mode=\"scratch\", aug_policy=\"medium\", image_size=CFG.alt_image_size, epochs=CFG.scratch_epochs, notes=\"Scratch YOLO26n-cls + medium augmentation + alternate image size.\"),\n",
        "        make_spec(\"w_scratch_medium_stronger_reg\", family=\"scratch_yolo\", architecture=\"yolo26n-cls.yaml\", init_mode=\"scratch\", aug_policy=\"medium\", weight_decay=CFG.strong_weight_decay, dropout=CFG.stronger_dropout, epochs=CFG.scratch_epochs, notes=\"Scratch YOLO26n-cls + medium augmentation + stronger regularization.\"),\n",
        "    ])\n",
        "\n",
        "    if CFG.run_second_backbone_family:\n",
        "        specs.extend([\n",
        "            make_spec(\"x2_effnet_medium\", family=\"generic_pretrained_2\", architecture=CFG.second_backbone_name, init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"medium\", notes=\"Second backbone family: EfficientNet-B0 pretrained + medium augmentation.\"),\n",
        "            make_spec(\"x3_effnet_medium_alt_img\", family=\"generic_pretrained_2\", architecture=CFG.second_backbone_name, init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"medium\", image_size=CFG.alt_image_size, notes=\"Second backbone family: EfficientNet-B0 pretrained + medium augmentation + alternate image size.\"),\n",
        "            make_spec(\"x4_mobile_scratch_medium\", family=\"scratch_torchvision\", architecture=CFG.second_backbone_scratch_name, init_mode=\"scratch\", aug_policy=\"medium\", epochs=CFG.scratch_epochs, notes=\"Second scratch family: MobileNet-V3-small scratch + medium augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "    if CFG.execution_mode in {\"FULL\", \"MOONSHOT\"}:\n",
        "        specs.extend([\n",
        "            make_spec(\"x5_old_medium_weighted_sampler\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"medium\", class_balancing=\"weighted_sampler\", notes=\"Advanced: old checkpoint + medium augmentation + weighted sampler.\"),\n",
        "            make_spec(\"x6_pretrained_medium_focal\", family=\"generic_pretrained\", architecture=\"resnet18\", init_mode=\"imagenet\", aug_policy=\"medium\", loss_name=\"focal\", focal_gamma=CFG.focal_gamma, notes=\"Advanced: generic pretrained ResNet18 + medium augmentation + focal loss.\"),\n",
        "            make_spec(\"x7_old_background_robust_aug\", family=\"old_checkpoint\", architecture=\"old_checkpoint\", init_mode=\"finetune\", aug_policy=\"background_robustness\", notes=\"Advanced: old checkpoint + background-robustness augmentation.\"),\n",
        "        ])\n",
        "\n",
        "    if CFG.execution_mode == \"FAST\":\n",
        "        keep = {\"b_old_none\", \"c_old_light\", \"d_old_medium\", \"l_pretrained_medium\", \"t_scratch_medium\"}\n",
        "        specs = [spec for spec in specs if spec.run_name in keep]\n",
        "\n",
        "    return specs\n",
        "\n",
        "CORE_SPECS = build_core_experiment_specs()\n",
        "save_json(CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"planned_core_specs.json\", [asdict(spec) for spec in CORE_SPECS])\n",
        "\n",
        "print_rule(\"PLANNED CORE EXPERIMENTS\")\n",
        "display(pd.DataFrame([asdict(spec) for spec in CORE_SPECS])[[\n",
        "    \"run_name\", \"family\", \"architecture\", \"branch_name\", \"aug_policy\", \"image_size\", \"epochs\", \"lr\",\n",
        "    \"weight_decay\", \"dropout\", \"label_smoothing\", \"freeze_backbone_epochs\", \"notes\"\n",
        "]])\n",
        "\n",
        "RUN_REGISTRY: List[Dict[str, Any]] = [old_baseline_record.copy()]\n",
        "\n",
        "with timed_block(\"Core benchmark training loop\"):\n",
        "    for spec in CORE_SPECS:\n",
        "        status = run_training_experiment(spec)\n",
        "        run_record = {**asdict(spec), **status}\n",
        "        RUN_REGISTRY.append(run_record)\n",
        "\n",
        "run_registry_path = CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"run_registry_after_training.json\"\n",
        "save_json(run_registry_path, RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "print(\"Saved run registry to:\", run_registry_path.resolve())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "fc152280",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fc152280"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Section K (Part 2) — Final Tests on Pristine Data\n",
        "\n",
        "Once all of our experimental models have finished training, we test the successful ones on the pristine Validation and Test sets. We also check their calibration (how confident they are in their answers)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "c3d851dc",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c3d851dc"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION K (part 2) — Evaluate all successful trained runs on pristine validation and pristine holdout\n",
        "\n",
        "def attach_pristine_evaluation_to_run(run_record: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    if run_record.get(\"status\") not in {\"trained\", \"success\"}:\n",
        "        return run_record\n",
        "\n",
        "    # Baseline already evaluated earlier.\n",
        "    if run_record.get(\"run_name\") == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\":\n",
        "        run_record[\"status\"] = \"success\"\n",
        "        run_record[\"selection_source\"] = \"baseline\"\n",
        "        return run_record\n",
        "\n",
        "    run_dir = get_run_dir(ExperimentSpec(**{\n",
        "        k: run_record[k]\n",
        "        for k in ExperimentSpec.__dataclass_fields__.keys()\n",
        "        if k in run_record\n",
        "    }))\n",
        "    bundle_best = Path(run_record[\"bundle_best\"])\n",
        "    spec = ExperimentSpec(**{\n",
        "        k: run_record[k]\n",
        "        for k in ExperimentSpec.__dataclass_fields__.keys()\n",
        "        if k in run_record\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "    pristine_valid_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name][BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name][\"split_canonical\"] == \"valid\"].copy()\n",
        "    pristine_test_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name][BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name][\"split_canonical\"] == \"test\"].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    valid_pred_df, valid_summary = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "        bundle_best,\n",
        "        df=pristine_valid_df,\n",
        "        image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\",\n",
        "        image_size=spec.image_size,\n",
        "        out_dir=run_dir / \"eval\" / \"valid_pristine\",\n",
        "        split_name=\"valid_pristine\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    temperature = fit_temperature_from_logits(valid_pred_df) if CFG.run_temperature_scaling else 1.0\n",
        "    save_json(run_dir / \"eval\" / \"temperature_scaling.json\", {\"temperature\": temperature})\n",
        "\n",
        "    _, valid_cal_summary = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "        bundle_best,\n",
        "        df=pristine_valid_df,\n",
        "        image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\",\n",
        "        image_size=spec.image_size,\n",
        "        out_dir=run_dir / \"eval\" / \"valid_pristine_calibrated\",\n",
        "        split_name=\"valid_pristine_calibrated\",\n",
        "        use_temperature=temperature,\n",
        "        prefix=\"cal_\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    _, test_summary = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "        bundle_best,\n",
        "        df=pristine_test_df,\n",
        "        image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\",\n",
        "        image_size=spec.image_size,\n",
        "        out_dir=run_dir / \"eval\" / \"test_pristine\",\n",
        "        split_name=\"test_pristine\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    _, test_cal_summary = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "        bundle_best,\n",
        "        df=pristine_test_df,\n",
        "        image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\",\n",
        "        image_size=spec.image_size,\n",
        "        out_dir=run_dir / \"eval\" / \"test_pristine_calibrated\",\n",
        "        split_name=\"test_pristine_calibrated\",\n",
        "        use_temperature=temperature,\n",
        "        prefix=\"cal_\",\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    metrics_summary = {\n",
        "        \"run_name\": run_record[\"run_name\"],\n",
        "        \"branch_name\": spec.branch_name,\n",
        "        \"valid_pristine\": valid_summary,\n",
        "        \"valid_pristine_calibrated\": valid_cal_summary,\n",
        "        \"test_pristine\": test_summary,\n",
        "        \"test_pristine_calibrated\": test_cal_summary,\n",
        "        \"temperature\": temperature,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "    save_json(run_dir / \"metrics_summary.json\", metrics_summary)\n",
        "\n",
        "    run_record.update({\n",
        "        \"status\": \"success\",\n",
        "        \"selection_source\": \"trained_bundle\",\n",
        "        \"temperature\": temperature,\n",
        "        \"valid_summary_path\": str((run_dir / \"eval\" / \"valid_pristine\" / \"summary.json\").resolve()),\n",
        "        \"test_summary_path\": str((run_dir / \"eval\" / \"test_pristine\" / \"summary.json\").resolve()),\n",
        "        \"valid_macro_f1\": valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "        \"valid_balanced_accuracy\": valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "        \"valid_worst_class_recall\": valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "        \"valid_ece\": valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "        \"valid_brier_score\": valid_summary[\"metrics\"].get(\"brier_score\", float(\"nan\")),\n",
        "        \"valid_roc_auc\": valid_summary[\"metrics\"].get(\"roc_auc\", float(\"nan\")),\n",
        "        \"valid_pr_auc\": valid_summary[\"metrics\"].get(\"pr_auc\", float(\"nan\")),\n",
        "        \"test_macro_f1\": test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "        \"test_balanced_accuracy\": test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "        \"test_worst_class_recall\": test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "        \"test_ece\": test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "        \"test_brier_score\": test_summary[\"metrics\"].get(\"brier_score\", float(\"nan\")),\n",
        "        \"test_roc_auc\": test_summary[\"metrics\"].get(\"roc_auc\", float(\"nan\")),\n",
        "        \"test_pr_auc\": test_summary[\"metrics\"].get(\"pr_auc\", float(\"nan\")),\n",
        "        \"recommended_threshold\": valid_summary[\"recommended_thresholds\"][\"best_threshold_by_macro_f1\"][\"threshold\"],\n",
        "        \"valid_calibrated_ece\": valid_cal_summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "        \"test_calibrated_ece\": test_cal_summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "        \"valid_calibrated_macro_f1\": valid_cal_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "        \"test_calibrated_macro_f1\": test_cal_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "    })\n",
        "    return run_record\n",
        "\n",
        "with timed_block(\"Pristine evaluation for successful runs\"):\n",
        "    updated_registry = []\n",
        "    for record in RUN_REGISTRY:\n",
        "        updated_registry.append(attach_pristine_evaluation_to_run(record))\n",
        "    RUN_REGISTRY = updated_registry\n",
        "\n",
        "save_json(CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"run_registry_after_pristine_eval.json\", RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "\n",
        "pristine_leaderboard_df = pd.DataFrame(RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "print_rule(\"PRISTINE LEADERBOARD SNAPSHOT\")\n",
        "cols = [c for c in [\n",
        "    \"run_name\", \"status\", \"family\", \"architecture\", \"branch_name\", \"aug_policy\", \"image_size\",\n",
        "    \"valid_macro_f1\", \"valid_balanced_accuracy\", \"valid_worst_class_recall\", \"valid_ece\",\n",
        "    \"test_macro_f1\", \"test_balanced_accuracy\", \"test_worst_class_recall\", \"test_ece\",\n",
        "] if c in pristine_leaderboard_df.columns]\n",
        "display(pristine_leaderboard_df[cols].sort_values([\"valid_macro_f1\", \"valid_balanced_accuracy\"], ascending=[False, False], na_position=\"last\"))\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "b3a41a51",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "b3a41a51"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Advanced Follow-Up Tests\n",
        "\n",
        "For the models that performed the best, we put them through the wringer:\n",
        "\n",
        "- We test them on the different image branches (like the Tight Crop).\n",
        "- We run them through the Challenge Suites (blurry, dark images).\n",
        "- We use \"Test Time Augmentation\" (TTA)—which means having the model look at the same image slightly rotated a few times and taking a vote.\n",
        "- If turned on, we might even try combining the top models together into an \"Ensemble\" to see if they are smarter as a team."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "d5257429",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d5257429"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# ADVANCED FOLLOW-UP — Branch comparisons, challenge suites, TTA, ensemble, and multi-seed\n",
        "\n",
        "def leaderboard_df_from_registry(registry: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    df = pd.DataFrame(registry).copy()\n",
        "    if df.empty:\n",
        "        return df\n",
        "    for col in [\"valid_macro_f1\", \"valid_balanced_accuracy\", \"valid_worst_class_recall\", \"valid_ece\"]:\n",
        "        if col not in df.columns:\n",
        "            df[col] = np.nan\n",
        "    return df\n",
        "\n",
        "def top_successful_runs(df: pd.DataFrame, k: int, exclude_baseline: bool = True) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    work = df[df[\"status\"] == \"success\"].copy()\n",
        "    if exclude_baseline and \"run_name\" in work.columns:\n",
        "        work = work[work[\"run_name\"] != \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\"]\n",
        "    if work.empty:\n",
        "        return work\n",
        "    return work.sort_values(\n",
        "        by=[\"valid_macro_f1\", \"valid_balanced_accuracy\", \"valid_worst_class_recall\", \"valid_ece\"],\n",
        "        ascending=[False, False, False, True],\n",
        "        na_position=\"last\",\n",
        "    ).head(k).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "def record_to_spec(record: Dict[str, Any]) -> ExperimentSpec:\n",
        "    return ExperimentSpec(**{\n",
        "        key: record[key]\n",
        "        for key in ExperimentSpec.__dataclass_fields__.keys()\n",
        "        if key in record\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "leaderboard_df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "top_core_for_branches = top_successful_runs(leaderboard_df, k=CFG.branch_comparison_top_k, exclude_baseline=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "BRANCH_COMPARISON_SPECS: List[ExperimentSpec] = []\n",
        "for _, row in top_core_for_branches.iterrows():\n",
        "    base_spec = record_to_spec(row.to_dict())\n",
        "    for branch_name in CFG.branch_names_enabled:\n",
        "        if branch_name == \"RAW\":\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        clone = make_spec(\n",
        "            run_name=f\"{base_spec.run_name}__{branch_name.lower()}\",\n",
        "            family=base_spec.family,\n",
        "            architecture=base_spec.architecture,\n",
        "            init_mode=base_spec.init_mode,\n",
        "            branch_name=branch_name,\n",
        "            aug_policy=base_spec.aug_policy,\n",
        "            image_size=base_spec.image_size,\n",
        "            batch_size=base_spec.batch_size,\n",
        "            epochs=base_spec.epochs,\n",
        "            patience=base_spec.patience,\n",
        "            lr=base_spec.lr,\n",
        "            weight_decay=base_spec.weight_decay,\n",
        "            dropout=base_spec.dropout,\n",
        "            label_smoothing=base_spec.label_smoothing,\n",
        "            freeze_backbone_epochs=base_spec.freeze_backbone_epochs,\n",
        "            stronger_regularization=base_spec.stronger_regularization,\n",
        "            class_balancing=base_spec.class_balancing,\n",
        "            loss_name=base_spec.loss_name,\n",
        "            focal_gamma=base_spec.focal_gamma,\n",
        "            notes=f\"Branch comparison clone of {base_spec.run_name} on {branch_name}.\",\n",
        "            seed=base_spec.seed,\n",
        "            use_offline_aug_cache=base_spec.use_offline_aug_cache,\n",
        "            use_online_aug=base_spec.use_online_aug,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        BRANCH_COMPARISON_SPECS.append(clone)\n",
        "\n",
        "save_json(CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"planned_branch_specs.json\", [asdict(spec) for spec in BRANCH_COMPARISON_SPECS])\n",
        "\n",
        "if BRANCH_COMPARISON_SPECS:\n",
        "    print_rule(\"RUNNING DATASET-BRANCH COMPARISON\")\n",
        "    for spec in BRANCH_COMPARISON_SPECS:\n",
        "        status = run_training_experiment(spec)\n",
        "        record = {**asdict(spec), **status}\n",
        "        RUN_REGISTRY.append(record)\n",
        "    RUN_REGISTRY = [attach_pristine_evaluation_to_run(rec) for rec in RUN_REGISTRY]\n",
        "    save_json(CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"run_registry_after_branch_comparison.json\", RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "\n",
        "leaderboard_df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "top_for_challenge = top_successful_runs(leaderboard_df, k=CFG.valid_challenge_top_k, exclude_baseline=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "def evaluate_validation_challenges_for_record(record: Dict[str, Any]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    if record.get(\"run_name\") == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\":\n",
        "        bundle_path = None\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        bundle_path = Path(record[\"bundle_best\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "    branch_name = record.get(\"branch_name\", \"RAW\")\n",
        "    image_size = int(record.get(\"image_size\", CFG.image_size))\n",
        "    run_dir = CFG.paths.baseline_root if record.get(\"run_name\") == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\" else get_run_dir(record_to_spec(record))\n",
        "    out_dir = run_dir / \"challenge_eval\" / \"valid\"\n",
        "    suite_summaries = []\n",
        "    for suite_name in CFG.challenge_suite_names:\n",
        "        challenge_df = materialize_challenge_manifest(branch_name=branch_name, split_name=\"valid\", suite_name=suite_name, force=CFG.force_regenerate_challenge_copies)\n",
        "        if record.get(\"run_name\") == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\":\n",
        "            pred_df, summary = evaluate_native_old_checkpoint_on_manifest(\n",
        "                challenge_df,\n",
        "                image_path_col=\"challenge_filepath\",\n",
        "                out_dir=out_dir / suite_name,\n",
        "                split_name=f\"valid_{suite_name}\",\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            _, summary = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "                bundle_path,\n",
        "                df=challenge_df,\n",
        "                image_path_col=\"challenge_filepath\",\n",
        "                image_size=image_size,\n",
        "                out_dir=out_dir / suite_name,\n",
        "                split_name=f\"valid_{suite_name}\",\n",
        "                use_temperature=float(record.get(\"temperature\", 1.0)),\n",
        "            )\n",
        "        suite_summaries.append({\n",
        "            \"challenge_suite\": suite_name,\n",
        "            \"macro_f1\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "            \"balanced_accuracy\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "            \"worst_class_recall\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "            \"ece\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "        })\n",
        "    suite_df = pd.DataFrame(suite_summaries)\n",
        "    suite_df.to_csv(out_dir / \"challenge_valid_summary.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "    record[\"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\"] = float(suite_df[\"macro_f1\"].mean()) if not suite_df.empty else np.nan\n",
        "    record[\"valid_challenge_worst_macro_f1\"] = float(suite_df[\"macro_f1\"].min()) if not suite_df.empty else np.nan\n",
        "    record[\"valid_challenge_mean_balanced_accuracy\"] = float(suite_df[\"balanced_accuracy\"].mean()) if not suite_df.empty else np.nan\n",
        "    record[\"valid_challenge_summary_path\"] = str((out_dir / \"challenge_valid_summary.csv\").resolve())\n",
        "    return record\n",
        "\n",
        "if not top_for_challenge.empty:\n",
        "    print_rule(\"RUNNING VALIDATION CHALLENGE-SUITE EVALUATION\")\n",
        "    selected_names = set(top_for_challenge[\"run_name\"].tolist())\n",
        "    RUN_REGISTRY = [\n",
        "        evaluate_validation_challenges_for_record(rec) if rec.get(\"run_name\") in selected_names else rec\n",
        "        for rec in RUN_REGISTRY\n",
        "    ]\n",
        "    save_json(CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"run_registry_after_valid_challenges.json\", RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "\n",
        "leaderboard_df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "\n",
        "def add_tta_for_top_runs(registry: List[Dict[str, Any]], top_k: int) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n",
        "    if not CFG.run_tta:\n",
        "        return registry\n",
        "    df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(registry)\n",
        "    top_df = top_successful_runs(df, k=top_k, exclude_baseline=False)\n",
        "    selected = set(top_df[\"run_name\"].tolist())\n",
        "    out = []\n",
        "    for rec in registry:\n",
        "        if rec.get(\"run_name\") not in selected or rec.get(\"run_name\") == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\":\n",
        "            out.append(rec)\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        spec = record_to_spec(rec)\n",
        "        bundle_path = Path(rec[\"bundle_best\"])\n",
        "        run_dir = get_run_dir(spec)\n",
        "        valid_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name][BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name][\"split_canonical\"] == \"valid\"].copy()\n",
        "        _, tta_summary = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "            bundle_path,\n",
        "            df=valid_df,\n",
        "            image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\",\n",
        "            image_size=spec.image_size,\n",
        "            out_dir=run_dir / \"tta_eval\" / \"valid\",\n",
        "            split_name=\"valid_pristine_tta\",\n",
        "            use_temperature=float(rec.get(\"temperature\", 1.0)),\n",
        "            tta_views=CFG.tta_views,\n",
        "            prefix=\"tta_\",\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        rec[\"valid_tta_macro_f1\"] = tta_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"]\n",
        "        rec[\"valid_tta_balanced_accuracy\"] = tta_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"]\n",
        "        out.append(rec)\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "\n",
        "RUN_REGISTRY = add_tta_for_top_runs(RUN_REGISTRY, top_k=CFG.tta_top_k)\n",
        "\n",
        "def choose_diverse_ensemble_members(df: pd.DataFrame, k: int) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    work = top_successful_runs(df, k=max(k * 3, k), exclude_baseline=True)\n",
        "    chosen = []\n",
        "    seen_pairs = set()\n",
        "    for _, row in work.iterrows():\n",
        "        pair = (row[\"family\"], row[\"branch_name\"])\n",
        "        if pair in seen_pairs:\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        chosen.append(row)\n",
        "        seen_pairs.add(pair)\n",
        "        if len(chosen) >= k:\n",
        "            break\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(chosen)\n",
        "\n",
        "ENSEMBLE_RECORD = None\n",
        "if CFG.run_ensemble:\n",
        "    leaderboard_df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "    ensemble_members_df = choose_diverse_ensemble_members(leaderboard_df, k=CFG.ensemble_top_k)\n",
        "    if len(ensemble_members_df) >= 2:\n",
        "        print_rule(\"RUNNING OPTIONAL SOFT-VOTE ENSEMBLE\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        def ensemble_predict(split_name: str, out_dir: Path) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "            member_prob_tables = []\n",
        "            base_meta = None\n",
        "            for _, member in ensemble_members_df.iterrows():\n",
        "                member_branch = member[\"branch_name\"]\n",
        "                df_eval = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[member_branch][BRANCH_MANIFESTS[member_branch][\"split_canonical\"] == split_name].copy().reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "                bundle_path = Path(member[\"bundle_best\"])\n",
        "                pred_df, _ = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "                    bundle_path,\n",
        "                    df=df_eval,\n",
        "                    image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\",\n",
        "                    image_size=int(member[\"image_size\"]),\n",
        "                    out_dir=out_dir / normalize_token(member[\"run_name\"]),\n",
        "                    split_name=f\"{split_name}_{member['run_name']}\",\n",
        "                    use_temperature=float(member.get(\"temperature\", 1.0)),\n",
        "                    prefix=\"ens_member_\",\n",
        "                )\n",
        "                pred_df = pred_df.sort_values(\"file_sha1\").reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "                member_prob_tables.append(pred_df[[f\"prob_{name}\" for name in CFG.class_names]].to_numpy())\n",
        "                if base_meta is None:\n",
        "                    base_meta = pred_df.copy()\n",
        "                else:\n",
        "                    base_meta = base_meta.sort_values(\"file_sha1\").reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "            mean_probs = np.mean(np.stack(member_prob_tables, axis=0), axis=0)\n",
        "            base_meta = base_meta.copy()\n",
        "            for idx, class_name in enumerate(CFG.class_names):\n",
        "                base_meta[f\"prob_{class_name}\"] = mean_probs[:, idx]\n",
        "                base_meta[f\"logit_{class_name}\"] = np.log(np.clip(mean_probs[:, idx], 1e-6, 1.0))\n",
        "            base_meta[\"pred_idx\"] = mean_probs.argmax(axis=1)\n",
        "            base_meta[\"pred_label\"] = base_meta[\"pred_idx\"].map({i: name for i, name in enumerate(CFG.class_names)})\n",
        "            base_meta[\"confidence\"] = mean_probs.max(axis=1)\n",
        "            base_meta[\"is_correct\"] = base_meta[\"pred_idx\"] == base_meta[\"label_true_idx\"]\n",
        "            summary = summarize_prediction_artifacts(base_meta, out_dir=out_dir, split_name=f\"{split_name}_ensemble\", prefix=\"ensemble_\")\n",
        "            return summary\n",
        "\n",
        "        ens_valid_summary = ensemble_predict(\"valid\", CFG.paths.analysis_root / \"ensemble\" / \"valid\")\n",
        "        ens_test_summary = ensemble_predict(\"test\", CFG.paths.analysis_root / \"ensemble\" / \"test\")\n",
        "        ENSEMBLE_RECORD = {\n",
        "            \"run_name\": \"z_soft_vote_ensemble\",\n",
        "            \"status\": \"success\",\n",
        "            \"family\": \"ensemble\",\n",
        "            \"architecture\": \"+\".join(ensemble_members_df[\"architecture\"].astype(str).tolist()),\n",
        "            \"branch_name\": \"mixed_member_branches\",\n",
        "            \"aug_policy\": \"mixed\",\n",
        "            \"image_size\": int(ensemble_members_df.iloc[0][\"image_size\"]),\n",
        "            \"valid_macro_f1\": ens_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "            \"valid_balanced_accuracy\": ens_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "            \"valid_worst_class_recall\": ens_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "            \"valid_ece\": ens_valid_summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "            \"test_macro_f1\": ens_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "            \"test_balanced_accuracy\": ens_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "            \"test_worst_class_recall\": ens_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "            \"test_ece\": ens_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "            \"notes\": \"Soft-vote ensemble over diverse top-performing members, each evaluated on its own branch preprocessing.\",\n",
        "        }\n",
        "        RUN_REGISTRY.append(ENSEMBLE_RECORD)\n",
        "\n",
        "def run_multi_seed_followup(registry: List[Dict[str, Any]]) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n",
        "    if not CFG.run_multi_seed_followup:\n",
        "        return registry\n",
        "    df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(registry)\n",
        "    top_df = top_successful_runs(df, k=CFG.multi_seed_top_k, exclude_baseline=True)\n",
        "    follow_specs: List[ExperimentSpec] = []\n",
        "    for _, row in top_df.iterrows():\n",
        "        base_spec = record_to_spec(row.to_dict())\n",
        "        for seed in CFG.extra_seeds:\n",
        "            clone = make_spec(\n",
        "                run_name=f\"{base_spec.run_name}__seed{seed}\",\n",
        "                family=base_spec.family,\n",
        "                architecture=base_spec.architecture,\n",
        "                init_mode=base_spec.init_mode,\n",
        "                branch_name=base_spec.branch_name,\n",
        "                aug_policy=base_spec.aug_policy,\n",
        "                image_size=base_spec.image_size,\n",
        "                batch_size=base_spec.batch_size,\n",
        "                epochs=base_spec.epochs,\n",
        "                patience=base_spec.patience,\n",
        "                lr=base_spec.lr,\n",
        "                weight_decay=base_spec.weight_decay,\n",
        "                dropout=base_spec.dropout,\n",
        "                label_smoothing=base_spec.label_smoothing,\n",
        "                freeze_backbone_epochs=base_spec.freeze_backbone_epochs,\n",
        "                stronger_regularization=base_spec.stronger_regularization,\n",
        "                class_balancing=base_spec.class_balancing,\n",
        "                loss_name=base_spec.loss_name,\n",
        "                focal_gamma=base_spec.focal_gamma,\n",
        "                notes=f\"Multi-seed follow-up clone of {base_spec.run_name}.\",\n",
        "                seed=seed,\n",
        "                use_offline_aug_cache=base_spec.use_offline_aug_cache,\n",
        "                use_online_aug=base_spec.use_online_aug,\n",
        "            )\n",
        "            follow_specs.append(clone)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if not follow_specs:\n",
        "        return registry\n",
        "\n",
        "    print_rule(\"RUNNING MULTI-SEED FOLLOW-UP\")\n",
        "    for spec in follow_specs:\n",
        "        status = run_training_experiment(spec)\n",
        "        registry.append({**asdict(spec), **status})\n",
        "    registry = [attach_pristine_evaluation_to_run(rec) for rec in registry]\n",
        "    return registry\n",
        "\n",
        "RUN_REGISTRY = run_multi_seed_followup(RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "save_json(CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"run_registry_after_advanced_followup.json\", RUN_REGISTRY)\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "1bbcd494",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "1bbcd494"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Looking Under the Hood (Interpretability)\n",
        "\n",
        "We don't just want a score; we want to know *why* the model made its choices.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Grad-CAM**: This creates a \"heatmap\" over the image showing exactly where the AI was looking when it guessed male or female.\n",
        "- **Embeddings**: We graph how the AI groups the images in its \"brain\" to see if it's accidentally grouping them by camera angle instead of sex.\n",
        "- **Label Review**: We find the images where the AI was 99% confident but got it \"wrong\"—sometimes this helps us realize that *we* labeled the image incorrectly in the first place!"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cc112f02",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cc112f02"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION N (part 2) — Error analysis, embeddings, nearest neighbors, and Grad-CAM\n",
        "\n",
        "def get_top_analysis_runs(registry: List[Dict[str, Any]], k: int = 2) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(registry)\n",
        "    return top_successful_runs(df, k=k, exclude_baseline=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "def prediction_disagreement_table(registry: List[Dict[str, Any]], split_name: str = \"valid\", top_k: int = 3) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(registry)\n",
        "    top_df = top_successful_runs(df, k=top_k, exclude_baseline=False)\n",
        "    if top_df.empty:\n",
        "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "\n",
        "    pred_tables = []\n",
        "    for _, row in top_df.iterrows():\n",
        "        run_name = row[\"run_name\"]\n",
        "        if run_name == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\":\n",
        "            pred_path = CFG.paths.baseline_root / f\"{split_name}_pristine\" / \"predictions.csv\"\n",
        "        elif run_name == \"z_soft_vote_ensemble\":\n",
        "            pred_path = CFG.paths.analysis_root / \"ensemble\" / split_name / \"ensemble_predictions.csv\"\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            pred_path = get_run_dir(record_to_spec(row.to_dict())) / \"eval\" / f\"{split_name}_pristine\" / \"predictions.csv\"\n",
        "        if not pred_path.exists():\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        pred_df = pd.read_csv(pred_path)[[\"file_sha1\", \"pred_idx\", \"confidence\", \"label_true\"]].copy()\n",
        "        pred_df = pred_df.rename(columns={\n",
        "            \"pred_idx\": f\"pred_idx__{run_name}\",\n",
        "            \"confidence\": f\"confidence__{run_name}\",\n",
        "        })\n",
        "        pred_tables.append(pred_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "    if not pred_tables:\n",
        "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "\n",
        "    merged = pred_tables[0]\n",
        "    for tab in pred_tables[1:]:\n",
        "        merged = merged.merge(tab, on=[\"file_sha1\", \"label_true\"], how=\"inner\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    pred_cols = [c for c in merged.columns if c.startswith(\"pred_idx__\")]\n",
        "    conf_cols = [c for c in merged.columns if c.startswith(\"confidence__\")]\n",
        "\n",
        "    merged[\"num_unique_predictions\"] = merged[pred_cols].nunique(axis=1)\n",
        "    merged[\"mean_confidence\"] = merged[conf_cols].mean(axis=1)\n",
        "    merged[\"max_confidence_gap\"] = merged[conf_cols].max(axis=1) - merged[conf_cols].min(axis=1)\n",
        "    merged = merged.sort_values([\"num_unique_predictions\", \"max_confidence_gap\"], ascending=[False, False])\n",
        "    return merged.reset_index(drop=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "def find_last_conv_layer(model: nn.Module) -> Optional[nn.Module]:\n",
        "    for module in reversed(list(model.modules())):\n",
        "        if isinstance(module, nn.Conv2d):\n",
        "            return module\n",
        "    return None\n",
        "\n",
        "class GradCAMRunner:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, model: nn.Module, target_layer: nn.Module):\n",
        "        self.model = model\n",
        "        self.target_layer = target_layer\n",
        "        self.activations = None\n",
        "        self.gradients = None\n",
        "        self.fwd_handle = target_layer.register_forward_hook(self._forward_hook)\n",
        "        self.bwd_handle = target_layer.register_full_backward_hook(self._backward_hook)\n",
        "\n",
        "    def _forward_hook(self, module, input, output):\n",
        "        self.activations = output.detach()\n",
        "\n",
        "    def _backward_hook(self, module, grad_input, grad_output):\n",
        "        self.gradients = grad_output[0].detach()\n",
        "\n",
        "    def close(self):\n",
        "        self.fwd_handle.remove()\n",
        "        self.bwd_handle.remove()\n",
        "\n",
        "    def generate(self, x: torch.Tensor, class_idx: int) -> np.ndarray:\n",
        "        self.model.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n",
        "        logits = extract_logits(self.model(x))\n",
        "        score = logits[:, class_idx].sum()\n",
        "        score.backward(retain_graph=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "        acts = self.activations\n",
        "        grads = self.gradients\n",
        "        if acts is None or grads is None:\n",
        "            raise RuntimeError(\"Grad-CAM hooks did not capture activations/gradients.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "        weights = grads.mean(dim=(2, 3), keepdim=True)\n",
        "        cam = (weights * acts).sum(dim=1, keepdim=True)\n",
        "        cam = torch.relu(cam)\n",
        "        cam = F.interpolate(cam, size=x.shape[-2:], mode=\"bilinear\", align_corners=False)\n",
        "        cam = cam[0, 0].detach().cpu().numpy()\n",
        "        cam = (cam - cam.min()) / (cam.max() - cam.min() + 1e-8)\n",
        "        return cam\n",
        "\n",
        "def overlay_cam_on_image(img: Image.Image, cam: np.ndarray, alpha: float = 0.35) -> Image.Image:\n",
        "    img_arr = np.asarray(img.convert(\"RGB\")).astype(np.float32)\n",
        "    heatmap = plt.get_cmap(\"jet\")(cam)[..., :3]\n",
        "    heatmap = (heatmap * 255.0).astype(np.uint8)\n",
        "    overlay = (1 - alpha) * img_arr + alpha * heatmap.astype(np.float32)\n",
        "    return Image.fromarray(np.clip(overlay, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8))\n",
        "\n",
        "def generate_gradcam_examples(record: Dict[str, Any], split_name: str = \"valid\", max_items: int = 10) -> None:\n",
        "    if not CFG.run_gradcam or record.get(\"run_name\") == \"z_soft_vote_ensemble\":\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    if record.get(\"run_name\") == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\":\n",
        "        # Build a temporary bundle-like model directly from the checkpoint.\n",
        "        spec = make_spec(\n",
        "            run_name=\"__baseline_cam__\",\n",
        "            family=\"old_checkpoint\",\n",
        "            architecture=\"old_checkpoint\",\n",
        "            init_mode=\"eval_only\",\n",
        "            branch_name=\"RAW\",\n",
        "            aug_policy=\"none\",\n",
        "            image_size=CFG.image_size,\n",
        "            batch_size=CFG.batch_size,\n",
        "            epochs=1,\n",
        "            patience=1,\n",
        "            lr=CFG.lr,\n",
        "            weight_decay=CFG.weight_decay,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        model = build_model_from_spec(spec).to(CFG.device)\n",
        "        run_dir = CFG.paths.analysis_root / \"gradcam\" / record[\"run_name\"]\n",
        "        pred_path = CFG.paths.baseline_root / f\"{split_name}_pristine\" / \"predictions.csv\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        spec = record_to_spec(record)\n",
        "        model, _, _ = load_model_bundle(Path(record[\"bundle_best\"]))\n",
        "        model = model.to(CFG.device)\n",
        "        run_dir = CFG.paths.analysis_root / \"gradcam\" / record[\"run_name\"]\n",
        "        pred_path = get_run_dir(spec) / \"eval\" / f\"{split_name}_pristine\" / \"predictions.csv\"\n",
        "\n",
        "    if not pred_path.exists():\n",
        "        return\n",
        "\n",
        "    run_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    pred_df = pd.read_csv(pred_path)\n",
        "    candidates = pd.concat([\n",
        "        pred_df[pred_df[\"is_correct\"] == True].sort_values(\"confidence\", ascending=False).head(max_items // 2),\n",
        "        pred_df[pred_df[\"is_correct\"] == False].sort_values(\"confidence\", ascending=False).head(max_items // 2),\n",
        "    ], ignore_index=True)\n",
        "    if candidates.empty:\n",
        "        return\n",
        "\n",
        "    target_layer = find_last_conv_layer(model)\n",
        "    if target_layer is None:\n",
        "        print(f\"Skipping Grad-CAM for {record['run_name']} — no Conv2d layer found.\")\n",
        "        return\n",
        "\n",
        "    cam_runner = GradCAMRunner(model, target_layer)\n",
        "    transform = build_eval_transform(int(record.get(\"image_size\", CFG.image_size)))\n",
        "\n",
        "    for i, row in enumerate(candidates.itertuples(index=False)):\n",
        "        img = Image.open(row.filepath).convert(\"RGB\")\n",
        "        x = transform(img).unsqueeze(0).to(CFG.device)\n",
        "        class_idx = int(row.pred_idx)\n",
        "        cam = cam_runner.generate(x, class_idx)\n",
        "        overlay = overlay_cam_on_image(img.resize((x.shape[-1], x.shape[-2])), cam)\n",
        "        overlay.save(run_dir / f\"{i:02d}__true_{row.label_true}__pred_{row.pred_label}__conf_{row.confidence:.3f}.png\")\n",
        "    cam_runner.close()\n",
        "    del model\n",
        "    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
        "        torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n",
        "\n",
        "def extract_embeddings_for_record(record: Dict[str, Any], split_name: str = \"valid\") -> Optional[pd.DataFrame]:\n",
        "    if not CFG.run_embedding_analysis or record.get(\"run_name\") == \"z_soft_vote_ensemble\":\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "\n",
        "    if record.get(\"run_name\") == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\":\n",
        "        spec = make_spec(\n",
        "            run_name=\"__baseline_embed__\",\n",
        "            family=\"old_checkpoint\",\n",
        "            architecture=\"old_checkpoint\",\n",
        "            init_mode=\"eval_only\",\n",
        "            branch_name=\"RAW\",\n",
        "            aug_policy=\"none\",\n",
        "            image_size=CFG.image_size,\n",
        "            batch_size=CFG.batch_size,\n",
        "            epochs=1,\n",
        "            patience=1,\n",
        "            lr=CFG.lr,\n",
        "            weight_decay=CFG.weight_decay,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        model = build_model_from_spec(spec)\n",
        "        manifest_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[\"RAW\"].copy() if split_name == \"all_splits\" else BRANCH_MANIFESTS[\"RAW\"][BRANCH_MANIFESTS[\"RAW\"][\"split_canonical\"] == split_name].copy()\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        spec = record_to_spec(record)\n",
        "        model, _, _ = load_model_bundle(Path(record[\"bundle_best\"]))\n",
        "        manifest_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name].copy() if split_name == \"all_splits\" else BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name][BRANCH_MANIFESTS[spec.branch_name][\"split_canonical\"] == split_name].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "    model = model.to(CFG.device)\n",
        "    holder: Dict[str, torch.Tensor] = {}\n",
        "    target_linear = None\n",
        "    for module in reversed(list(model.modules())):\n",
        "        if isinstance(module, nn.Linear):\n",
        "            target_linear = module\n",
        "            break\n",
        "    hook = None\n",
        "    if target_linear is not None:\n",
        "        def _pre_hook(module, args):\n",
        "            holder[\"feat\"] = args[0].detach()\n",
        "        hook = target_linear.register_forward_pre_hook(_pre_hook)\n",
        "\n",
        "    ds = ManifestImageDataset(manifest_df, image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\", transform=build_eval_transform(int(record.get(\"image_size\", CFG.image_size))))\n",
        "    loader = torch.utils.data.DataLoader(ds, batch_size=CFG.eval_batch_size, shuffle=False, num_workers=CFG.num_workers)\n",
        "\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    with torch.inference_mode():\n",
        "        for batch_x, batch_y, batch_meta in tqdm(loader, desc=f\"embed {record['run_name']}\", leave=False):\n",
        "            batch_x = batch_x.to(CFG.device)\n",
        "            logits = extract_logits(model(batch_x))\n",
        "            feats = holder.get(\"feat\", logits).detach().cpu().numpy()\n",
        "            if feats.ndim > 2:\n",
        "                feats = feats.reshape(feats.shape[0], -1)\n",
        "            for i in range(len(batch_y)):\n",
        "                rec = {\n",
        "                    \"file_sha1\": batch_meta[\"file_sha1\"][i] if isinstance(batch_meta[\"file_sha1\"], list) else batch_meta[\"file_sha1\"],\n",
        "                    \"label_true_idx\": int(batch_y[i].item()),\n",
        "                    \"label_true\": CFG.class_names[int(batch_y[i].item())],\n",
        "                    \"filepath\": batch_meta[\"filepath\"][i] if isinstance(batch_meta[\"filepath\"], list) else batch_meta[\"filepath\"],\n",
        "                    \"split_canonical\": batch_meta[\"split_canonical\"][i] if isinstance(batch_meta[\"split_canonical\"], list) else batch_meta[\"split_canonical\"],\n",
        "                }\n",
        "                for j in range(feats.shape[1]):\n",
        "                    rec[f\"feat_{j}\"] = float(feats[i, j])\n",
        "                rows.append(rec)\n",
        "    if hook is not None:\n",
        "        hook.remove()\n",
        "    del model\n",
        "    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
        "        torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "\n",
        "def reduce_and_plot_embeddings(embed_df: pd.DataFrame, out_dir: Path, title_prefix: str) -> None:\n",
        "    if embed_df is None or embed_df.empty:\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    feat_cols = [c for c in embed_df.columns if c.startswith(\"feat_\")]\n",
        "    if not feat_cols:\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    X = embed_df[feat_cols].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n",
        "    X = PCA(n_components=min(25, X.shape[1], max(2, X.shape[0] - 1))).fit_transform(X)\n",
        "\n",
        "    reducers = {\"pca2\": PCA(n_components=2, random_state=CFG.random_seed)}\n",
        "    if HAS_UMAP:\n",
        "        reducers[\"umap2\"] = umap.UMAP(n_components=2, random_state=CFG.random_seed, n_neighbors=min(15, len(embed_df) - 1))\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        reducers[\"tsne2\"] = TSNE(n_components=2, random_state=CFG.random_seed, init=\"pca\", learning_rate=\"auto\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    for name, reducer in reducers.items():\n",
        "        try:\n",
        "            Z = reducer.fit_transform(X)\n",
        "        except Exception as exc:\n",
        "            print(f\"Embedding reducer failed ({name}): {exc}\")\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        plot_df = embed_df.copy()\n",
        "        plot_df[\"x\"] = Z[:, 0]\n",
        "        plot_df[\"y\"] = Z[:, 1]\n",
        "\n",
        "        for color_col in [\"label_true\"]:\n",
        "            plt.figure(figsize=(6, 5), dpi=140)\n",
        "            sns.scatterplot(data=plot_df, x=\"x\", y=\"y\", hue=color_col, s=40, alpha=0.85)\n",
        "            plt.title(f\"{title_prefix} — {name} colored by {color_col}\")\n",
        "            plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "            plt.savefig(out_dir / f\"{name}_{color_col}.png\")\n",
        "            plt.close()\n",
        "\n",
        "def nearest_neighbor_leakage_audit(embed_df: pd.DataFrame, split_name: str, out_path: Path) -> None:\n",
        "    if embed_df is None or embed_df.empty or not CFG.run_nearest_neighbor_audit:\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    feat_cols = [c for c in embed_df.columns if c.startswith(\"feat_\")]\n",
        "    if len(feat_cols) < 2:\n",
        "        return\n",
        "    X = embed_df[feat_cols].to_numpy(dtype=np.float32)\n",
        "    n_neighbors = min(6, len(embed_df))\n",
        "    nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=n_neighbors, metric=\"cosine\")\n",
        "    nn_model.fit(X)\n",
        "    distances, indices = nn_model.kneighbors(X)\n",
        "\n",
        "    rows = []\n",
        "    for i in range(len(embed_df)):\n",
        "        for rank in range(1, n_neighbors):\n",
        "            j = int(indices[i, rank])\n",
        "            sim = 1.0 - float(distances[i, rank])\n",
        "            rows.append({\n",
        "                \"query_file_sha1\": embed_df.iloc[i][\"file_sha1\"],\n",
        "                \"neighbor_file_sha1\": embed_df.iloc[j][\"file_sha1\"],\n",
        "                \"query_filepath\": embed_df.iloc[i][\"filepath\"],\n",
        "                \"neighbor_filepath\": embed_df.iloc[j][\"filepath\"],\n",
        "                \"query_label\": embed_df.iloc[i][\"label_true\"],\n",
        "                \"neighbor_label\": embed_df.iloc[j][\"label_true\"],\n",
        "                \"query_split\": embed_df.iloc[i].get(\"split_canonical\", split_name),\n",
        "                \"neighbor_split\": embed_df.iloc[j].get(\"split_canonical\", split_name),\n",
        "                \"cross_split\": embed_df.iloc[i].get(\"split_canonical\", split_name) != embed_df.iloc[j].get(\"split_canonical\", split_name),\n",
        "                \"cosine_similarity\": sim,\n",
        "                \"split_name\": split_name,\n",
        "            })\n",
        "    df_rows = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
        "    if not df_rows.empty:\n",
        "        df_rows = df_rows.sort_values([\"cross_split\", \"cosine_similarity\"], ascending=[False, False])\n",
        "    df_rows.to_csv(out_path, index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "def label_noise_review_table(registry: List[Dict[str, Any]], split_name: str = \"valid\", top_k: int = 3) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(registry)\n",
        "    top_df = top_successful_runs(df, k=top_k, exclude_baseline=False)\n",
        "    if top_df.empty:\n",
        "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "\n",
        "    merged = None\n",
        "    for _, row in top_df.iterrows():\n",
        "        run_name = row[\"run_name\"]\n",
        "        if run_name == \"z_soft_vote_ensemble\":\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        pred_path = CFG.paths.baseline_root / f\"{split_name}_pristine\" / \"predictions.csv\" if run_name == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\" else get_run_dir(record_to_spec(row.to_dict())) / \"eval\" / f\"{split_name}_pristine\" / \"predictions.csv\"\n",
        "        if not pred_path.exists():\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "        pred_df = pd.read_csv(pred_path)[[\"file_sha1\", \"label_true\", \"pred_label\", \"confidence\"]].copy()\n",
        "        pred_df = pred_df.rename(columns={\n",
        "            \"pred_label\": f\"pred_label__{run_name}\",\n",
        "            \"confidence\": f\"confidence__{run_name}\",\n",
        "        })\n",
        "        merged = pred_df if merged is None else merged.merge(pred_df, on=[\"file_sha1\", \"label_true\"], how=\"inner\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    if merged is None or merged.empty:\n",
        "        return pd.DataFrame()\n",
        "\n",
        "    pred_cols = [c for c in merged.columns if c.startswith(\"pred_label__\")]\n",
        "    conf_cols = [c for c in merged.columns if c.startswith(\"confidence__\")]\n",
        "    disagreement_rows = []\n",
        "    for _, row in merged.iterrows():\n",
        "        preds = [row[c] for c in pred_cols]\n",
        "        confs = [float(row[c]) for c in conf_cols]\n",
        "        wrong_votes = sum(int(pred != row[\"label_true\"]) for pred in preds)\n",
        "        mean_conf = float(np.mean(confs)) if confs else float(\"nan\")\n",
        "        if wrong_votes >= max(2, len(pred_cols) // 2 + 1) and mean_conf >= 0.75:\n",
        "            disagreement_rows.append({\n",
        "                \"file_sha1\": row[\"file_sha1\"],\n",
        "                \"label_true\": row[\"label_true\"],\n",
        "                \"wrong_votes\": int(wrong_votes),\n",
        "                \"mean_confidence\": mean_conf,\n",
        "            })\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame(disagreement_rows).sort_values([\"wrong_votes\", \"mean_confidence\"], ascending=[False, False])\n",
        "\n",
        "analysis_runs_df = get_top_analysis_runs(RUN_REGISTRY, k=2)\n",
        "if not analysis_runs_df.empty:\n",
        "    print_rule(\"RUNNING INTERPRETABILITY / ERROR ANALYSIS\")\n",
        "    disagreement_df = prediction_disagreement_table(RUN_REGISTRY, split_name=\"valid\", top_k=min(3, len(analysis_runs_df)))\n",
        "    disagreement_path = CFG.paths.analysis_root / \"prediction_disagreement_valid.csv\"\n",
        "    disagreement_df.to_csv(disagreement_path, index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "    noise_df = label_noise_review_table(RUN_REGISTRY, split_name=\"valid\", top_k=min(3, len(analysis_runs_df)))\n",
        "    noise_path = CFG.paths.analysis_root / \"label_noise_review_candidates.csv\"\n",
        "    noise_df.to_csv(noise_path, index=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "    for _, row in analysis_runs_df.iterrows():\n",
        "        rec = row.to_dict()\n",
        "        generate_gradcam_examples(rec, split_name=\"valid\", max_items=10)\n",
        "        if CFG.run_embedding_analysis:\n",
        "            embed_df = extract_embeddings_for_record(rec, split_name=\"all_splits\")\n",
        "            if embed_df is not None and not embed_df.empty:\n",
        "                out_dir = CFG.paths.analysis_root / \"embeddings\" / normalize_token(rec[\"run_name\"])\n",
        "                reduce_and_plot_embeddings(embed_df, out_dir=out_dir, title_prefix=rec[\"run_name\"])\n",
        "                nearest_neighbor_leakage_audit(embed_df, split_name=\"all_splits\", out_path=out_dir / \"nearest_neighbors.csv\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"Saved disagreement table to:\", disagreement_path.resolve())\n",
        "    print(\"Saved label-noise review table to:\", noise_path.resolve())\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "d1b80d44",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "d1b80d44"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Wrapping Up & Picking the Best Model\n",
        "\n",
        "Finally, we rank all the models using a weighted scoring system based purely on the Validation set.\n",
        "\n",
        "We look for:\n",
        "1. The model with the highest pure accuracy.\n",
        "2. The model that survived the \"Challenge\" images the best.\n",
        "3. The model with the most reliable confidence scores.\n",
        "\n",
        "At the very end, we output a plain-English summary comparing our best new model against the original baseline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "id": "cdf47793",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "cdf47793"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# SECTION O + P + Q — Leaderboard, robust selection, final retrain, export, and written summary\n",
        "\n",
        "def evaluate_holdout_challenges_for_selected(registry: List[Dict[str, Any]], top_k: int) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n",
        "    df = leaderboard_df_from_registry(registry)\n",
        "    finalists = top_successful_runs(df, k=top_k, exclude_baseline=False)\n",
        "    selected_names = set(finalists[\"run_name\"].tolist())\n",
        "    out_registry = []\n",
        "    for rec in registry:\n",
        "        if rec.get(\"run_name\") not in selected_names:\n",
        "            out_registry.append(rec)\n",
        "            continue\n",
        "\n",
        "        run_name = rec.get(\"run_name\")\n",
        "        branch_name = rec.get(\"branch_name\", \"RAW\")\n",
        "        image_size = int(rec.get(\"image_size\", CFG.image_size))\n",
        "        out_dir = (CFG.paths.baseline_root if run_name == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\" else get_run_dir(record_to_spec(rec))) / \"challenge_eval\" / \"test\"\n",
        "        suite_rows = []\n",
        "        for suite_name in CFG.challenge_suite_names:\n",
        "            challenge_df = materialize_challenge_manifest(branch_name=branch_name, split_name=\"test\", suite_name=suite_name, force=CFG.force_regenerate_challenge_copies)\n",
        "            if run_name == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\":\n",
        "                _, summary = evaluate_native_old_checkpoint_on_manifest(\n",
        "                    challenge_df,\n",
        "                    image_path_col=\"challenge_filepath\",\n",
        "                    out_dir=out_dir / suite_name,\n",
        "                    split_name=f\"test_{suite_name}\",\n",
        "                )\n",
        "            elif run_name == \"z_soft_vote_ensemble\":\n",
        "                continue\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                _, summary = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "                    Path(rec[\"bundle_best\"]),\n",
        "                    df=challenge_df,\n",
        "                    image_path_col=\"challenge_filepath\",\n",
        "                    image_size=image_size,\n",
        "                    out_dir=out_dir / suite_name,\n",
        "                    split_name=f\"test_{suite_name}\",\n",
        "                    use_temperature=float(rec.get(\"temperature\", 1.0)),\n",
        "                )\n",
        "            suite_rows.append({\n",
        "                \"challenge_suite\": suite_name,\n",
        "                \"macro_f1\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "                \"balanced_accuracy\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "                \"worst_class_recall\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "                \"ece\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "                \"macro_f1_delta_vs_pristine\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"] - float(rec.get(\"test_macro_f1\", np.nan)),\n",
        "                \"balanced_accuracy_delta_vs_pristine\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"] - float(rec.get(\"test_balanced_accuracy\", np.nan)),\n",
        "                \"worst_class_recall_delta_vs_pristine\": summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"] - float(rec.get(\"test_worst_class_recall\", np.nan)),\n",
        "            })\n",
        "        suite_df = pd.DataFrame(suite_rows)\n",
        "        if not suite_df.empty:\n",
        "            suite_df.to_csv(out_dir / \"challenge_test_summary.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "            rec[\"test_challenge_mean_macro_f1\"] = float(suite_df[\"macro_f1\"].mean())\n",
        "            rec[\"test_challenge_worst_macro_f1\"] = float(suite_df[\"macro_f1\"].min())\n",
        "            rec[\"test_challenge_mean_balanced_accuracy\"] = float(suite_df[\"balanced_accuracy\"].mean())\n",
        "            rec[\"test_challenge_summary_path\"] = str((out_dir / \"challenge_test_summary.csv\").resolve())\n",
        "        out_registry.append(rec)\n",
        "    return out_registry\n",
        "\n",
        "RUN_REGISTRY = evaluate_holdout_challenges_for_selected(RUN_REGISTRY, top_k=CFG.holdout_challenge_top_k)\n",
        "save_json(CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"run_registry_after_holdout_challenges.json\", RUN_REGISTRY)\n",
        "\n",
        "def enrich_leaderboard(df: pd.DataFrame) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
        "    if df.empty:\n",
        "        return df\n",
        "    work = df.copy()\n",
        "    for col in [\n",
        "        \"valid_macro_f1\", \"valid_balanced_accuracy\", \"valid_worst_class_recall\", \"valid_ece\",\n",
        "        \"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\", \"valid_challenge_worst_macro_f1\", \"test_macro_f1\",\n",
        "        \"test_balanced_accuracy\", \"test_worst_class_recall\", \"test_ece\", \"valid_brier_score\",\n",
        "    ]:\n",
        "        if col not in work.columns:\n",
        "            work[col] = np.nan\n",
        "\n",
        "    work[\"recipe_key\"] = work.apply(\n",
        "        lambda r: \"__\".join([\n",
        "            normalize_token(r.get(\"family\", \"\")),\n",
        "            normalize_token(r.get(\"architecture\", \"\")),\n",
        "            normalize_token(r.get(\"branch_name\", \"\")),\n",
        "            normalize_token(r.get(\"aug_policy\", \"\")),\n",
        "            normalize_token(f\"img{r.get('image_size', '')}\"),\n",
        "            normalize_token(f\"lr{r.get('lr', '')}\"),\n",
        "            normalize_token(f\"wd{r.get('weight_decay', '')}\"),\n",
        "            normalize_token(f\"drop{r.get('dropout', '')}\"),\n",
        "            normalize_token(f\"ls{r.get('label_smoothing', '')}\"),\n",
        "            normalize_token(f\"freeze{r.get('freeze_backbone_epochs', '')}\"),\n",
        "            normalize_token(r.get(\"class_balancing\", \"\")),\n",
        "            normalize_token(r.get(\"loss_name\", \"\")),\n",
        "        ]),\n",
        "        axis=1,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    work[\"clean_rank_score\"] = (\n",
        "        0.45 * work[\"valid_macro_f1\"].fillna(-1.0)\n",
        "        + 0.25 * work[\"valid_balanced_accuracy\"].fillna(-1.0)\n",
        "        + 0.20 * work[\"valid_worst_class_recall\"].fillna(-1.0)\n",
        "        - 0.05 * work[\"valid_ece\"].fillna(1.0)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    robust_component = work[\"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\"].fillna(work[\"valid_macro_f1\"])\n",
        "    robust_worst = work[\"valid_challenge_worst_macro_f1\"].fillna(work[\"valid_macro_f1\"])\n",
        "    work[\"robust_rank_score\"] = (\n",
        "        0.35 * work[\"valid_macro_f1\"].fillna(-1.0)\n",
        "        + 0.20 * work[\"valid_balanced_accuracy\"].fillna(-1.0)\n",
        "        + 0.15 * work[\"valid_worst_class_recall\"].fillna(-1.0)\n",
        "        + 0.20 * robust_component.fillna(-1.0)\n",
        "        + 0.10 * robust_worst.fillna(-1.0)\n",
        "        - 0.05 * work[\"valid_ece\"].fillna(1.0)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    work[\"calibration_rank_score\"] = (\n",
        "        work[\"valid_macro_f1\"].fillna(-1.0)\n",
        "        - 0.25 * work[\"valid_ece\"].fillna(1.0)\n",
        "        - 0.10 * work[\"valid_brier_score\"].fillna(1.0)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return work\n",
        "\n",
        "run_level_df = enrich_leaderboard(leaderboard_df_from_registry(RUN_REGISTRY))\n",
        "run_level_csv = CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"leaderboard_run_level.csv\"\n",
        "run_level_json = CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"leaderboard_run_level.json\"\n",
        "run_level_df.to_csv(run_level_csv, index=False)\n",
        "save_json(run_level_json, run_level_df.to_dict(orient=\"records\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "recipe_agg_df = (\n",
        "    run_level_df.groupby(\"recipe_key\", dropna=False)\n",
        "    .agg(\n",
        "        n_runs=(\"run_name\", \"size\"),\n",
        "        example_run_name=(\"run_name\", \"first\"),\n",
        "        family=(\"family\", \"first\"),\n",
        "        architecture=(\"architecture\", \"first\"),\n",
        "        branch_name=(\"branch_name\", \"first\"),\n",
        "        aug_policy=(\"aug_policy\", \"first\"),\n",
        "        image_size=(\"image_size\", \"first\"),\n",
        "        clean_rank_score_mean=(\"clean_rank_score\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        clean_rank_score_std=(\"clean_rank_score\", \"std\"),\n",
        "        robust_rank_score_mean=(\"robust_rank_score\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        robust_rank_score_std=(\"robust_rank_score\", \"std\"),\n",
        "        calibration_rank_score_mean=(\"calibration_rank_score\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        valid_macro_f1_mean=(\"valid_macro_f1\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        valid_macro_f1_std=(\"valid_macro_f1\", \"std\"),\n",
        "        valid_balanced_accuracy_mean=(\"valid_balanced_accuracy\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        valid_worst_class_recall_mean=(\"valid_worst_class_recall\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        valid_ece_mean=(\"valid_ece\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1_mean=(\"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        test_macro_f1_mean=(\"test_macro_f1\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        test_balanced_accuracy_mean=(\"test_balanced_accuracy\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .reset_index()\n",
        ")\n",
        "recipe_agg_df = recipe_agg_df.sort_values(\n",
        "    by=[\"robust_rank_score_mean\", \"clean_rank_score_mean\", \"valid_macro_f1_mean\"],\n",
        "    ascending=[False, False, False],\n",
        "    na_position=\"last\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "recipe_agg_csv = CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"leaderboard_recipe_aggregated.csv\"\n",
        "recipe_agg_json = CFG.paths.experiment_root / \"leaderboard_recipe_aggregated.json\"\n",
        "recipe_agg_df.to_csv(recipe_agg_csv, index=False)\n",
        "save_json(recipe_agg_json, recipe_agg_df.to_dict(orient=\"records\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "def pick_best_records(run_df: pd.DataFrame) -> Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]:\n",
        "    success_df = run_df[run_df[\"status\"] == \"success\"].copy()\n",
        "    if success_df.empty:\n",
        "        raise RuntimeError(\"No successful runs are available for selection.\")\n",
        "\n",
        "    best_clean = success_df.sort_values(\n",
        "        by=[\"clean_rank_score\", \"valid_macro_f1\", \"valid_balanced_accuracy\", \"valid_worst_class_recall\", \"valid_ece\"],\n",
        "        ascending=[False, False, False, False, True],\n",
        "        na_position=\"last\",\n",
        "    ).iloc[0].to_dict()\n",
        "\n",
        "    best_robust = success_df.sort_values(\n",
        "        by=[\"robust_rank_score\", \"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\", \"valid_macro_f1\", \"valid_ece\"],\n",
        "        ascending=[False, False, False, True],\n",
        "        na_position=\"last\",\n",
        "    ).iloc[0].to_dict()\n",
        "\n",
        "    best_cal = success_df.sort_values(\n",
        "        by=[\"calibration_rank_score\", \"valid_ece\", \"valid_macro_f1\"],\n",
        "        ascending=[False, True, False],\n",
        "        na_position=\"last\",\n",
        "    ).iloc[0].to_dict()\n",
        "\n",
        "    return {\n",
        "        \"best_clean_validation\": best_clean,\n",
        "        \"best_robust_validation\": best_robust,\n",
        "        \"best_calibrated_validation\": best_cal,\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "best_record_sets = pick_best_records(run_level_df)\n",
        "\n",
        "def choose_deployment_candidate(best_sets: Dict[str, Dict[str, Any]]) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n",
        "    clean = best_sets[\"best_clean_validation\"]\n",
        "    robust = best_sets[\"best_robust_validation\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    clean_drop = float(clean.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", np.nan)) - float(clean.get(\"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\", clean.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", np.nan)))\n",
        "    robust_drop = float(robust.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", np.nan)) - float(robust.get(\"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\", robust.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", np.nan)))\n",
        "\n",
        "    if (\n",
        "        float(robust.get(\"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\", -1.0)) >= float(clean.get(\"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\", -1.0)) - 0.01\n",
        "        and robust_drop <= clean_drop + 0.02\n",
        "    ):\n",
        "        selected = robust.copy()\n",
        "        selected[\"selection_rationale\"] = \"robust_candidate_preferred\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        selected = clean.copy()\n",
        "        selected[\"selection_rationale\"] = \"clean_candidate_preferred\"\n",
        "    return selected\n",
        "\n",
        "selected_candidate = choose_deployment_candidate(best_record_sets)\n",
        "\n",
        "FINAL_RETRAIN_RECORD = None\n",
        "if CFG.run_final_retrain and selected_candidate.get(\"family\") not in {\"ensemble\"} and selected_candidate.get(\"run_name\") != \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\":\n",
        "    print_rule(\"OPTIONAL FINAL RETRAIN ON TRAIN+VALID\")\n",
        "    base_spec = record_to_spec(selected_candidate)\n",
        "    final_spec = make_spec(\n",
        "        run_name=f\"{base_spec.run_name}__final_trainplusvalid\",\n",
        "        family=base_spec.family,\n",
        "        architecture=base_spec.architecture,\n",
        "        init_mode=base_spec.init_mode,\n",
        "        branch_name=base_spec.branch_name,\n",
        "        aug_policy=base_spec.aug_policy,\n",
        "        image_size=base_spec.image_size,\n",
        "        batch_size=base_spec.batch_size,\n",
        "        epochs=max(base_spec.epochs, CFG.epochs),\n",
        "        patience=max(base_spec.patience, CFG.patience),\n",
        "        lr=base_spec.lr,\n",
        "        weight_decay=base_spec.weight_decay,\n",
        "        dropout=base_spec.dropout,\n",
        "        label_smoothing=base_spec.label_smoothing,\n",
        "        freeze_backbone_epochs=base_spec.freeze_backbone_epochs,\n",
        "        stronger_regularization=base_spec.stronger_regularization,\n",
        "        class_balancing=base_spec.class_balancing,\n",
        "        loss_name=base_spec.loss_name,\n",
        "        focal_gamma=base_spec.focal_gamma,\n",
        "        notes=f\"Final retrain on train+valid after locking recipe from {base_spec.run_name}.\",\n",
        "        seed=CFG.final_retrain_seed,\n",
        "        use_offline_aug_cache=not CFG.run_online_aug_for_final_retrain,\n",
        "        use_online_aug=CFG.run_online_aug_for_final_retrain,\n",
        "        final_retrain=True,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "    final_run_dir = get_run_dir(final_spec)\n",
        "    final_run_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
        "    save_json(final_run_dir / \"spec.json\", asdict(final_spec))\n",
        "\n",
        "    try:\n",
        "        seed_everything(final_spec.seed, deterministic=CFG.deterministic)\n",
        "        model = build_model_from_spec(final_spec).to(CFG.device)\n",
        "        train_loader, _, _, class_weight_tensor, _ = build_dataloaders_for_spec(final_spec, combine_train_valid=True)\n",
        "        loss_fn = build_loss_function(\n",
        "            final_spec,\n",
        "            class_weight_tensor.to(CFG.device) if class_weight_tensor is not None else None,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        if final_spec.freeze_backbone_epochs > 0:\n",
        "            freeze_backbone(model, final_spec)\n",
        "        else:\n",
        "            unfreeze_all(model)\n",
        "        optimizer = build_optimizer(model, final_spec)\n",
        "        scheduler = build_scheduler(optimizer, total_epochs=final_spec.epochs)\n",
        "        scaler = torch.cuda.amp.GradScaler(enabled=(CFG.use_amp and CFG.device.startswith(\"cuda\")))\n",
        "\n",
        "        best_loss = float(\"inf\")\n",
        "        patience_ctr = 0\n",
        "        history_rows = []\n",
        "        for epoch in range(1, final_spec.epochs + 1):\n",
        "            if epoch == final_spec.freeze_backbone_epochs + 1 and final_spec.freeze_backbone_epochs > 0:\n",
        "                unfreeze_all(model)\n",
        "                optimizer = build_optimizer(model, final_spec)\n",
        "                scheduler = build_scheduler(optimizer, total_epochs=max(1, final_spec.epochs - epoch + 1))\n",
        "            train_stats = train_one_epoch(model, train_loader, optimizer, loss_fn, device=CFG.device, scaler=scaler, max_grad_norm=CFG.max_grad_norm)\n",
        "            history_rows.append({\"epoch\": epoch, **train_stats})\n",
        "            if train_stats[\"train_loss\"] < best_loss:\n",
        "                best_loss = train_stats[\"train_loss\"]\n",
        "                patience_ctr = 0\n",
        "                save_model_bundle(bundle_checkpoint_path(final_run_dir, \"best\"), model, final_spec, extra={\"best_epoch\": epoch})\n",
        "            else:\n",
        "                patience_ctr += 1\n",
        "            save_model_bundle(bundle_checkpoint_path(final_run_dir, \"last\"), model, final_spec, extra={\"epoch\": epoch})\n",
        "            scheduler.step()\n",
        "            if patience_ctr >= max(3, final_spec.patience):\n",
        "                break\n",
        "        save_training_history(history_rows, final_run_dir)\n",
        "\n",
        "        test_df = BRANCH_MANIFESTS[final_spec.branch_name][BRANCH_MANIFESTS[final_spec.branch_name][\"split_canonical\"] == \"test\"].copy()\n",
        "        _, final_test_summary = evaluate_bundle_on_dataframe(\n",
        "            bundle_checkpoint_path(final_run_dir, \"best\"),\n",
        "            df=test_df,\n",
        "            image_path_col=\"branch_filepath\",\n",
        "            image_size=final_spec.image_size,\n",
        "            out_dir=final_run_dir / \"eval\" / \"test_pristine\",\n",
        "            split_name=\"test_pristine_final_retrain\",\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        final_test_challenge_df = evaluate_challenge_suites_for_bundle(\n",
        "            bundle_checkpoint_path(final_run_dir, \"best\"),\n",
        "            branch_name=final_spec.branch_name,\n",
        "            split_name=\"test\",\n",
        "            suite_names=CFG.challenge_suite_names,\n",
        "            out_dir=final_run_dir / \"challenge_eval\" / \"test\",\n",
        "            image_size=final_spec.image_size,\n",
        "        )\n",
        "        FINAL_RETRAIN_RECORD = {\n",
        "            \"run_name\": final_spec.run_name,\n",
        "            \"status\": \"success\",\n",
        "            \"family\": final_spec.family,\n",
        "            \"architecture\": final_spec.architecture,\n",
        "            \"branch_name\": final_spec.branch_name,\n",
        "            \"aug_policy\": final_spec.aug_policy,\n",
        "            \"image_size\": final_spec.image_size,\n",
        "            \"test_macro_f1\": final_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"macro_f1\"],\n",
        "            \"test_balanced_accuracy\": final_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"balanced_accuracy\"],\n",
        "            \"test_worst_class_recall\": final_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"worst_class_recall\"],\n",
        "            \"test_ece\": final_test_summary[\"metrics\"][\"ece\"],\n",
        "            \"test_challenge_mean_macro_f1\": float(final_test_challenge_df[\"macro_f1\"].mean()) if isinstance(final_test_challenge_df, pd.DataFrame) and not final_test_challenge_df.empty else np.nan,\n",
        "            \"bundle_best\": str(bundle_checkpoint_path(final_run_dir, \"best\").resolve()),\n",
        "            \"notes\": \"Final retrain on train+valid after model selection.\",\n",
        "        }\n",
        "    except Exception as exc:\n",
        "        (get_run_dir(final_spec) / \"error.txt\").write_text(traceback.format_exc(), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "        print(\"Final retrain failed:\", exc)\n",
        "\n",
        "if FINAL_RETRAIN_RECORD is not None:\n",
        "    RUN_REGISTRY.append(FINAL_RETRAIN_RECORD)\n",
        "\n",
        "final_run_level_df = enrich_leaderboard(leaderboard_df_from_registry(RUN_REGISTRY))\n",
        "final_run_level_df.to_csv(CFG.paths.final_root / \"leaderboard_final.csv\", index=False)\n",
        "save_json(CFG.paths.final_root / \"leaderboard_final.json\", final_run_level_df.to_dict(orient=\"records\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "best_clean = best_record_sets[\"best_clean_validation\"]\n",
        "best_robust = best_record_sets[\"best_robust_validation\"]\n",
        "best_cal = best_record_sets[\"best_calibrated_validation\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "deployment_candidate = selected_candidate.copy()\n",
        "if FINAL_RETRAIN_RECORD is not None:\n",
        "    deployment_candidate[\"final_retrain_bundle\"] = FINAL_RETRAIN_RECORD[\"bundle_best\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "old_baseline = next(rec for rec in RUN_REGISTRY if rec[\"run_name\"] == \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\")\n",
        "successful_non_baseline = final_run_level_df[(final_run_level_df[\"status\"] == \"success\") & (final_run_level_df[\"run_name\"] != \"a_old_checkpoint_eval_only\")].copy()\n",
        "best_non_baseline = (\n",
        "    successful_non_baseline.sort_values([\"valid_macro_f1\", \"valid_balanced_accuracy\"], ascending=[False, False], na_position=\"last\").iloc[0].to_dict()\n",
        "    if not successful_non_baseline.empty else None\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "materially_beats_old = False\n",
        "if best_non_baseline is not None:\n",
        "    materially_beats_old = (\n",
        "        float(best_non_baseline.get(\"test_macro_f1\", -1.0)) >= float(old_baseline.get(\"test_macro_f1\", -1.0)) + CFG.narrative_materiality_delta\n",
        "    )\n",
        "\n",
        "summary_payload = {\n",
        "    \"best_clean_validation_run\": best_clean[\"run_name\"],\n",
        "    \"best_robust_validation_run\": best_robust[\"run_name\"],\n",
        "    \"best_calibrated_validation_run\": best_cal[\"run_name\"],\n",
        "    \"recommended_deployment_run\": deployment_candidate[\"run_name\"],\n",
        "    \"recommended_threshold\": deployment_candidate.get(\"recommended_threshold\"),\n",
        "    \"recommended_temperature\": deployment_candidate.get(\"temperature\", 1.0),\n",
        "    \"recommended_model_bundle\": deployment_candidate.get(\"bundle_best\", deployment_candidate.get(\"final_retrain_bundle\", str(CFG.old_model_path))),\n",
        "    \"materially_beats_old_model\": materially_beats_old,\n",
        "    \"old_model_path\": str(CFG.old_model_path),\n",
        "}\n",
        "save_json(CFG.paths.final_root / \"best_run_summary.json\", summary_payload)\n",
        "\n",
        "def best_family_record(df: pd.DataFrame, family_name: str) -> Optional[Dict[str, Any]]:\n",
        "    sub = df[(df[\"status\"] == \"success\") & (df[\"family\"] == family_name)].copy()\n",
        "    if sub.empty:\n",
        "        return None\n",
        "    return sub.sort_values([\"valid_macro_f1\", \"valid_balanced_accuracy\"], ascending=[False, False], na_position=\"last\").iloc[0].to_dict()\n",
        "\n",
        "best_old_ft = best_family_record(final_run_level_df, \"old_checkpoint\")\n",
        "best_generic = best_family_record(final_run_level_df, \"generic_pretrained\")\n",
        "best_scratch = best_family_record(final_run_level_df, \"scratch_yolo\")\n",
        "\n",
        "best_by_branch = (\n",
        "    final_run_level_df[final_run_level_df[\"status\"] == \"success\"]\n",
        "    .groupby(\"branch_name\")[\"valid_macro_f1\"]\n",
        "    .max()\n",
        "    .to_dict()\n",
        ")\n",
        "best_raw_val = float(best_by_branch.get(\"RAW\", np.nan))\n",
        "best_nonraw_val = max([float(v) for k, v in best_by_branch.items() if k != \"RAW\"], default=float(\"nan\"))\n",
        "crop_background_helped = bool(np.isfinite(best_raw_val) and np.isfinite(best_nonraw_val) and best_nonraw_val >= best_raw_val + 0.01)\n",
        "\n",
        "best_aug_policy = (\n",
        "    final_run_level_df[final_run_level_df[\"status\"] == \"success\"]\n",
        "    .groupby(\"aug_policy\")[\"valid_macro_f1\"]\n",
        "    .max()\n",
        "    .sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
        ")\n",
        "best_aug_name = best_aug_policy.index[0] if len(best_aug_policy) else \"unknown\"\n",
        "\n",
        "selected_valid = float(deployment_candidate.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", np.nan))\n",
        "selected_valid_challenge = float(deployment_candidate.get(\"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\", selected_valid))\n",
        "selected_challenge_drop = selected_valid - selected_valid_challenge if np.isfinite(selected_valid) and np.isfinite(selected_valid_challenge) else float(\"nan\")\n",
        "challenge_fragility = bool(np.isfinite(selected_challenge_drop) and selected_challenge_drop > 0.05)\n",
        "\n",
        "shortcut_learning_likely = crop_background_helped or challenge_fragility\n",
        "\n",
        "final_narrative = f'''\n",
        "# Final written summary\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1) Does the old model transfer?\n",
        "- Validation macro F1: **{old_baseline.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", float(\"nan\")):.3f}**\n",
        "- Holdout macro F1: **{old_baseline.get(\"test_macro_f1\", float(\"nan\")):.3f}**\n",
        "- Holdout balanced accuracy: **{old_baseline.get(\"test_balanced_accuracy\", float(\"nan\")):.3f}**\n",
        "- Holdout ECE: **{old_baseline.get(\"test_ece\", float(\"nan\")):.3f}**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 2) Does fine-tuning beat the old checkpoint directly?\n",
        "- Material improvement threshold: **{CFG.narrative_materiality_delta:.3f} macro F1**\n",
        "- Materially beats old baseline: **{materially_beats_old}**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 3) Best clean-validation model\n",
        "- Run: **{best_clean[\"run_name\"]}**\n",
        "- Validation macro F1: **{float(best_clean.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", float(\"nan\"))):.3f}**\n",
        "- Validation balanced accuracy: **{float(best_clean.get(\"valid_balanced_accuracy\", float(\"nan\"))):.3f}**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 4) Best robustness-oriented model\n",
        "- Run: **{best_robust[\"run_name\"]}**\n",
        "- Validation challenge mean macro F1: **{float(best_robust.get(\"valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1\", float(\"nan\"))):.3f}**\n",
        "- Validation worst challenge macro F1: **{float(best_robust.get(\"valid_challenge_worst_macro_f1\", float(\"nan\"))):.3f}**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 5) Best calibration-oriented model\n",
        "- Run: **{best_cal[\"run_name\"]}**\n",
        "- Validation ECE: **{float(best_cal.get(\"valid_ece\", float(\"nan\"))):.3f}**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 6) Recommended deployment candidate\n",
        "- Run: **{deployment_candidate[\"run_name\"]}**\n",
        "- Selection rationale: **{deployment_candidate.get(\"selection_rationale\", \"n/a\")}**\n",
        "- Recommended threshold (from validation only): **{float(deployment_candidate.get(\"recommended_threshold\", float(\"nan\"))):.2f}**\n",
        "- Recommended temperature (fit on validation only): **{float(deployment_candidate.get(\"temperature\", 1.0)):.3f}**\n",
        "- Model bundle: **{deployment_candidate.get(\"bundle_best\", deployment_candidate.get(\"final_retrain_bundle\", str(CFG.old_model_path)))}**\n",
        "\n",
        "## 6b) Family comparison\n",
        "- Best old-checkpoint fine-tuned run: **{best_old_ft[\"run_name\"] if best_old_ft else \"n/a\"}** (val macro F1 **{float(best_old_ft.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", float(\"nan\"))) if best_old_ft else float(\"nan\"):.3f}**)\n",
        "- Best generic pretrained run: **{best_generic[\"run_name\"] if best_generic else \"n/a\"}** (val macro F1 **{float(best_generic.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", float(\"nan\"))) if best_generic else float(\"nan\"):.3f}**)\n",
        "- Best scratch run: **{best_scratch[\"run_name\"] if best_scratch else \"n/a\"}** (val macro F1 **{float(best_scratch.get(\"valid_macro_f1\", float(\"nan\"))) if best_scratch else float(\"nan\"):.3f}**)\n",
        "\n",
        "This section answers whether old-checkpoint transfer beats generic pretrained and whether scratch is competitive.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 7) Did crop / background reduction help?\n",
        "Inspect the branch-comparison runs in the final leaderboard. Compare matched recipes on:\n",
        "- `RAW`\n",
        "- `TIGHT_CROP`\n",
        "- `BACKGROUND_REDUCED`\n",
        "- `STANDARDIZED_FRAME`\n",
        "\n",
        "## 8) Did augmentation help?\n",
        "Compare matched runs within each family across:\n",
        "- `none`\n",
        "- `light`\n",
        "- `medium`\n",
        "\n",
        "## 9) Did challenge suites expose fragility?\n",
        "Use:\n",
        "- `valid_challenge_mean_macro_f1`\n",
        "- `valid_challenge_worst_macro_f1`\n",
        "- `test_challenge_mean_macro_f1`\n",
        "for the shortlisted finalists. Large drops indicate nuisance sensitivity or remaining shortcut learning risk.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 10) Is shortcut learning still likely?\n",
        "Use the following diagnostics:\n",
        "- branch comparison deltas\n",
        "- embedding plots\n",
        "- nearest-neighbor audit\n",
        "- Grad-CAM overlays\n",
        "- label-noise review CSV\n",
        "- prediction disagreement CSV\n",
        "\n",
        "If the strongest models improve substantially on crop/background-reduced branches, or if Grad-CAM focuses on background regions, shortcut risk remains real.\n",
        "'''.strip()\n",
        "\n",
        "final_summary_md = CFG.paths.final_root / \"final_written_summary.md\"\n",
        "final_summary_md.write_text(final_narrative, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n",
        "\n",
        "print_rule(\"FINAL LEADERBOARD\")\n",
        "display(final_run_level_df.sort_values([\"robust_rank_score\", \"clean_rank_score\", \"valid_macro_f1\"], ascending=[False, False, False], na_position=\"last\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "print_rule(\"FINAL SELECTION SUMMARY\")\n",
        "print(json.dumps(summary_payload, indent=2))\n",
        "display(Markdown(final_narrative))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Saved run-level leaderboard to:\", (CFG.paths.final_root / \"leaderboard_final.csv\").resolve())\n",
        "print(\"Saved best-run summary to:\", (CFG.paths.final_root / \"best_run_summary.json\").resolve())\n",
        "print(\"Saved written summary to:\", final_summary_md.resolve())\n"
      ]
    }
